window.KT_I18N=window.KT_I18N||{};window.KT_I18N["zh-Hans"]={"About | KungfuTutor":"关于 | KungfuTutor","About KungfuTutor.com — interactive movement lessons for kung fu, martial arts, self-defence and sports.":"关于 KungfuTutor.com——功夫、武术、自卫与运动的互动动作课程。","{a} topics · {b} lessons":"{a} 个项目 · {b} 课","Kung Fu":"功夫","Fighting":"格斗技","Self-Defence":"自我防卫","Sports":"运动技巧","Fitness":"体能训练","Sign in":"登录","Every human movement · from traditional kung fu to modern sport":"每一个人体动作 · 从传统功夫到现代运动","See the movement.":"看懂动作，","Understand why it works.":"理解原理，","Master the art.":"练出真功夫。","Kung fu, fighting sports, self-defence, golf and gym — every move is an animation you can slow down, pause and step through, with clear cues, common mistakes and a drill to practise. Free, in 17 languages.":"功夫、格斗技、自我防卫、高尔夫与健身——每个动作都是可以放慢、暂停、逐步检视的动画，附上清楚的要领、常见错误与练习方法。完全免费，17 种语言。","Explore all lessons":"浏览全部课程","New: BJJ basics":"最新：巴西柔术入门","disciplines":"个项目","animated lessons":"个动画课程","languages":"种语言","Free":"免费","every lesson":"所有课程","All":"全部","Interactive lesson":"互动课程","Playing now":"正在播放","Watch every joint move":"看清楚每一个关节怎么动","Each lesson is a moving figure you can slow down, pause and step through, with the contact point and body line marked.":"每课都是一个会动的人形，可以放慢、暂停、一步一步看，并标出接触点与身体线条。","Bow-stance straight punch":"弓步冲拳","Front knee over toes · back leg straight":"前膝对脚尖 · 后腿蹬直","Step by step":"动作分解","Slow it down. Step through it.":"放慢它，拆开它","Learning speed or full speed, numbered steps, common mistakes and a drill — every lesson works the same way.":"学习速度或实战速度、编号步骤、常见错误和练习方法——每一课都一样清楚。","Try Wing Chun basics":"试试咏春入门","Free membership":"免费会员","Join with your email or phone":"用电邮或手机号码加入","Create a free member account. Every lesson stays free and open to everyone.":"创建免费会员账号。所有课程永远对每个人免费开放。","Email sign-in":"电邮登录","Phone code sign-in":"手机短信验证","01 · Traditional kung fu":"01 · 传统功夫","Chinese kung fu and internal arts":"中国功夫与内家拳","Start with the stances and basic punches and kicks, then Wing Chun's centreline and the Tai Chi 24-form.":"从步型和基本拳脚开始，再学咏春的中线与太极拳 24 式。","Foundations":"基础","The five stances":"五大步型","Horse, bow, empty, drop and cross: front/side animation, foot map and stance timer.":"马步、弓步、虚步、仆步、歇步：正侧面动画、脚位图与站桩计时。","5 lessons":"5 课","Start →":"开始 →","Punches & kicks":"拳法与腿法","Basic punches & kicks":"基本拳法与腿法","Straight punch, palm strike, snap, heel, side and stretch kicks — step by step.":"冲拳、推掌、弹腿、蹬腿、侧踹、正踢腿，逐步拆解。","6 lessons":"6 课","Wing Chun":"咏春","Wing Chun basics":"咏春入门 8 式","Stance, vertical & chain punch, tan/bong/fuk/pak sao, with a centreline guide.":"二字钳羊马、日字冲拳、连环拳、摊膀伏拍，附中线辅助线。","8 lessons":"8 课","Tai Chi":"太极拳","Tai Chi 24-form":"24 式太极拳","All 24 postures animated, with a breathing cue and play-the-whole-form mode.":"全部 24 式逐式动画、呼吸提示与连续播放全套。","24 postures":"24 式","02 · Fighting sports":"02 · 格斗技","World fighting sports: striking and grappling":"世界格斗技：打击与摔技","From Muay Thai and boxing to judo and sambo — every move is shown against a partner, so you see the distance and the point of contact.":"从泰拳、拳击到柔道、桑搏，每个动作都对着伙伴示范，看清楚距离与接触点。","Brazil":"巴西","Ground fighting":"地面技","Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu":"巴西柔术","Closed guard, shrimp, bridge and roll, hip bump sweep, knee cut pass, mount, armbar and rear naked choke.":"封闭式防守、虾式逃脱、挺腰翻身、撞臀扫倒、膝切过腿、骑乘位、手臂锁与裸绞。","Japan":"日本","Olympic sport":"奥运项目","Judo":"柔道","Bow and grips, breakfalls, foot sweep, outer and inner reaps, hip throw, scarf hold and armlock.":"礼与组手、受身、出足扫、大外刈、小内刈、大腰、袈裟固与十字固。","Soviet Union":"苏联","Sport · Combat":"运动 · 格斗","Sambo":"桑搏","Grips, breakfalls, foot sweep, back trip, leg pick-up, hold-down, ankle lock and strikes into throws.":"抓握、受身、扫脚、绊摔、抱腿、压制、脚踝锁与打击接摔。","Philippines":"菲律宾","Filipino martial arts":"菲律宾武术棍法","Grip, diagonal strikes, thrust, figure-8 flow, roof block, live-hand check and disarm.":"握棍、斜劈、直刺、8 字流动、屋顶挡、活手检查与缴械。","Worldwide":"全球","MMA basics":"综合格斗入门","Stance, striking, double-leg, sprawl, ground and pound and the technical stand-up.":"站架、打击、双腿抱摔、防摔下压、地面打击与安全起身。","Myanmar":"缅甸","Art of nine limbs":"九肢艺术","Lethwei basics":"缅甸拳入门","Bare knuckles, headbutt, rising elbow, flying knee and catch-and-sweep.":"裸拳、头撞、上挑肘、飞膝与接腿扫倒。","10 lessons":"10 课","Thailand":"泰国","Art of eight limbs":"八肢艺术","Muay Thai basics":"泰拳入门 10 招","Teep, roundhouse, low kick, elbow, clinch, knee and check — shown against an opponent.":"前蹬、中段踢、低踢、肘、箍颈、膝与挡踢，附对手示范。","Boxing basics":"拳击入门 10 课","Jab, cross, hook, uppercut, slip, bob and weave, parry and footwork.":"刺拳、直拳、勾拳、上勾拳、闪躲、下潜、拍挡与步法。","Coming soon":"即将推出","Wrestling":"摔与防摔","Freestyle, Greco-Roman and folkstyle.":"自由式、古典式与美式学生摔跤。","03 · Personal safety":"03 · 自我防卫","Self-defence: protect yourself, then get away":"自我防卫：先保护自己，再安全离开","Simple, practical moves for ordinary people — every one ends with getting away safely.":"简单、有效、适合一般人的防身动作，每一招的目标都是安全离开。","Basics":"基本防身术","Self-defence basics":"基本防身术 8 招","The fence, keeping distance, palm heel, elbow, wrist-grab release and head cover.":"戒备姿势、保持距离、掌根击、肘击、手腕脱困、护头。","Israel":"以色列","Krav Maga basics":"以色列格斗术入门","Defend and counter at once, front-choke release, non-stop counters — then get away.":"同时防守与反击、掐喉脱困、连续攻击，最后安全离开。","Safety":"安全须知","Falling safely":"安全倒地","Back and side breakfalls.":"后倒与侧倒的护身倒法。","04 · Sports skills":"04 · 运动技巧","Sports skills: the swing, race stations and more":"运动技巧：挥杆、比赛关卡与更多","The golf swing and HYROX race stations, broken into a movement chain you can follow.":"把高尔夫挥杆和 HYROX 比赛拆成看得懂的动作链。","Scotland":"苏格兰","Golf":"高尔夫","Golf swing":"高尔夫挥杆","Setup, backswing, downswing, impact and finish — plus driver, chip and putt.":"站姿、上杆、下杆、击球、收杆，加上一号木、切球与推杆。","Fitness racing":"健身竞赛","HYROX: 8 stations":"HYROX 8 大关卡","Animated demos, loads for every division, judging rules and training tips.":"8 站动画示范、各组别负重、通关规则与训练重点。","8 stations":"8 站","Racket sports":"球拍运动","Badminton smash":"羽球杀球","The full chain from backswing and trunk rotation to contact point.":"从引拍、转体到击球点的完整动作链。","05 · Fitness & mobility":"05 · 体能训练","Strength, conditioning and mobility":"力量、体能与柔韧度","The essential gym lifts, with beginner versions and the right line of force.":"健身房的基本动作，附初学版本与正确的发力路线。","Gym":"健身房","10 essential gym exercises":"健身房 10 个基本动作","Squat, deadlift, bench, press, row, pull-up and more — with beginner versions and bar path.":"深蹲、硬举、卧推、肩推、划船、引体向上等，附初学版本与杠铃路线。","Mobility":"柔韧度","Stretches for high kicks":"踢腿柔软度","Safe hip and hamstring stretches.":"髋关节与腿后肌的安全伸展。","Balance":"平衡","Balance training":"平衡训练","Weight-shift drills for every age.":"适合各年龄的重心转移练习。","How it works":"动作要领","Learn any move in three steps":"三步学会一个动作","Every lesson works the same way — learn one page and you can use them all.":"每一课的结构都一样，学会一个，就会用全部。","Pick a move":"选一个动作","Choose from the five areas; the lessons are numbered in the best order to learn them.":"从五大类别中选择，建议依编号顺序学习。","Watch it slowly, step by step":"慢动作逐步看","Use learning speed, 0.25× slow motion or the next-step button to see every joint.":"用学习速度、0.25× 慢放或「下一步」按钮，看清楚每一个关节。","Practise and mark it mastered":"照着练，标记熟练","Follow the drill, avoid the common mistakes, and mark the move as mastered when you have it.":"照着练习方法做，避开常见错误，熟练后标记“已熟悉”。","Start training today":"今天就开始练习","Every lesson is free. Create a member account with your email or phone number.":"所有课程都免费。用你的电邮或手机号码建立会员账号。","Join free":"免费加入","Browse lessons":"浏览课程","Check your health before training, and practise under a qualified coach where possible.":"练习前请评估自身健康状况，并尽可能在合格教练指导下进行。","Interactive animated lessons for every human movement — from traditional kung fu and world fighting sports to golf and the gym.":"互动动画课程，涵盖所有人体动作——从传统功夫、世界格斗运动到高尔夫与健身。","Lessons":"课程","Newest":"最新","Site":"本站","About":"关于我们","Privacy":"隐私权政策","Terms & Safety":"使用条款与安全声明","Contact":"联络","Content is for education only. Check your health before training and practise under a qualified instructor where possible.":"本站内容仅供教育参考。练习前请评估自身健康状况，并尽可能在合格教练指导下进行。","KungfuTutor — Interactive Kung Fu, Martial Arts & Sports Movement Lessons":"KungfuTutor — 互动式功夫、武术与运动动作课程","Learn kung fu, fighting sports, self-defence, golf and gym skills from animated, interactive movement lessons. Slow them down, step through them and understand why they work — free, in 17 languages.":"通过动画互动的动作课程，学习功夫、格斗运动、自卫、高尔夫和健身技能。放慢动作，逐步拆解，理解它们为何有效——免费，提供17种语言。","Privacy Policy | KungfuTutor":"隐私政策 | KungfuTutor","How KungfuTutor.com handles data, cookies and advertising.":"KungfuTutor.com 如何处理数据、Cookie 和广告。","Terms & Safety | KungfuTutor":"条款与安全 | KungfuTutor","Terms of use and training safety notice for KungfuTutor.com.":"KungfuTutor.com 的使用条款及训练安全须知。","Member":"会员","My account":"我的账号","The email or password is not right.":"电邮或密码不正确。","No account with that email — create one first.":"找不到这个电邮的账号，请先建立账号。","That email is already registered — sign in instead.":"这个电邮已经注册，请直接登录。","Please enter a valid email address.":"请输入有效的电邮地址。","The password needs at least 6 characters.":"密码至少需要 6 个字符。","Please enter your password.":"请输入密码。","Too many tries — please wait a little and try again.":"尝试次数太多，请稍后再试。","Enter your phone number with the country code, e.g. +60 12 345 6789.":"请输入含国码的手机号码，例如 +60 12 345 6789。","That code is not right.":"验证码不正确。","The code has expired — send a new one.":"验证码已过期，请重新发送。","Network problem — please try again.":"网络连接有问题，请再试一次。","This sign-in method is not switched on yet.":"这种登录方式尚未开放。","Text-message limit reached for today — please use email instead.":"今天的短信额度已用完，请改用电邮登录。","Something went wrong — please try again.":"发生错误，请再试一次。","Close":"关闭","Email":"电邮","Phone":"手机","Email address":"电邮地址","Password":"密码","Create a new account":"建立新账号","Forgot your password?":"忘记密码？","Phone number (with country code)":"手机号码（含国码）","Text me a code":"发送验证码","6-digit code":"6 位数验证码","Confirm and sign in":"确认并登录","We will text you a one-time code; your carrier's normal text-message rates may apply.":"我们会发送一则短信验证码；电信运营商可能收取一般短信费用。","Sign out":"登出","Member sign-in is being set up and will open soon. Every lesson is free to use right now.":"会员登录正在设置中，很快就会开放。所有课程现在都可以免费使用。","By continuing you agree to the <a href=\"{t}\">terms</a> and <a href=\"{p}\">privacy policy</a>.":"继续即表示你同意本站的<a href=\"{t}\">使用条款</a>与<a href=\"{p}\">隐私权政策</a>。","Signed in as ":"已登录：","Member sign-in":"会员登录","Sign in or join free":"登录或免费加入","Use your email or phone number. Every lesson is free.":"使用电邮或手机号码。所有课程都免费。","Account created! We have sent a confirmation link to your email.":"账号已建立！我们已把确认链接寄到你的电邮。","Enter your email address first.":"请先输入你的电邮地址。","We have emailed you a link to reset your password.":"我们已寄出重设密码的链接，请查看你的电邮。","Code sent — check your text messages.":"验证码已发送，请查看你的短信。","Please wait…":"请稍候…","Clearest from the other view":"这个动作以另一视角最清楚","MASTERED":"已熟悉","✓ Marked as mastered":"✓ 已标记为熟悉","Mark as mastered":"标记为已熟悉","Progress is saved in your browser only":"进度只存在你的浏览器"," — demo":"动作示意","Your best hold: ":"你的最佳纪录：","Finish a hold to record your best time":"完成一次计时就会记下你的最佳纪录","Stop":"停止","Start hold":"开始站桩","Closed Guard":"封闭式防守","Guard":"防守位","Legs round the waist":"双腿夹腰","Ground (bottom)":"地面（下位）","Control and breaking posture":"控制与姿势破坏","ANKLES CROSSED · COLLAR AND SLEEVE · PULL THEM DOWN":"脚踝交叉 · 抓领抓袖 · 拉低对方","Lie on your back with your legs round the waist of a partner kneeling between them, ankles crossed and locked behind their back. Grip their collar with one hand and their sleeve with the other. Pull with your legs and arms so they bend forward. With their posture broken they struggle to pass your legs or strike, while you set up sweeps and submissions.":"仰躺，双腿夹住跪在你双腿之间的对方的腰，脚踝在对方背后交叉锁住。一手抓对方衣领，一手抓袖子。用双腿把对方拉向你、双手往下拉，让对方弯腰。对方姿势被破坏时，很难过你的腿，也很难出拳，你则可以准备扫倒或降伏。","Legs too loose, so they sit up tall; pulling with the arms but not the legs; lying flat and waiting; straightening the legs after crossing the ankles (easy to open).":"双腿夹得太松（对方坐直）；只用手拉不用腿；平躺不动等对方进攻；脚踝交叉后把腿伸直（容易被打开）。","Your partner tries to sit up straight in your guard for 1 minute while you keep pulling them down with legs and arms — 3 rounds each.":"伙伴在你的防守里尝试坐直 1 分钟，你用腿和手不断把对方拉低，轮流 3 回合。","BJJ lets a smaller person stay safe and in control even when on their back; the closed guard is the clearest example.":"柔术让体型较小的人在背部着地时仍能安全地控制对方，封闭式防守是最基本的例子。","Hip Escape (Shrimp)":"虾式逃脱","Movement":"移动","Foot pushes the mat":"脚推地面","Hip mobility and core":"髋部活动与核心","FOOT DOWN · TURN TO THE SIDE · HIPS BACK":"踩地 · 转侧 · 臀部后推","Lie on your back with your knees bent and feet flat. Push off one foot to lift your hips and turn onto one shoulder, then drive your hips back — away from your feet — curling onto your side like a shrimp. Return flat and repeat. When you are pinned, this movement makes space between you and your partner so you can bring your legs back in front and rebuild your guard.":"仰卧，双膝弯曲，双脚平放在地上。用一只脚蹬地，抬起臀部并转到一侧肩膀，然后把臀部向后推离双脚，身体像虾一样蜷向一侧。回到平躺后重复。被压制时，这个动作能在你和对方之间创造空间，让你把腿收回到身前，重新建立防守。","Wriggling the upper body while the hips stay put; pushing before turning onto your side; leaving the arms away from the body; forgetting to bring the legs back in after the move.":"只扭动上身而臀部不动；还没转到侧身就先推；双手离开身体不管；动作做完忘了把腿收回来。","Shrimp up and down the length of the mat 4 times as part of every warm-up.":"沿着垫子的长边，连续做虾式移动来回 4 趟，作为每次练习的热身。","Almost every escape uses it: getting out of side control or the mount, or recovering your guard when they start to pass.":"几乎所有地面逃脱都用到虾式：从侧压、骑乘位逃脱，或在对方过腿时把腿放回来。","Bridge and Roll Escape":"挺腰翻身逃脱","Escape":"脱困","Hips drive up":"臀部往上挺","Explosiveness and timing":"爆发力与时机","TRAP THE ARM · FOOT OUTSIDE · BRIDGE AND ROLL":"锁手臂 · 脚踩外侧 · 挺腰翻身","With them mounted on you, keep your elbows in and your feet flat near your hips. Trap one of their arms to your chest and step your foot outside their foot on the same side, so that side has no post. Then bridge hard, driving your hips up and towards the trapped side's shoulder. They roll over and you come up on top, kneeling between their legs.":"对方骑在你身上时，手肘贴身保护自己，双脚靠近臀部踩地。把对方一只手臂锁在胸前，同侧的脚踩到对方脚外侧，让对方那一边没有支撑。然后用力挺腰，把臀部往上、往被锁的那一侧肩膀方向推，对方会翻过去，你翻到上面，跪在对方双腿之间。","Bridging without trapping the arm (they post their hand); not trapping the foot; bridging straight up instead of over the shoulder; pushing their chest with straight arms (gives them an armbar).":"没锁住手臂就挺腰（对方用手撑住）；脚没踩到外侧；往正上方挺而不是往肩膀方向；双手推对方胸口（容易被锁手臂）。","With your partner in mount, drill trap the arm, trap the foot and bridge slowly 10 times to each side, with your partner rolling over cooperatively.":"伙伴骑在你身上，慢速练「锁手 + 锁脚 + 挺腰」左右各 10 次，伙伴配合翻过去。","The mount is one of the worst places to be; the bridge and roll takes you from bottom to top in one move.":"骑乘位是最危险的下位之一；挺腰翻身让你一次就从最差的位置回到上面。","Hip Bump Sweep":"撞臀扫倒","Sweep":"扫倒","Hips into their chest":"臀部撞胸口","Bottom → top":"下位 → 上位","THEY SIT UP · SIT UP AND POST · HIPS IN":"对方坐直 · 坐起撑手 · 臀部撞进去","When they sit up straight in your closed guard, open your legs and sit up, posting one hand behind you and reaching the other over their shoulder. Then lift your hips and drive them into their chest so they fall backwards. Come forward with them and land straight in the mount. In competition a sweep scores 2 points.":"对方在你的封闭式防守里坐直时，打开双腿坐起来，一手在身后撑地，另一手伸过对方的肩膀。然后抬起臀部，用臀部撞进对方的胸口，对方会往后倒。你跟着往前，直接坐上骑乘位。比赛中扫倒得 2 分。","Trying it when they are bent over (it works when they sit up); no posted hand, so the hips cannot lift; not reaching over the shoulder; bumping and then not following them.":"等对方弯腰才做（要在对方坐直时做）；没有撑手，臀部抬不起来；手臂没伸过肩膀；撞完没跟上去。","With your partner sitting up in your guard, drill it slowly 10 times each side while your partner falls back cooperatively.":"伙伴在你的防守里坐直，慢速练习左右各 10 次，伙伴配合往后倒。","When they sit up to avoid being pulled down, they give you the hip bump; it also links to the guillotine and the kimura.":"对方为了不被拉低而坐直时，正好给你撞臀扫倒的机会；它也常接到断头台勒颈或木村锁。","Knee Cut Guard Pass":"膝切过腿","Guard pass":"过腿","Knee across the thigh":"膝盖切过大腿","Ground (top)":"地面（上位）","Pressure and balance":"压力与平衡","CONTROL COLLAR AND LEG · KNEE CUTS THE THIGH · CHEST DOWN":"控制领与裤 · 膝切大腿 · 胸压下","With them on their back and legs up, kneel in front of them and control their collar and trouser leg. Slice your front knee across their thigh to the mat, drop your chest and put your arm round their head. Then free your back leg and settle chest to chest in side control. In competition a guard pass scores 3 points.":"对方仰躺、双腿抬起时，你单膝跪在前方，一手抓衣领，一手控制裤管。把前膝斜切过对方的大腿，压到地面，胸口跟着压下，手臂绕过对方的头。最后抽出后腿，胸贴胸进入侧压。比赛中过腿得 3 分。","Staying upright with no pressure (they bring the legs back); not cutting the knee far enough; leaving the back leg for them to hook; standing up instead of settling low after the pass.":"上身挺直不压（对方把腿放回来）；膝盖切得不够远；后腿被对方勾住；过完不压低就马上站起来。","Your partner lies on their back with feet on your hips; drill the knee cut slowly 8 times each side with light resistance.":"伙伴仰躺做蝴蝶防守，你慢速练膝切过腿左右各 8 次，伙伴只轻微抵抗。","From the top, passing the guard takes you from their legs to side control — where scoring and attacks begin.":"在上面时，过腿把对方从防守带到侧压，是得分和进攻的起点。","Side Control to Mount":"侧压转骑乘","Transition":"位置转换","Knee across the belly":"膝盖滑过肚子","Control and weight":"控制与重量","CHEST ON CHEST · KNEE SLIDES OVER · KNEES TIGHT":"胸压胸 · 膝盖滑过 · 双膝贴身","In side control keep your chest on theirs and your hips low. Slide the knee nearest their legs across their belly while your chest stays heavy so they get no space. Once you are over, sit up with your knees tight to both sides of their body and your weight low. In competition the mount scores 4 points.":"在侧压中，胸口压着对方、臀部压低。把靠近对方腿部的膝盖从对方肚子上滑过去，胸口继续压着，不给对方空间。跨过去之后坐起来，双膝贴着对方身体两侧，重心压低。比赛中骑乘位得 4 分。","Lifting the chest during the move (they escape into the space); getting the knee blocked by their leg; sitting too high once mounted (easy to roll); knees too wide.":"转换时胸口抬起（对方趁机逃脱）；膝盖被对方的腿挡住；骑上去后坐得太高（容易被翻）；双膝张太开。","With light resistance, go from side control to mount and back again, 10 times in a row.":"伙伴轻微抵抗，你从侧压转骑乘、再回侧压，连续 10 次。","The mount is one of BJJ's most dominant positions, leading to armbars or to taking the back when they turn.":"骑乘位是柔术最有优势的位置之一，可以接到手臂锁或让对方翻身后拿背。","Armbar from Guard":"防守位手臂锁","Submission":"降伏","Pressure on their elbow":"压力在对方手肘","Control and safety":"控制与安全意识","HUG THE ARM · TURN · LEG OVER THE HEAD · KNEES IN, HIPS UP":"抱手臂 · 转身 · 腿过头 · 夹膝抬臀","When they are bent over in your guard with one hand on your chest, hug that arm with both hands. Put one foot on their hip to help you turn and swing the other leg up and over their head. Bring both legs down, squeeze your knees together with their thumb pointing up, then lift your hips a little — the pressure goes onto their elbow. The moment they tap, let go.":"对方在你的防守里弯腰、一只手撑在你胸口时，双手抱住那只手臂。一脚踩在对方臀部上帮助转身，另一腿抬起越过对方的头。双腿压下、双膝夹紧，对方拇指朝上，然后臀部微微抬起，压力就落在对方手肘。对方一拍地，马上放开。","Jerking it on fast (causes injuries); not turning, so the hips stay far from their shoulder; not holding the head down with the leg (they stand up); not letting go after the tap.":"猛然用力（会造成受伤）；没转身，臀部离对方肩膀太远；腿没压住对方的头（对方站起来）；对方拍地后还不放。","Under a coach, practise the position with very light pressure, 5 times to each side, and both partners practise tapping.":"在教练指导下，搭档之间只做「位置 + 极轻施压」左右各 5 次，双方都练习拍地。","A submission wins the match outright, whatever the score.":"让对方认输直接获胜，不论比分是多少。","Rear Naked Choke":"Rear Naked Choke","Arm round both sides of the neck":"手臂绕过颈部两侧","Ground (back)":"地面（背后）","HOOKS IN · ARM UNDER CHIN · GRAB BICEPS · SQUEEZE":"勾脚 · 手臂穿下巴 · 抓二头肌 · 慢慢夹","In back control keep your chest on their back with both heels hooked inside their thighs. Slide your choking arm under their chin so your elbow is in front of their throat, grab your other biceps with that hand, and put the other hand behind their head. Squeeze your elbows together slowly — the pressure goes on both sides of the neck. The moment they tap or say stop, let go.":"在背后控制中，胸口贴着对方的背，双脚脚跟勾在对方大腿内侧。锁颈的手臂从对方下巴下方穿过，手肘对准喉咙正前方，手掌抓住另一只手的二头肌，另一只手放在对方头后。慢慢把双肘夹紧，压力在颈部两侧。对方一拍地或说“停”，马上放开。","Cranking it on fast (dangerous); the arm across the jaw instead of the neck; crossing your feet in front of their belly (they can lock your ankles); not letting go after the tap.":"猛然用力（危险）；手臂压在下巴上而不是颈部；双脚交叉在对方肚子前（容易被锁脚）；对方拍地后还不放。","Only with a qualified coach: practise the hooks and arm position 5 times each with light contact and no squeeze.":"只在合格教练指导下练习：伙伴之间练「勾脚 + 手臂位置」各 5 次，只轻轻接触，不施压。","Back control is one of the most dominant positions in BJJ, and the rear naked choke is its most common finish.":"背后控制是柔术最有优势的位置之一，裸绞是从那里最常用的降伏。","BJJ's signature position":"柔术的招牌位置","Control from underneath":"在下面也能控制","One of BJJ's most important movements":"柔术最重要的动作之一","Makes space on the ground":"在地上制造空间","The first escape from mount":"被骑乘时的第一个逃脱","Trap the arm, trap the foot, bridge":"锁手、锁脚、挺腰","A sweep scores 2 points":"掃倒得 2 分","Best when they sit up straight":"对方坐直时最有效","A guard pass scores 3 points":"过腿得 3 分","Cut, chest down, side control":"膝切、压胸、侧压","The mount scores 4 points":"骑乘位得 4 分","Keep the chest heavy":"胸口一直压着","One of BJJ's classic submissions":"柔术最经典的降伏之一","Apply slowly; release on the tap":"慢慢施压，对方拍地即放","Back control scores 4 points":"背后控制得 4 分","Squeeze slowly; release on the tap":"慢慢夹紧，对方拍地即放","You are on your back with your legs locked round their waist, ankles crossed behind them":"你仰躺，双腿夹住对方的腰，脚踝在对方背后交叉","Grip the collar with one hand and the sleeve with the other":"一手抓衣领，一手抓袖子","Pull with your legs and arms so they bend forward — their posture is broken":"双腿把对方拉向你、双手往下拉，打破对方的姿势","Keep them bent over: they cannot pass or strike well, and you can set up attacks":"保持对方弯腰：对方很难过腿或出手，你可以准备进攻","Lie on your back, knees bent, feet flat, elbows in":"仰躺，双膝弯起，双脚踩地，手肘贴身","Push off one foot, lift the hips and turn onto one shoulder":"用脚推地，臀部抬起，转到一侧肩膀","Drive your hips back, away from your feet, curling onto your side like a shrimp":"把臀部往后推开，远离双脚，身体缩成侧躺的虾形","Back flat and repeat — you have made space on the ground":"回到仰躺，再做一次 —— 这样就在地上制造了空间","They are mounted on you: elbows in, feet flat near your hips":"对方骑在你身上：手肘贴身，双脚靠近臀部踩地","Trap one of their arms to your chest and step your foot outside their foot on the same side":"锁住对方一只手臂在胸前，同侧的脚踩到对方脚外侧","Bridge hard: drive your hips up and over your shoulder":"用力挺腰：臀部往上、往你的肩膀方向推","They lose their balance and roll over your shoulder":"对方失去平衡，从你的肩膀方向翻过去","You end on top, kneeling between their legs — posture up first":"你翻到上面，跪在对方的双腿之间 —— 先稳住姿势","They sit up straight in your guard":"对方在你的防守里坐直","Open your legs and sit up, posting one hand behind you and reaching the other over their shoulder":"打开双腿坐起来，一手在身后撑地，另一手伸过对方肩膀","Lift your hips and drive them into their chest":"抬起臀部，用臀部撞进对方胸口","They fall back and you come forward with them":"对方往后倒，你跟着往前","Land straight in the mount — 2 points for the sweep, then 4 for the mount":"直接落入骑乘位 —— 扫倒得 2 分，骑乘再得 4 分","They are on their back with legs up; you kneel in front, controlling the collar and trouser leg":"对方仰躺、双腿抬起；你单膝跪在前方，控制衣领与裤管","Slice your knee across their thigh to the mat":"膝盖斜切过对方的大腿，压到地面","Drop your chest and put your arm round their head":"胸口下压，手臂绕过对方的头","Free your back leg and settle chest to chest in side control — 3 points for the pass":"抽出后腿，胸贴胸落入侧压 —— 过腿得 3 分","Side control: chest on chest, hips low":"侧压：胸贴胸，臀部压低","Slide your knee across their belly while your chest stays heavy":"膝盖从对方肚子上滑过去，胸口继续压着","Step over, knees tight to both sides of their body":"跨过去，双膝紧贴对方身体两侧","Settle into the mount with your weight low — 4 points":"坐稳骑乘位，重心压低 —— 4 分","They are bent over in your guard with one hand on your chest":"对方在你的防守里弯腰，一只手撑在你胸口","Hug that arm, put a foot on their hip to turn, and swing the other leg up over their head":"双手抱住那只手臂，脚踩对方臀部转身，另一条腿抬过对方的头","Legs down, knees squeezed, lift the hips a little — the pressure goes on their elbow":"双腿压下、夹紧膝盖，臀部微微抬起 —— 压力落在对方手肘","They tap — let go at once":"对方拍地认输 —— 立刻放开","Back control: chest to their back, both heels hooked inside their thighs":"背后控制：胸贴对方背，双脚脚跟勾住对方大腿内侧","Slide your choking arm under their chin, elbow in front of their throat":"锁颈的手臂从下巴下方穿过，手肘对准对方喉咙正前方","Grab your other biceps, put that hand behind their head, and squeeze slowly":"手抓另一只手的二头肌，那只手放到对方头后，慢慢夹紧","CONTACT: ":"接触点：","Control":"控制","Leg strength":"腿力","Gripping":"抓握","Patience":"耐心","Hip mobility":"髋部柔韧度","Core":"核心","Coordination":"协调","Endurance":"耐力","Explosiveness":"爆发力","Timing":"时机","Linking":"衔接","Pressure":"压力","Weight pressure":"重量压力","Current speed: ":"目前速度：","Learning (slow motion)":"学习（慢动作）","Fight speed":"实战速度","Phase: ":"阶段：","Technique {n} of 8 · {type}":"第 {n} 个技术（共 8 个）· {type}","What is Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu?":"什么是巴西柔术？","Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu (BJJ) is a martial art and sport that grew in Brazil from the judo and jujutsu taught there in the early twentieth century, developed above all by the Gracie family. It focuses on the ground: with the right position and leverage, a smaller person can stay safe, control a bigger opponent and even make them submit. It is usually trained in a jacket (the gi), and also without one (no-gi).":"巴西柔术（BJJ）是一种在20世纪初由巴西传授的柔道和柔术发展而来的格斗术与运动，主要由格雷西（Gracie）家族发扬光大。它专注于地面：凭借正确的位置和杠杆原理，体型较小的人也能保护自己、控制更高大的对手，甚至让对方认输。训练时通常穿着道服（gi），也会不穿道服（no-gi）练习。","The eight lessons at a glance":"八堂课一览","Technique":"技术","Type":"类型","Phase":"阶段","How scoring works":"如何计分与获胜","Under International Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu Federation (IBJJF) rules a takedown, sweep or knee on belly scores 2 points, passing the guard scores 3, and the mount or back control scores 4; a position usually has to be held for about 3 seconds to score. Near-misses earn \"advantages\", used to break ties. A submission wins outright, whatever the score. Rules differ a little between events, so check the rules of the one you enter.":"依国际巴西柔术联盟（IBJJF）规则：摔倒、扫倒或膝压腹各得 2 分，过腿得 3 分，骑乘位或背后控制得 4 分，位置通常要稳住约 3 秒才给分。差一点完成的动作会得到“优势”，用来分出平手。不论比分多少，让对方认输都直接获胜。不同赛事的规则略有不同，比赛前请查看该赛事的规则。","Starting out safely":"入门与安全","Learn the shrimp, the bridge and how to fall safely before learning submissions.":"先学会虾式、挺腰和安全倒地，再学降伏。","Practise submissions only on mats, with a coach.":"降伏技只在软垫上、在教练指导下练习。","Apply locks and chokes slowly — let go the moment your partner taps or says stop.":"关节技和勒颈要慢慢施压：对方一拍地或说“停”，马上放开。","Tap early when you are caught — never fight through a lock or choke.":"被锁时早点拍地认输，不要硬撑。","Related: <a href=\"../judo/\">judo basics</a>, <a href=\"../sambo/\">sambo basics</a> and <a href=\"../mma/\">MMA basics</a>.":"相关课程：<a href=\"../judo/\">柔道入门</a>、<a href=\"../sambo/\">桑搏入门</a>、<a href=\"../mma/\">MMA 入门</a>。","Frequently asked questions":"常见问题","How is BJJ different from judo?":"巴西柔术和柔道有什么不同？","They share the same roots. Judo competition rewards throws and gives little time on the ground; BJJ spends most of its time on the ground and has developed many guards, sweeps and submissions.":"两者同源。柔道比赛重视把对方摔倒，地面时间很短；巴西柔术则把大部分时间花在地面，发展出很多防守位、扫倒与降服。","What should a beginner learn first?":"初学者应该先学什么？","The shrimp, the bridge, the closed guard and escapes from mount and side control — learn to stay safe before you learn to attack.":"蚝式、挺腰、封闭式防守和从骑乘位、侧压逃脱——先学会保护自己，再学进攻。","What are the belt colours?":"腰带有哪些颜色？","Adults start at white and go through blue, purple and brown to black; children have their own belts in between. Reaching black belt usually takes many years.":"成人从白带开始，依次是蓝带、紫带、棕带和黑带；儿童另有中间的腰带。升到黑带通常需要很多年。","FIGHTING SPORTS · BJJ FOR BEGINNERS":"格斗运动 · 巴西柔术入门","Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu Basics: Guard, Escapes, Sweeps, Passes and Submissions in 8 Lessons":"巴西柔术入门：防守、逃脱、扫倒、过腿与降服 8 课","Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu is a grappling art built around fighting on the ground, using position and leverage so a smaller person can control a bigger one. These 8 lessons start with the closed guard and the shrimp, then escapes and a sweep from underneath, passing the guard and taking the mount, and finish with the armbar and the rear naked choke. Blue gi is you, white is your partner; the red ring marks the point of contact.":"巴西柔术是以地面技术为主的格斗术，靠位置与杠杆让体型较小的人也能控制对手。这 8 课从封闭式防守和虾式逃脱开始，学从下方逃脱和扫倒，再学过腿、骑乘位，最后是手臂锁与裸绞。蓝色道服是你，白色是伙伴，红圈标示接触点。","Bottom":"下位","Guard, escapes and sweeps":"防守、逃脱与扫倒","Top":"上位","Passing, side control and mount":"过腿、侧压与骑乘","Submissions":"降服","Armbar and rear naked choke":"手臂锁与裸绞","Adult belts":"成人腰带","White · blue · purple · brown · black":"白 · 蓝 · 紫 · 棕 · 黑","This technique's phase":"目前技术阶段","Mount or back control":"骑乘或背后控制","Guard pass 3 · sweep 2":"过腿 3 分 · 扫倒 2 分","Techniques you have mastered":"技术掌握进度","Mark each technique as mastered below":"可在下方标记为「已熟悉」","Choose the speed (the animation updates instantly)":"选择速度（动画即时改变）","Learning · slow motion":"学习 · 慢动作","Reset mastered marks":"重置熟练标记","Pick a technique (best learned in order)":"选择技术查看细节（建议依序学习）","Click a card or use the ← / → keys":"点选卡片或键盘 ← / → 方向键切换","Contact point":"接触点","What it builds":"练的是什么","How to do it":"动作要领","Common mistakes":"常见错误","Drill":"练习方法","In a fight":"实战用途","SIDE · BLUE = YOU · WHITE = PARTNER":"侧面 · 蓝＝你 · 白＝伙伴","RIGHT":"右式","LEFT":"左式","NEXT STEP ▸":"下一步 ▸","What this technique trains":"此技术训练重点","Relative importance":"相对重要度","For education only; the animations are simplified. Practise submissions only on mats with a qualified coach; apply locks and chokes slowly, let go the moment your partner taps or says stop, and tap early yourself.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，动画为简化示意。降伏技只在有合格教练的软垫上练习；关节技与勒颈要慢慢施压，对方拍地或说停立即放开，被锁时早点拍地。","Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu (BJJ) Basics: Guard, Escapes, Sweeps, Passes & Submissions — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"巴西柔术（BJJ）基础：守位、脱逃、翻转、过位与降服技——互动指南 | KungfuTutor","Learn 8 Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu fundamentals with animated demos against a partner: closed guard, hip escape, bridge and roll, hip bump sweep, knee cut pass, side control to mount, armbar and rear naked choke.":"通过与搭档的动画示范，学习8项巴西柔术基本功：闭合守位、髋部脱逃、桥与翻滚、髋撞翻转、膝切过位、侧控转骑乘位、十字固和裸绞。","BJJ Basics — Guard, Sweeps, Passes and Submissions, Step by Step":"巴西柔术基础——守位、翻转、过位与降服技，循序渐进","A grappling martial art and sport that grew in Brazil from the judo and jujutsu taught there in the early twentieth century, developed above all by the Gracie family. It focuses on fighting on the ground, using position and leverage so a smaller person can control and submit a larger one.":"一种格斗摔跤武术与运动，二十世纪初在巴西由当地教授的柔道和柔术发展而来，主要由Gracie家族发展完善。它专注于地面格斗，利用位置和杠杆原理，使体型较小的人能够控制并迫使体型较大的对手认输。","How are points scored in BJJ?":"巴西柔术的得分方式是什么？","Under IBJJF rules a takedown, sweep or knee on belly scores 2 points, passing the guard scores 3, and the mount or back control scores 4. A submission wins the match outright, whatever the score.":"根据IBJJF规则，摔倒、扫翻或膝压腹部得2分，通过对方守位得3分，骑乘位或背部控制得4分。降服技直接赢得比赛，无论比分如何。","What are the BJJ belt colours?":"巴西柔术的腰带颜色有哪些？","Adults go from white to blue, purple, brown and black belt. Children have their own belts in between, and progress usually takes many years.":"成人的腰带依次为白带、蓝带、紫带、棕带和黑带。儿童另有适合其年龄段的腰带，位于其间。晋级通常需要多年时间。","Stance & Guard":"站架与防守姿势","Foundation":"基本","Side-on, chin down":"侧身、下巴收","Balance and defence":"平衡与防守","SIDE-ON · SOFT KNEES · GLOVES AT CHEEKS · CHIN DOWN":"侧身 · 膝微弯 · 手护脸颊 · 下巴收","Right-handers stand left foot forward (orthodox), feet about shoulder-width, lead toes pointing forward and the back foot turned out about 45° with the heel slightly raised. Turn a little side-on to present a smaller target, knees soft, weight even. Keep the gloves by your cheeks, elbows in front of the ribs, chin tucked, eyes on the opponent over your gloves.":"右撇子左脚在前（正架），双脚约与肩同宽，前脚尖朝前、后脚约 45° 外转、后脚跟微微抬起。身体侧一点以减少被击中的面积，膝盖微弯、重心平均。双手护在脸颊两侧，手肘收在肋骨前，下巴收，眼睛从手套上方看对方。","Feet on one line (no balance); chin up; elbows flared, exposing the body; locked knees.":"双脚站在同一直线上（失去平衡）；下巴抬起；手肘外张、暴露身体；膝盖锁死。","Hold your stance in a mirror and bounce lightly, 3 × 1 minute, checking chin and hands.":"对镜保持站架并轻轻弹动 3 × 1 分钟，检查下巴与手的位置。","A good stance lets you attack, defend and move at the same time.":"好的站架让你能同时攻击、防守和移动。","Jab":"刺拳","Straight punch":"直拳","Face":"脸","Fast out, fast back":"快出快收","Speed and range":"速度与距离感","STRAIGHT OUT · TURN PALM-DOWN · SAME LINE BACK":"直线出 · 拳心转下 · 原路收回","From your stance, shoot the lead hand straight out, turning it palm-down just before impact, with the lead shoulder raised to protect the chin and the rear glove by your chin. Bring it back along the same line, fast. A small step with the lead foot adds reach.":"从站架出发，前手直线向前打出，快到终点时拳头转成拳心向下，前肩抬起保护下巴，后手留在下巴旁。打完沿原路快速收回。可以配合前脚小步上前以增加距离。","Pulling back before punching (telegraphing); dropping the hand on the way back; flaring the elbow; leaning forward.":"出拳前先往后拉（预告）；收回时手往下掉；手肘向外甩；身体往前倾。","3 × 2-minute rounds of jabs only, in the air or on the bag — the return as fast as the punch.":"空击或沙袋只打刺拳 3 回合 × 2 分钟，重点是收手速度和出手一样快。","The jab finds range, distracts, breaks the opponent's rhythm and sets up every combination.":"刺拳用来量距离、干扰对方、打断对方节奏，并带出所有组合拳。","Cross":"后手直拳","Chin, face":"下巴、脸","Turn foot, hip, shoulder":"转脚、转髋、转肩","Rotational power":"转体发力","PIVOT THE BACK HEEL · TURN THE HIPS · LEAD GLOVE ON THE CHIN":"后脚跟转 · 转髋 · 前手护下巴","From your stance, pivot the back heel out so the hips and shoulders turn forward, and drive the rear hand straight out — power travels from the floor through the hips to the fist. The lead glove stays by your chin; return along the same line.":"从站架，后脚跟往外转、带动髋部与肩膀往前转，后手沿直线打出，力量从地面经腰传到拳头。打出时前手留在下巴旁，打完沿原路收回。","Arm-only punching; not turning the back heel; dropping the lead hand; leaving the weight out front.":"只用手臂；后脚跟不转；前手掉下来；打完身体停在前方。","10 slow reps of pivot → hip → punch, then 3 rounds on the bag.":"慢速练「转脚 → 转髋 → 出拳」10 次，再到沙袋打 3 回合。","The cross usually follows the jab and is the most common power punch.":"后手直拳常接在刺拳之后，是最常见的得分重拳。","Lead Hook":"前手勾拳","Hook":"勾拳","Side of the jaw":"下巴侧面","Elbow level, turn the body":"手肘抬平、转身","Short-range rotation":"近距离转体","ELBOW LEVEL WITH THE FIST · PIVOT · ARM AT ~90°":"手肘与拳同高 · 前脚转 · 手臂约 90°","Shift a little weight to the lead foot, pivot on it and turn the hips and shoulders together. Bend the arm to about 90° with the elbow raised level with the fist and swing it across into the side of the jaw. The arm shape stays fixed — the power comes from turning. Return to the guard. (In this side view the fist travels across, into the screen.)":"重心稍移到前脚，前脚脚尖往内转、髋部与肩膀一起转，手臂弯成约 90°，手肘抬到与拳头同高，拳头横向勾向对方下巴侧面。手臂的形状固定，力量来自转身。打完回到护头。（侧面动画中，拳头是朝画面内横向移动。）","Winding up wide into a looping swing; dropping the elbow; arm-only with no body turn; the other hand leaving the chin.":"手臂拉得太开（变成大甩拳）；手肘掉下来；只用手不转身；另一手离开下巴。","Hooks on pads, 3 × 10, then add them after a jab and cross (1-2-3).":"对手靶练勾拳 3 × 10，熟练后接在刺拳、直拳之后（1-2-3）。","The hook comes from outside the opponent's line of sight and is a classic knockout punch.":"勾拳从对方视线之外的角度打来，是经典的击倒拳。","Rear Uppercut":"后手上勾拳","Uppercut":"上勾拳","Under the chin":"下巴下方","Dip, then drive up":"先蹲再往上","Leg drive and rotation":"腿部与转体发力","DIP THE KNEES · DRIVE AND TURN · FIST TRAVELS UP":"膝盖微蹲 · 蹬地转髋 · 拳往上","At close range, dip the knees and lower the rear hand slightly (don't pull it behind you), then drive up through the legs and turn the hips so the fist travels upward into the chin, palm facing you. Snap back to the guard.":"近距离时，膝盖微蹲，后手稍微放低（不要拉到身后），接着双腿蹬地、转髋，让拳头由下往上打向对方下巴，拳心朝向自己。打完立刻回到护头。","Dropping the hand low and back (telegraphing); lifting with the arm only; throwing from too far; leaving the face open afterwards.":"手放得太低太靠后（会暴露意图）；只用手臂往上举；距离太远才出拳；打完后脸部暴露。","On pads or an uppercut bag, 3 × 10, feeling the legs drive.":"在手靶或上勾拳沙袋上练 3 × 10，感受腿部发力。","Uppercuts punish an opponent who ducks or leans in, especially in close exchanges.":"上勾拳专门惩罚低头或前倾靠近的对手，在近身缠斗时特别有效。","The 1-2 (Jab–Cross)":"一二连击（直拳–前手直拳）","Combination":"组合拳","Face, chin":"脸、下巴","One returns as the other fires":"一手收回的同时另一手出拳","Combination rhythm":"组合节奏","THE JAB OPENS · THE CROSS FIRES AS IT RETURNS":"刺拳开路 · 收回的同时打直拳","Throw the jab, and as it comes back pivot the back foot and turn the hips to fire the cross. No pause between the two, and never have both hands away from your face at once. Finish with both hands back in the guard.":"先打刺拳，刺拳收回的同时转后脚、转髋打出后手直拳。两拳之间不要停顿，也不要两手同时离开脸。打完两手都回到护头。","Pausing between punches; firing the cross before the jab returns; not guarding afterwards; falling forward off balance.":"两拳之间停顿；刺拳还没收回就打直拳；打完不回防；身体前倾失去平衡。","3 × 2-minute rounds in the air or on the bag, moving your feet after every 1-2.":"空击或沙袋 3 回合 × 2 分钟，每次打完 1-2 后都要移动脚步。","The 1-2 is the base of every combination; hooks and uppercuts follow from it.":"1-2 是所有组合拳的基础，后面可以接勾拳或上勾拳。","Slip":"闪躲（侧闪）","Defence":"防守","Make the punch miss":"让拳头落空","Small move, use the knees":"小动作、用膝盖","Reaction and timing":"反应与时机","BEND THE KNEES · HEAD OFF THE LINE · EYES ON THEM":"膝盖微弯 · 头移出直线 · 眼睛看对方","As a straight punch comes, bend the knees and shift the upper body slightly forward and to the side, moving your head off the punch's line so it slides over your shoulder. Keep it small, keep your eyes on them, and come straight back to stance or counter. (The side view can't show the sideways part — only the dip and lean.)":"对方直拳打来时，膝盖微弯、上身稍微往前侧方移动，把头移出拳头的直线，让拳头从肩膀上方擦过。动作要小，眼睛一直看着对方，闪完马上回到站架或反击。（侧面动画看不到左右移动，只能看到身体下沉前移。）","Slipping too far and losing balance; closing your eyes; bending only at the waist; never countering.":"闪太大、失去平衡；闭眼；只弯腰不弯膝；闪完不反击。","Slip along a rope line, 3 × 1 minute, then have a partner throw slow jabs.":"在双层绳或绳子旁练习左右闪躲 3 × 1 分钟，再请伙伴慢速出刺拳。","Slipping keeps both hands free to counter immediately.":"闪躲让双手保持自由，可以立刻反击。","Bob & Weave":"下潜闪躲","Duck under the hook":"从勾拳下穿过","Use the legs, not the waist":"用腿蹲、不弯腰","Leg strength and rhythm":"腿力与节奏","BEND THE KNEES · UNDER THE PUNCH · HANDS UP":"彎膝下蹲 · 头从拳下穿过 · 手护头","As a hook swings in, bend your knees and sink so your head passes under the punch, moving in a U shape and rising on the other side. Keep your back fairly straight, eyes on the opponent and hands up throughout.":"对方勾拳挥来时，弯膝往下蹲，让头从拳头下方穿过，以 U 字形路线移到另一侧再站起来。背部保持挺直、眼睛看对方、双手一直护头。","Bending at the waist and looking at the floor (blind, open to uppercuts); sinking so deep you can't come up; dropping the hands.":"弯腰低头（看不到对方、容易被上勾拳）；蹲太深站不起来；手掉下来。","Weave back and forth under a rope line, 3 × 1 minute.":"在拉好的绳子下左右穿梭 3 × 1 分钟。","Bobbing and weaving takes you under hooks and into position to counter from the side.":"下潜闪躲让你躲过勾拳，并在对方身侧反击。","Parry":"拍挡","Their glove":"对方的拳套","Small, fast, straight back":"小、快、马上回来","Reaction and hand control":"反应与手部控制","SHORT TAP · DON'T REACH · BACK TO THE CHIN":"后手短拍 · 不伸太远 · 立刻回下巴","As the jab comes, tap it aside with the palm of your rear glove just in front of your face. Don't reach out to meet it — move only a short distance in front of the face — then snap the glove back to your chin and counter.":"对方刺拳打来时，用后手掌心在脸前方短促地往前一拍，把拳头拨偏到一边。手不要伸出去迎，只在脸前一小段距离内动作，拍完立刻回到下巴，接着反击。","Reaching out for the punch (leaves an opening); too big a movement; not bringing the hand back; parrying without countering.":"手伸太远去迎拳（露出空当）；动作太大；拍完手没回来；只拍不反击。","Partner throws slow jabs while you parry, 3 × 1 minute; then add a counter cross after each parry.":"同伴慢速打刺拳，你练拍挡 3 × 1 分钟；熟练后加上拍挡后的反击直拳。","Parrying neutralises straight punches without stepping back and creates instant counters.":"拍挡让你不用后退就能化解直拳，并马上创造反击机会。","Footwork: Step & Drag":"前进与后退步法","Footwork":"步法","Control distance":"控制距离","The foot nearest the direction moves first":"先动的脚朝方向走","Distance and balance":"距离与平衡","FORWARD: LEAD FOOT FIRST · BACK: REAR FOOT FIRST · SAME WIDTH":"前进先动前脚 · 后退先动后脚 · 站距不变","To move forward, step the lead foot a short distance and bring the rear foot up the same amount; to move back, step the rear foot first and let the lead foot follow. Every step keeps your stance width, soft knees and hands up — never cross or bring the feet together.":"前进时前脚先踏出一小步，后脚立刻跟上同样距离；后退时后脚先往后踏，前脚跟上。每一步都保持站架宽度、膝盖微弯、双手护头，双脚不要交叉或并拢。","Crossing or closing the feet; steps too big; bouncing up and down; dropping the hands as you move.":"双脚交叉或并拢；步伐太大；移动时身体跳上跳下；手掉下来。","Along a line on the floor, 10 steps forward and back, 3 sets; then add punches as you move.":"在地上画一条线，沿线前进、后退各 10 步，3 组；再加上出拳。","Footwork controls distance — in range when you want to punch, out of range when you need to be.":"步法让你控制距离：该出拳时进得去，危险时退得出来。","Everything starts here":"所有动作的起点","Balance · protect the chin":"平衡 · 保护下巴","The most important punch in boxing":"拳击最重要的一拳","Measures distance, sets up":"量距离、开路","The main power punch":"最主要的重拳","Power comes from the ground":"力量来自地面","A short-range power punch":"近距离的重拳","The whole body turns":"整个身体一起转","An upward close-range punch":"由下往上的近身拳","Power from the legs":"腿部发力","Boxing's basic combination":"拳击最基本的组合","Smooth rhythm":"节奏流畅","Defence without the hands":"不用手的防守","Slip, then counter":"闪完马上反击","The answer to a hook":"躲勾拳的方法","A U-shaped path":"U 字形路线","Stops straight punches with minimal effort":"用最小的力气挡直拳","Redirect, don't block":"拨偏而不是硬挡","The root of good boxing":"好拳手的根本","Never cross the feet":"双脚不交叉","Stand side-on, feet about shoulder-width, knees soft, weight even":"侧身站，双脚约肩宽，膝盖微弯，重心平均","Gloves by the cheeks, elbows in front of the ribs":"双手护在脸颊两侧，手肘收在肋骨前","Chin down, eyes on the opponent over your gloves":"下巴收、眼睛从手套上方看对方","Stance":"站架","Snap the lead hand straight out, turning it palm-down":"前手直线打出，拳头转成拳心向下","Bring it straight back to the face":"原路收回护脸","Turn the back heel, hips and shoulders and throw the rear hand straight":"后脚跟转、髋肩转，后手直拳打出","Return — the lead glove guards the chin the whole time":"收回，前手一直护住下巴","Stance, at close range":"站架，近距离","Shift a little weight onto the lead foot":"重心稍移到前脚","Pivot the lead foot and turn the hips; elbow up level with the fist, which swings across":"前脚转、髋转，手肘抬到与拳同高，拳头横向勾入","Back to the guard":"收回护头","Dip the knees and drop the rear hand slightly":"膝盖微蹲、后手稍微放低","Drive up through the legs, turn the hips and bring the fist up under the chin":"腿蹬地、转髋，拳头由下往上打向下巴","\"One\": the jab":"「一」：前手直拳","\"Two\": the cross fires as the jab comes back":"「二」：前手收回的同时打出后手直拳","Both hands back to the guard":"两手都回到护头","Stance; watch their shoulders":"站架；看对方的肩膀","They throw a jab":"对方出前手拳","Bend the knees and shift forward and to the side so the punch slides over your shoulder":"膝盖微弯、身体往前侧移，让拳头从肩膀上方擦过","Keep your eyes on them":"眼睛一直看着对方","Back to stance, ready to counter":"回到站架，准备反击","They swing a hook":"对方挥出勾拳","Bend the knees and drop under the punch — legs, not the waist":"弯膝盖往下蹲，头从拳头下方穿过（不是弯腰）","Move in a U shape and come up on the other side":"以U字路线移到另一侧站起","Back to stance; the hands stay up throughout":"回到站架，双手一直护头","A short tap forward with the rear glove knocks the jab off line":"后手短促地往前一拍，把拳头拨偏","The glove snaps straight back to the chin":"手立刻回到下巴","Counter straight after the parry":"拍挡后马上反击","Advance: the lead foot steps first, a small step":"前进：前脚先踏出一小步","The rear foot follows the same distance — stance width stays the same":"后脚跟上同样距离，站距不变","Retreat: the rear foot steps back first":"后退：后脚先往后踏","The lead foot follows — never cross the feet":"前脚跟回来，双脚不交叉","TARGET: ":"目标：","Relaxation":"放松","Speed":"速度","Range":"距离感","Shoulder endurance":"肩部耐力","Rotation":"转体发力","Pivot":"脚步转动","Shoulder & arm":"肩臂","Arm structure":"手臂结构","Lead-foot pivot":"前脚转动","Leg drive":"腿部蹬地","Close range":"近身距离","Rhythm":"节奏","Reaction":"反应","Legs":"腿部","Hand control":"手部控制","Distance control":"距离控制","Leg endurance":"腿部耐力","Lesson {n} of 10 · {type}":"第 {n} 课 / 共 10 课 · {type}","Punch numbers":"拳的编号","Coaches call combinations by number: 1 jab, 2 cross, 3 lead hook, 4 rear hook, 5 lead uppercut, 6 rear uppercut. \"1-2-3\" means jab, cross, lead hook. Some gyms number them slightly differently.":"教练常用数字喊组合：1 刺拳、2 后手直拳、3 前手勾拳、4 后手勾拳、5 前手上勾拳、6 后手上勾拳。例如「1-2-3」就是刺拳、直拳接前手勾拳。不同拳馆的编号可能略有不同。","The ten lessons at a glance":"十堂课一览","Lesson":"课程","Target":"目标","Key point":"重点","A beginner session":"初学者的一堂练习","Skip rope for 3 × 3-minute rounds to warm up.":"跳绳 3 回合 × 3 分钟热身。","Shadowbox for 2 rounds, focusing on stance, footwork and returning the hands.":"影子拳 2 回合，专注站架、步法和收手。","Heavy bag for 3 rounds: jabs, 1-2s and 1-2-3s.":"重沙袋 3 回合：刺拳、1-2、1-2-3。","Defence: 1 minute each of slips and bob-and-weaves.":"防守练习：闪躲与下潜各 1 分钟。","Finish with core work and stretching.":"以核心训练和伸展收操。","Gear and safety":"护具与安全","Always wrap your hands and wear gloves on the bag to protect wrists and knuckles; add a mouthguard and headgear to spar, and only spar under a coach's supervision. Stop and see a doctor after any blow to the head that leaves you dizzy, with a headache or nauseous.":"打沙袋一定要缠手带并戴拳套，保护手腕和指节；对打时加上护齿和头盔，并且只在教练监督下进行。头部受到重击后出现头晕、头痛或恶心，必须停止训练并就医。","Want kicks, knees and elbows too? See <a href=\"../muay-thai/\">Muay Thai basics</a>.":"想同时学踢、膝、肘？看看 <a href=\"../muay-thai/\">泰拳入门 10 招</a>。","What does \"1-2\" mean?":"「1-2」是什么意思？","A jab followed by a cross — boxing's basic combination.":"刺拳接后手直拳，是拳击最基本的组合。","Slip or bob and weave — what's the difference?":"闪躲和下潜有什么不同？","A slip moves the head slightly sideways to beat a straight punch; a bob and weave bends the knees to duck under a hook in a U shape.":"闪躲是头往旁边小幅移动，躲直拳；下潜是弯膝盖从勾拳下方以 U 字形穿过。","Can I practise without a partner?":"没有对手可以练吗？","Yes — shadowboxing, the heavy bag and skipping are all solo, and you can practise bobbing under a rope. Sparring needs a coach and partner.":"可以。空击、沙袋和跳绳都能单独练；防守可以用拉好的绳子练下潜。对打则需要教练和伙伴。","Boxing":"拳击","FIGHTING SPORTS · BOXING FOR BEGINNERS":"格斗技 · 拳击入门","Boxing Basics: Punches, Defence & Footwork in 10 Lessons":"拳击入门：出拳、防守与步法 10 课","Start with the stance, then learn the four basic punches, the first combination, three ways to defend — slip, bob and weave, parry — and how to step in and out. The grey figure is the opponent and the red ring shows where a punch lands; lefties press SOUTHPAW.":"从站架开始，学会四种基本拳、最基本的组合，以及闪躲、下潜、拍挡三种防守和前进后退的步法。灰色人形是对手，红圈标示击中的位置；左撇子请按「反架」。","Lead hook":"前手勾拳","Rear hook":"后手勾拳","Lead uppercut":"前手上勾","Rear uppercut":"后手上勾","Basic punches":"基本拳种","Jab · cross · hook · uppercut":"刺拳 · 直拳 · 勾拳 · 上勾拳","Key point, this lesson":"本课重点","Amateur bout":"业余赛制","3 rounds × 3 minutes (varies by category)":"3 回合 × 3 分钟（各组别略有不同）","Lessons you have mastered":"课程掌握进度","Mark each lesson as mastered below":"可在下方标记为「已熟悉」","Pick a lesson (best learned in order)":"选择课程（建议依序学习）","In the ring":"实战用途","SIDE · GREY = OPPONENT":"侧面 · 灰色＝对手","ORTHODOX":"正架","SOUTHPAW":"反架","What this lesson trains":"此课训练重点","For education only; the animations are simplified. Boxing is a contact sport: train under a qualified coach, wrap your hands and wear gloves on the bag, and wear a mouthguard and headgear to spar.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，动画为简化示意。拳击是接触性运动：请在合格教练指导下训练，打沙袋要缠手带、戴拳套，对打要戴护齿与头盔。","Boxing Basics: Stance, Jab, Cross, Hook, Uppercut & Defence — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"拳击基础：站姿、Jab、Cross、Hook、Uppercut 与防守 — 互动指南 | KungfuTutor","Learn 10 boxing fundamentals with animated demos against an opponent: stance and guard, jab, cross, lead hook, rear uppercut, the 1-2, slip, bob and weave, parry and footwork — with mistakes and drills.":"通过与对手对打的动画示范，学习 10 项拳击基本功：站姿与护手、Jab、Cross、前手勾拳、后手上勾拳、1-2、闪避、低头摇闪、格挡与步法，并附常见错误与练习方法。","Boxing Basics — Punches, Defence & Footwork, Step by Step":"拳击基础——出拳、防守与步法，循序渐进","What are the basic punches in boxing?":"拳击的基本拳法有哪些？","The jab, the cross, the hook and the uppercut. Coaches often number them: 1 jab, 2 cross, 3 lead hook, 4 rear hook, 5 lead uppercut, 6 rear uppercut.":"分别是刺拳（Jab）、直拳（Cross）、勾拳（Hook）和上勾拳（Uppercut）。教练常为它们编号：1 Jab、2 Cross、3 前手 Hook、4 后手 Hook、5 前手 Uppercut、6 后手 Uppercut。","What does 1-2 mean in boxing?":"拳击中的「1-2」是什么意思？","A jab followed immediately by a cross — the most basic boxing combination.":"刺拳后紧接着一记直拳——是最基本的拳击组合。","What is the difference between a slip and a bob and weave?":"闪避（Slip）和低头摇闪（Bob and Weave）有什么区别？","A slip moves the head a little to the side to make a straight punch miss; a bob and weave bends the knees to duck under a hook in a U-shaped path.":"闪避是将头部稍微侧移，让直线拳落空；低头摇闪则是屈膝，沿U形路线低身闪过勾拳。","Stance & Grip":"站姿与握棍","Single stick":"单棍","Control and balance":"控制与平衡","BUTT SHOWING · FIRM, NOT TENSE · LIVE HAND UP":"棍尾外露 · 握紧不僵 · 活手护胸","Hold the stick in a full grip with two or three finger-widths of the butt (punyo) showing below your little finger — it is used for close strikes and hooking. Grip firmly but not rigidly so the wrist can turn freely. Keep the weapon hand in front with the stick up; the other hand, the \"live hand\", stays by your chest ready to check, push or grab. Stand with feet staggered and knees soft.":"用整只手握住棍子，让棍尾（punyo）在小指下方露出两到三指宽，用于近身打击和勾挂。握得稳但不要僵硬，让手腕能自由转动。持棍的手在前，棍子竖起；另一只手称为“活手”，放在胸前，随时准备挡、推或抓。双脚前后错开站立，膝盖放松微屈。","Holding the very end (poor control, easy to knock away); gripping so hard the wrist locks; letting the live hand hang; standing too upright.":"握在棍子最尾端（控制差、容易被打掉）；握太紧手腕僵硬；活手垂下不动；站得太直。","Hold the ready stance with the stick and move forward and back for a minute, checking the butt and the live hand.":"持棍保持戒备姿势并前后移动 1 分钟，检查棍尾外露与活手位置。","FMA usually teaches the weapon first; a correct grip and an active live hand underpin everything else.":"FMA 先学武器再学空手，正确的握法与活手习惯是所有技术的基础。","Forehand Diagonal Strike":"正手斜劈","Strike":"反击","Upper part of the stick":"棍子前段","Hip turn and wrist":"转髋与手腕","COCK OVER THE SHOULDER · DIAGONAL DOWN · FOLLOW THROUGH":"收到肩上 · 斜线往下 · 打穿目标","Cock the stick over the shoulder on your weapon side, then turn the hips so the body drives the arm and the stick travels down a diagonal to the side of the head or the collarbone, following through past the opposite hip instead of stopping on the target. The live hand stays by your chest. Many systems call this line \"angle 1\", though the numbering varies between styles.":"把棍子收到持棍手同侧的肩上，转髋让身体带动手臂，棍子沿着斜线由上往下打向对方头侧或锁骨，然后顺势打穿到另一侧髋部，不要停在目标上。活手保持在胸前。很多流派把这条斜线称为「第一角度」，但编号因流派而异。","Arm only, no hip turn; stopping on the target (weak, easy to grab); dropping the live hand; a big telegraphed loop behind you.":"只用手臂不转髋；打到目标就停住（力量小、容易被抓）；活手垂下；棍子在身后绕大圈预告动作。","20 slow strikes on a tyre or striking post, then speed up; train both hands.":"对着轮胎或打击柱慢速练 20 次，再逐渐加快，左右手都要练。","The forehand diagonal is the most natural, powerful line, and almost every FMA style starts with it.":"正手斜劈是最自然、最有力的打击线，几乎所有 FMA 流派都从它开始。","Backhand Diagonal Strike":"反手斜劈","Turning back the other way":"反方向转体","TO THE OTHER SHOULDER · BACK OF HAND OUT · TURN BACK THROUGH":"收到另一肩 · 手背朝外 · 转回打穿","Bring the stick across to your opposite shoulder with the back of the hand facing out, then turn the body back so the stick travels down the opposite diagonal to the other side of the head, following through to your weapon side. Forehand and backhand are usually thrown together. (In the side view the two diagonals look alike — the difference is which shoulder they start from.)":"把棍子收到另一侧肩上，手背朝外，接着身体转回来，带动棍子沿相反的斜线由上往下打向对方另一侧头部，再打穿回到持棍侧。正手和反手常常连在一起打。（侧面动画中两种斜劈看起来相似，差别在于从哪一侧的肩膀出发。）","Lifting the elbow too high in a big wind-up; flicking from the wrist only; no body turn; the live hand getting in the way.":"手肘抬太高、动作太大；只用手腕甩；身体不转回；活手挡住自己的路线。","Forehand + backhand pairs, 20 per set, 3 sets.":"正手 + 反手连续打 20 次为一组，练 3 组。","Paired with the forehand, it lets you strike from both sides without a gap.":"正反手配合，让你可以从两边连续攻击，不给对方空档。","Thrust to the Body":"直刺至身体","Thrust":"刺击","Stick tip":"棍尖","Range and speed":"距离与速度","DRAW TO THE HIP · STEP IN · STRAIGHT LINE":"收到腰侧 · 上步 · 直线刺出","Draw the stick back to your hip with the tip forward, then step in with the lead foot and extend the arm so the tip drives straight into the stomach, and recover to the ready stance. The thrust takes the shortest path and is often used to interrupt the opponent.":"棍子收到腰侧、棍尖朝前，接着前脚上步、手臂伸直，棍尖沿直线刺向对方腹部，然后收回戒备。刺击路线最短，常用来打断对方的动作。","The tip wobbling up and down; reaching without stepping; leaving the stick out where it can be grabbed.":"棍尖上下晃动；没有上步只伸手；刺完停在前面被抓住棍子。","Thrust at a hanging ball or soft target, 3 × 10, hitting the same spot every time.":"对着挂起的网球或软靶刺击 3 × 10，要求每次都刺中同一点。","In FMA the thrust also underpins blade work; it trains a straight line and distance.":"刺击在 FMA 也是持刀技术的基础，训练的是直线与距离感。","Figure-8 Flow":"8 字流动","Flow drill":"流动练习","Flow and wrist":"流畅与手腕","FOREHAND → ROLL THE WRIST → BACKHAND → NON-STOP":"正手 → 翻腕 → 反手 → 不停","Throw a forehand diagonal, roll the wrist as you follow through so the stick loops up to the other shoulder, throw a backhand diagonal, then roll back again — the two diagonals cross in front of you in a figure 8 that never stops. Start slowly and speed up as it becomes smooth.":"先打正手斜劈，打穿后手腕翻转，让棍子绕到另一侧肩上，接着打反手斜劈，再翻腕回到原侧，两条斜线在身体前方交叉成 8 字形，一直流动不停。先慢慢做，熟练后加快速度。","Pausing between strikes; drawing big circles with the arm instead of the wrist; a stiff body; watching the stick instead of looking ahead.":"每一下之间停顿；用手臂画大圈而不是用手腕；身体僵硬；眼睛看棍子不看前方。","3 × 1 minute a day, alternating hands, adding steps forward and back.":"每天 3 × 1 分钟，左右手轮流，可以配合前进后退的步法。","Flow drills make your attacks continuous and lead into the double-stick weaving drills (sinawali).":"流动练习让攻击连续不断，也是 FMA 双棍编织练习（Sinawali）的基础。","Roof Block & Counter":"屋顶挡与反击","Defend + counter":"防守 + 反击","The sloping stick":"棍子斜面","Timing and flow":"时机与流动","HAND OVERHEAD · TIP SLOPES DOWN AND BACK · FLOW INTO THE COUNTER":"手举头上 · 棍尖斜向后下 · 顺势反击","As a strike comes down from above, raise your weapon hand above your head with the tip sloping down and back, like a roof, so their stick slides off along yours instead of meeting it head-on. Let the stick flow on round to your shoulder and counter at once with a forehand.":"对方从上方劈下时，把持棍的手举过头顶，棍尖斜向后下方，像屋顶一样，让对方的棍子沿着你的棍子滑开，而不是正面硬碰。然后让棍子顺势绕到肩上，立刻用正手反击。","Blocking flat and square (jars the hand and can break the stick); not raising the hand high enough; stopping after the block.":"水平、正面硬挡（会震痛手，还可能打断棍子）；手举得不够高；挡完就停住。","Partner strikes slowly from above while you roof-block and counter, sets of 10 — with protective gear and slow speed.":"同伴从上方慢速劈下，你练习屋顶挡 → 反击，每组 10 次。全程佩戴护具并慢速进行。","The roof block turns defence and attack into one flowing move — a good example of FMA's \"the block is the strike\" idea.":"屋顶挡把防守和攻击合为一个流畅的动作，是 FMA「以挡即是打」思想的好例子。","Live-Hand Check & Disarm":"活手检查与缴械","Live hand on their weapon hand":"活手按住对方的持械手","Control and coordination":"控制与协调","BLOCK · CHECK WITH THE LIVE HAND · STRIP DOWN · GET DISTANCE":"先挡 · 活手按住 · 往下剥离 · 拉开距离","Block their strike with your stick, then immediately pin their weapon hand or wrist with your live hand (the \"check\") so they cannot pull back for another strike. Use your stick to strip theirs downward out of their hand, then step back to a safe distance. It is one of the most basic disarms — always practise it slowly and with protective gear.":"先用你的棍子挡住对方的攻击，然后立刻用活手按住对方持械的手或手腕（即«检查»），让对方无法收回再次攻击。接着用你的棍子把对方的棍子从手中向下剥离，然后后退到安全距离。这是最基本的缴械动作之一，练习时一定要慢速并戴好护具。","Remembering the live hand only after the block (too slow); grabbing their stick instead of their hand (easily pulled away — and a blade would cut); staying close after the disarm.":"挡完才想起用活手（太慢）；抓住对方的棍子而不是手（容易被抽走，若是刀则会割伤）；缴械后仍留在近身。","Partner strikes very slowly while you block → check → strip, 10 reps; speed up only once it is smooth.":"伙伴非常慢地打下来，你练「挡 → 检查 → 剥离」10 次，熟练后才逐渐加快。","The live hand is a hallmark of FMA: the weapon hand attacks and defends, the live hand controls.":"活手是 FMA 的特色之一：持棍手负责攻防，活手负责控制。","Empty-Hand Application":"空手应用","Empty hand":"空手","Bottom of the fist or the palm":"拳底或手掌","Transfer and understanding":"转换与理解","SAME DIAGONAL · HAMMER FIST OR PALM · LIVE HAND STILL WORKS":"同样的斜线 · 锤拳或手刀 · 活手照样工作","A hallmark of FMA is that weapon and empty hand use the same angles and movements. Put the stick down and the forehand diagonal becomes a downward hammer fist or slashing palm, the backhand becomes a backhand slap or elbow, and the live-hand check works just the same. Train the stick well and your empty-hand skills improve at the same time.":"FMA 的特点是武器和空手使用同一套角度与动作。放下棍子后，正手斜劈的手部动作就变成由上往下的锤拳或手掌劈击，反手斜劈变成反手拍击或手肘，活手的检查也一样适用。所以练好棍法，空手技术也会同时进步。","Thinking empty hand is a separate system; hitting with the knuckles instead of the bottom of the fist; forgetting the live hand.":"以为空手要重新学一套；用指节打而不是拳底；忘了活手。","Do a drill 10 times with the stick, then 10 times empty-handed, feeling that the movement is identical.":"同一组练习先用棍子做 10 次，再空手做 10 次，感受动作完全相同。","This \"one set of angles, many tools\" principle is what makes FMA such a practical self-defence system.":"这个「一套角度、多种工具」的原则，让 FMA 成为很实用的自我防卫系统。","Leave a little butt showing":"棍尾留两三指","The live hand is always working":"活手永远在工作","Angle 1 in many systems":"许多流派的第一角度","High to low on a diagonal":"由上往下斜劈","Angle 2 in many systems":"许多流派的第二角度","The mirror of the forehand":"正手的镜像","The fastest, straightest attack":"最快、最直的攻击","Step with it":"上步配合","Forehand and backhand joined up":"正手反手连成一线","The key to a loose wrist":"手腕灵活的关键","Let their stick slide off":"让对方的棍子滑开","Counter straight after":"挡完立刻反击","Block → check → strip":"挡 → 检查 → 剥离","What the live hand is for":"活手的真正用途","Weapon and hand share the same angles":"武器与空手同一套角度","A core FMA idea":"FMA 的核心概念","Grip the stick with two or three finger-widths of butt showing below the hand":"握棍时棍尾留出约两到三指宽","Weapon hand forward with the stick up; the other, \"live\" hand guards the chest":"持棍手在前、棍子竖起，另一只手（活手）护在胸前","Feet staggered, knees soft, weight even":"双脚前后站立，膝盖微屈，重心均匀","Ready stance":"戒备姿势","Cock the stick over the shoulder on the weapon side":"棍子收到持棍手同侧的肩上","Turn the hips and swing down on a diagonal to the side of the head":"转髋，棍子沿斜线由上往下打向对方头侧","Follow through past the opposite hip — don't stop on the target":"顺势打穿到另一侧髋部，不要停在目标上","Recover to the ready stance":"收回戒备姿势","Bring the stick across to the opposite shoulder, back of the hand facing out":"棍子收到另一侧肩上，手背朝外","Swing back down on the opposite diagonal, the body turning back with it":"反手沿斜线往下打，身体随之转回","Follow through and finish on the weapon side":"打穿后回到持棍一侧","Draw the stick back to the hip, tip pointing forward":"棍子收到腰侧，棍尖朝前","Step in and drive the tip straight into the stomach, arm extending":"前脚上步，手臂伸直，棍尖直线刺向腹部","Back to the ready stance":"收回戒备","Forehand: from the shoulder, diagonally down":"正手：从肩上斜劈而下","Roll the wrist and loop the stick up to the other shoulder":"翻转手腕，棍子绕到另一侧肩上","Backhand: diagonally down — the two strikes join into a non-stop figure 8":"反手：斜劈而下——两击连成不间断的 8 字形","They raise the stick to strike down":"对方举棍从上往下打","Raise the weapon hand overhead with the tip sloping down and back, so their stick slides off":"持棍手举过头顶，棍尖斜向后下，让对方的棍子滑开","Let the stick flow on round to the shoulder":"顺势让棍子带到肩上","Counter straight away with a forehand":"立即以正手反击","Ready stance at close range":"近距离戒备姿势","They swing down":"对方挥棍打下","Block with your stick first":"先用棍子格挡","The live hand immediately checks their weapon hand":"活手立即控制对方持棍的手","Use your stick to strip theirs downward out of their hand":"用你的棍子把对方的棍子往下剥离其手","Step back to a safe distance":"后退，拉开安全距离","Put the stick down — same ready stance":"放下棍子，同样的戒备姿势","The hand moves exactly as in the forehand stick strike":"手的动作和正手棍法一样","The same diagonal becomes a hammer fist or a slashing palm":"同一条斜线，变成锤拳或手刀","Weapon and empty hand share the same angles":"武器与空手用同一套角度","Grip control":"握棍控制","Live-hand awareness":"活手意识","Hip rotation":"转髋","Wrist":"手腕","Accuracy":"准确度","Follow-through":"打穿目标","Flow":"流畅度","Wrist mobility":"手腕灵活","Angles":"角度","Counter":"反击","Transfer":"转换能力","Angle awareness":"角度理解","Live hand":"活手","Real speed":"实际速度","Contact: ":"联系点：","Lesson {n} of 8 · {type}":"第 {n} 课 · {type}","Kali, Eskrima, Arnis — what is the difference?":"Kali、Eskrima、Arnis 有什么不同？","All three are names for the Filipino martial arts (FMA); which one is used depends mostly on region and school, and the content overlaps a great deal. In 2009 the Philippines made arnis its national martial art and sport. What every style shares is weapons first — usually stick and blade — with the same angles then applied to the empty hand.":"这三个名称都是指菲律宾武术（FMA），用哪个名称主要取决于地区与流派，技术内容大同小异。菲律宾在 2009 年把 Arnis 定为国家武术与国家运动。所有流派的共同特色是：先学武器（通常是棍与刀），再把同一套角度用在空手。","Tool":"工具","The angle system":"「角度」系统","Instead of memorising individual techniques, FMA sorts attacks into a few \"angles\": forehand and backhand diagonals from above, horizontal strikes, rising diagonals from below, and thrusts. Each style numbers them differently (commonly 5 to 12), but the principle is the same: learn to defend each angle and you can answer a stick, a blade or an empty hand the same way.":"FMA 不是记住一招一式，而是把攻击分成几条「角度」：由上往下的正手与反手斜劈、水平横打、由下往上的斜撩，以及直刺。每个流派的角度编号和数量不同（常见 5 到 12 个），但原则相同：只要学会防守每一条角度，不管对方拿的是棍、刀或空手，都能用同一套方法应对。","Practise safely":"安全练习","Train alone or on a tyre or striking post before partner drills.":"先单独练习或打轮胎、打击柱，再和伙伴对练。","Wear a helmet, hand and eye protection for partner drills, starting very slowly.":"对练时戴头盔、护手与护目，从非常慢的速度开始。","Use rattan or foam training sticks — never hardwood or metal for partner work.":"使用藤棍或泡棉训练棍，不要用硬木或金属棍对练。","Blade work uses blunt trainers only, under an instructor.":"刀术只用钝的训练刀，并且只在教练指导下练习。","Related: <a href=\"../../self-defence/krav-maga/\">Krav Maga basics</a> and <a href=\"../../kungfu/wing-chun/\">Wing Chun basics</a>.":"相关课程：<a href=\"../../self-defence/krav-maga/\">以色列格斗术入门</a>、<a href=\"../../kungfu/wing-chun/\">咏春入门</a>。","Why learn the weapon first?":"为什么要先学武器？","A weapon magnifies mistakes, making distance, angles and timing easier to learn — and the same movements carry straight over to the empty hand.":"武器会放大错误，让距离、角度与时机更容易学会；而且同一套动作可以直接用在空手。","What is the live hand?":"什么是活手？","The hand without the weapon, used to check, push or control the opponent's weapon hand.":"没有拿武器的那只手，用来检查、推开或控制对方持武器的手。","What equipment do I need?":"需要什么装备？","One or two rattan sticks of about 70 cm to start; add a helmet and hand protection for partner work.":"一到两根约 70 厘米的藤棍就可以开始；对练时再加上头盔与护手。","Kali / Eskrima / Arnis":"菲律宾武术","FIGHTING ARTS · FILIPINO MARTIAL ARTS FOR BEGINNERS":"格斗技 · 菲律宾武术入门","Filipino Martial Arts Basics: Kali, Eskrima & Arnis Stick in 8 Lessons":"菲律宾武术（Kali / Eskrima / Arnis）入门：棍法 8 课","Filipino martial arts teach the weapon first and the empty hand second, using the same angles for stick, blade and hand. These 8 lessons use the single stick (baston): stance, diagonal strikes, the thrust, figure-8 flow, the roof block, the live-hand check and disarm, and finally the same angles with the empty hand. The brown stick is yours; the grey figure is your training partner.":"菲律宾武术先学武器、再学空手，同一套角度用在棍、刀与徒手上。这 8 课用单棍（baston）学站姿、斜劈、直刺、8 字流动、屋顶挡、活手检查与缴械，最后把同样的角度用在空手。棕色是你的棍子，灰色人形是练习伙伴。","Three names":"三个名称","Depends on region and school":"依地区与流派而异","Tool in this lesson":"本课动作使用的工具","Stick length":"棍长","Traditionally rattan":"传统为藤棍（rattan）","SIDE · GREY = PARTNER":"侧面 · 灰色＝伙伴","RIGHT HAND":"右手持棍","LEFT HAND":"左手持棍","For education only; the animations are simplified. Train stick work under a qualified instructor, wear a helmet, hand and eye protection for partner drills and start slowly. This page does not cover live-blade training.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，动画为简化示意。棍法练习请在合格教练指导下进行，对练时戴头盔、护手与护目，并从慢速开始；本页不包含刀术对练。","Filipino Martial Arts Basics: Kali, Eskrima & Arnis Stick Fighting — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"菲律宾武术基础：Kali、Eskrima 与 Arnis 棍术——互动指南 | KungfuTutor","Learn 8 Filipino martial arts (Kali, Eskrima, Arnis) basics with animated stick demos: stance and grip, forehand and backhand diagonal strikes, thrust, figure-8 flow, roof block and counter, live-hand check and disarm, and empty-hand application.":"通过动画棍法示范，学习8种菲律宾武术（Kali、Eskrima、Arnis）的基础：站姿与握法、正手与反手斜向击打、刺击、8字回转动作、屋顶格挡与反击、活手检查与缴械，以及空手应用。","Kali, Eskrima & Arnis Basics — Stick Fighting, Step by Step":"Kali、Eskrima 与 Arnis 基础——循序渐进学棍术","What is the difference between Kali, Eskrima and Arnis?":"Kali、Eskrima 和 Arnis 有什么区别？","They are three common names for the Filipino martial arts; which name is used depends largely on region and school. All of them train weapons first, usually sticks and blades, and apply the same angles to empty-hand fighting.":"它们是菲律宾武术的三个常见名称，具体用哪个名称很大程度上取决于地区和门派。它们都先练习武器，通常是棍和刀，并把相同的角度运用到徒手格斗中。","Why do Filipino martial arts start with weapons?":"菲律宾武术为什么先从武器练起？","Because the same angles and movements carry over to the empty hand: a forehand stick strike becomes a hammer fist or palm strike, and the live-hand check works the same way.":"因为相同的角度和动作可以转用到空手上：正手棍击会变成锤拳或掌击，活手检查的运作方式也相同。","What is the live hand in FMA?":"FMA 中的活手是什么？","The hand that does not hold the weapon. It checks, pushes, grabs and controls the opponent's weapon hand while the weapon hand attacks and defends.":"不持武器的那只手。当持武器的手在进攻和防守时，它负责格挡、推开、抓住并控制对方持武器的手。","What is judo?":"什么是柔道？","Judo is a Japanese martial art founded by Jigoro Kano in Tokyo in 1882. He took the older jujutsu styles, removed the most dangerous techniques and kept throws, hold-downs, chokes and armlocks that can be practised at full effort safely; his school is the Kodokan. Judo means \"the gentle way\": use the partner's force and balance instead of meeting strength with strength. Judo joined the Olympics at Tokyo 1964, and women's judo has been an Olympic event since 1992.":"柔道是嘉纳治五郎于1882年在东京创立的日本武道。他保留了传统柔术的摔法、压制、勒颈和关节技，去掉了其中最危险的技术，使这些技术可以在全力练习时保持安全；他的道场叫“讲道馆”。柔道的意思是“柔之道”：利用对方的力量和平衡，而不是以力对力。柔道于东京1964年奥运会成为奥运项目，女子柔道自1992年起成为奥运项目。","Ippon wins the match at once: a throw that lands the opponent largely on their back with force and speed, a 20-second hold-down, or a submission to a choke or armlock. A less complete throw, or a 10-second hold-down, is waza-ari, and two waza-ari add up to ippon. The International Judo Federation reviews its rules every few years, so check the current version before a competition.":"一本会立即赢得比赛：以有力、快速的方式把对手摔到大致背部着地；将对手压制20秒；或让对手因勒颈或关节技而认输。摔得不够完整，或压制10秒，是技有；两个技有合计为一本。国际柔道联合会每隔几年会检讨规则，因此比赛前请查看最新版本。","Modern judo rules do not allow gripping, hooking or touching the opponent's legs with the hands — it is penalised with shido. This is one of the biggest differences from sambo and wrestling.":"现代柔道规则不允许用手抓、勾或碰对方的腿，违者会被判“指导”（shido）；这是柔道与桑搏、摔跤最大的区别之一。","Learn to breakfall before you learn any throw.":"先学会受身（安全倒地），再学任何摔法。","Practise throws and locks only on mats, with a coach.":"摔法和关节技只在软垫上、在教练指导下练习。","Keep hold of the sleeve when you throw so your partner can breakfall.":"摔对方时拉住袖子，让对方可以做好受身。","Apply armlocks slowly and let go the moment your partner taps or says \"maitta\"; tap early yourself when caught.":"关节技要慢慢施压：对方一拍地或说“maitta”，就马上放开；被锁时尽早拍地认输。","Related: <a href=\"../sambo/\">sambo basics</a>, <a href=\"../mma/\">MMA basics</a> and <a href=\"../../self-defence/basics/\">self-defence basics</a>.":"相关课程：<a href=\"../sambo/\">桑搏入门</a>、<a href=\"../mma/\">MMA 入门</a>、<a href=\"../../self-defence/basics/\">自我防卫基础</a>。","How is judo different from sambo?":"柔道和桑搏有什么不同？","Both throw in a jacket. Judo has chokes but bans grabbing the legs with the hands and allows locks on the elbow only; sport sambo allows leg grabs and leg locks but no chokes.":"两者都穿外套摔人。柔道有勒颈，但禁止用手抓腿，关节技只能锁手肘；运动桑搏允许抓腿和腿部关节技，但没有勒颈。","Etiquette, breakfalls, posture and grips, then basic throws such as the foot sweep and major outer reap, and the scarf hold-down.":"礼仪、受身、自然体与组手，然后是出足扫、大外刈等基本摔法和袈裟固。","What do the belt colours mean?":"腰带颜色代表什么？","Beginners wear a white belt and move through coloured belts as they grade (the order differs by country). A black belt marks the dan grades — in judo it is seen as the real start of learning.":"初学者系白带，随着考级换成不同颜色（各国顺序不同），黑带代表达到段位，但在柔道里黑带被看作真正学习的开始。","FIGHTING SPORTS · JUDO FOR BEGINNERS":"格斗技 · 柔道入门","Judo Basics: Breakfalls, Throws, Hold-Downs and the Armlock in 8 Lessons":"柔道入门：受身、摔、压制与关节技 8 课","Judo is a Japanese martial art and Olympic sport founded by Jigoro Kano in Tokyo in 1882; the name means \"the gentle way\". These 8 lessons start with the bow, posture and grips, teach you to fall safely, then four basic throws, the scarf hold-down and the cross armlock. Blue judogi is you, white is your partner; the red ring marks the point of contact.":"柔道是 1882 年由嘉纳治五郎在东京创立的日本武道，也是奥运项目，意思是「柔之道」。这 8 课从礼、自然体与组手开始，学会受身，再学四种基本摔法、袈裟固压制与腕挫十字固。蓝色柔道服是你，白色是伙伴，红圈标示接触点。","Ukemi":"受身","Nage-waza":"投技","Foot and hip throws":"足技与腰技","Katame-waza":"固技","Hold-downs and the armlock":"压制与关节技","Founded":"创立年份","Jigoro Kano · Kodokan, Tokyo":"嘉纳治五郎 · 东京讲道馆","Hold-down for ippon":"压制一本","10 seconds is waza-ari, 20 seconds is ippon":"压制 10 秒是技有，20 秒是一本","For education only; the animations are simplified. Learn to breakfall first, and practise throws and locks only on mats with a qualified coach; apply locks slowly and let go the moment your partner taps. Chokes and armlocks are usually taught only to older students.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，动画为简化示意。请先学会受身，摔法与关节技只在有合格教练的软垫上练习；关节技要慢慢施压，对方拍地立即放开。勒颈与关节技通常只教给较年长的学员。","Judo Basics: Bow, Breakfalls, Throws, Hold-Downs & Armlock — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"柔道基础：礼仪、倒法、投技、固技与关节技——互动指南 | KungfuTutor","Learn 8 judo fundamentals with animated demos against a partner: bow, posture and grips, the back breakfall, advanced foot sweep, major outer reap, minor inner reap, major hip throw, scarf hold-down and the cross armlock.":"通过与搭档的动画示范，学习 8 项柔道基础：行礼、姿势与握法、背部倒法、高级扫脚、大外刈、小内刈、大腰投、袈裟固压制和十字固关节技。","Judo Basics — Throws, Hold-Downs and the Armlock, Step by Step":"柔道基础——投技、固技与关节技，循序渐进","A Japanese martial art and Olympic sport founded by Jigoro Kano in Tokyo in 1882. Players wear a jacket (judogi) and win by throwing, holding down or making the opponent submit. The name means 'the gentle way'.":"一种日本武术，也是奥运项目，由嘉纳治五郎于1882年在东京创立。选手穿着道服（judogi），通过投摔、压制或使对手认输来获胜。这个名字的意思是「柔和之道」。","How do you score ippon in judo?":"柔道中如何得到一本？","By throwing the opponent largely onto their back with force and speed, by holding them down for 20 seconds, or by making them submit to a choke or armlock. Two waza-ari also add up to ippon.":"以力量和速度将对手大幅度摔到背部着地、压制对手20秒，或使对手因绞技或关节技认输。两个技有效也可合计为一本。","Can you grab the legs in judo?":"柔道中可以抓腿吗？","No. Under International Judo Federation rules, gripping, hooking or touching the legs with the hands is not allowed and is penalised with shido.":"不可以。根据国际柔道联合会的规则，用手抓、勾或触摸腿部是不允许的，会被判罚shido（指导）。","Bow, Posture and Grips":"礼、自然体与组手","Lapel and sleeve":"衣领与袖子","Standing":"站立","Gripping and balance":"抓握与平衡","BOW · NATURAL POSTURE · LAPEL · SLEEVE":"鞠躬 · 自然体 · 前手领 · 后手袖","Bow to your partner (rei) before and after practice. Stand in natural posture (shizentai): feet shoulder-width apart, knees soft, back straight, weight between both feet. Move with sliding steps, feet close to the mat. The lead hand grips their lapel and the rear hand grips the sleeve just below the elbow — the grip (kumikata). Then pull the sleeve and lift the lapel to move their weight onto their toes or heels. This is kuzushi, breaking the balance, and it comes before every throw.":"练习前后互相鞠躬（礼）。站成自然体：双脚与肩同宽、膝盖微弯、背挺直，重心在两脚中间。移动时用滑步，脚底贴近垫子。前手抓对方衣领，后手抓对方手肘下方的袖子，这叫组手。抓好后拉袖、提领，让对方的重心移到脚尖或脚跟，这叫破势（崩し），是每一个摔法的准备。","Bending forward with the head down (an over-defensive posture); crossing the feet as you walk (easy to sweep); gripping so hard the arms go stiff; holding on without breaking the balance.":"弯腰低头（防守姿势过低）；走路时双脚交叉（容易被扫）；抓得太紧、手臂僵硬；只抓不破势。","Grip up with a partner and move around the mat for 3 × 1 minute, taking turns to pull and push them off balance without throwing.":"和伙伴抓好后，在软垫上移动 3 × 1 分钟，轮流练习拉、推让对方失去平衡（不摔）。","Judo is fought in a jacket, so the grip fight decides who throws first — and the bow is at the heart of the sport.":"柔道比赛穿柔道服，组手决定谁能先发动摔法；柔道的「礼」是这项运动的核心。","Back Breakfall":"后倒受身","Breakfall":"受身","Both arms slap the mat":"双臂拍垫","Falling":"倒地","CHIN TUCKED · ROUND BACK · SLAP THE MAT":"下巴贴胸 · 圆背滚 · 双手拍垫","From standing, squat down with the chin on your chest and eyes on your belt knot. Sit the hips down just behind your heels and roll back with a rounded back. As your back meets the mat, slap it with both whole arms at about 45° from your body to spread the impact. Your head never touches the mat. Judo also has side, front and rolling breakfalls — learn each one with a coach.":"从站立深蹲下去，下巴贴胸、眼睛看自己的腰带结。臀部坐在脚跟后方，背部弓圆往后滚。背部着地的同时，双臂在身体两侧约 45° 用整只手臂拍垫，把冲击分散掉。头始终不碰地。柔道还有侧受身、前受身和前回转受身，都要在教练指导下学。","Letting the head snap back onto the mat; putting a hand down to catch yourself (hurts the wrist and elbow); falling flat like a board; slapping too late.":"头往后仰撞地；用手撑地（容易伤手腕和手肘）；背部挺直像木板一样倒下；拍垫太晚。","10 rolls from sitting, then 10 from a squat, then 10 from standing — always on mats.":"先从坐姿往后滚拍垫 10 次，再从蹲姿 10 次，最后从站姿 10 次。只在软垫上练习。","In judo you will be thrown a lot; a good breakfall is what lets you train safely for years.":"柔道的意思是「柔之道」，你会被摔很多次。好的受身让你可以安全地练习很多年。","Advanced Foot Sweep":"出足扫","Foot technique":"足技","Sole against the ankle":"脚掌贴着脚踝扫","Standing → ground":"站立 → 地面","Timing and rhythm":"时机与节奏","THEY STEP · SWEEP BEFORE THE WEIGHT LANDS":"对方踏步 · 重心落下前扫脚","Grip up and move with them. As they step forward and the foot is about to land — before their weight is on it — sweep the sole of your foot against their ankle in the direction their toes point, while your hands pull and turn their upper body. With the foot gone and the body turned, they fall.":"组手后跟着对方移动。当对方往前踏步、脚快要落地但重心还没放上去时，用你的脚底贴着对方脚踝，往对方脚尖的方向扫，同时双手拉转对方的上身。脚被扫走、上身被转，对方就会倒下。","Kicking the shin (it is a sweep, not a kick); sweeping too late when their weight is already down; using only the foot and not the hands; losing your own balance afterwards.":"踢对方的小腿（是扫，不是踢）；扫得太晚，对方重心已经放上去；只用脚不用手；扫完自己失去平衡。","Partner walks slowly back and forth; you just practise touching the sweep at the right moment, 20 times, without throwing.":"搭档慢慢地前后走动；你只练习在正确的时机轻扫脚踝，练 20 次，不必摔倒对方。","With the right timing it takes almost no strength — the clearest example of judo's \"gentle way\".":"时机对了几乎不用力气，是「柔能制刚」最好的例子。","Major Outer Reap":"大外刈","Back of thigh against back of thigh":"大腿后侧刈大腿后侧","Drive and balance":"推进与平衡","WEIGHT ON THE HEELS · SWING · REAP BACK · CHEST FORWARD":"重心到脚跟 · 摆腿 · 往后刈 · 胸往前","Pull the sleeve and push the lapel to put their weight on their heels. Plant your support foot beside theirs, swing your reaping leg forward past their leg, then reap back so the back of your thigh hits the back of theirs while your chest drives forward. Without its supporting leg their body falls back. Stay on your feet and keep the sleeve so they can breakfall.":"拉袖、推领，让对方的重心落到脚跟。支撑脚踏到对方脚旁边，刈脚往前摆过对方的腿，再用你大腿后侧往后刈对方大腿后侧，同时胸口往前压。对方失去支撑脚，往后倒。你站稳，拉住袖子让对方受身。","Reaping before breaking the balance (they are rooted); support foot too far away; using the leg without the upper body; letting go of the sleeve (makes their breakfall harder).":"没先破势就刈（对方站得很稳）；支撑脚离太远；只用脚不用上身；刈完放开袖子（对方受身困难）。","With your partner standing still, drill step, swing and reap slowly 10 times each side without throwing; then full throws on mats with your partner breakfalling.":"伙伴站好，你慢速练「踏步 + 摆腿 + 刈」各 10 次不摔；之后在垫上完整练，伙伴做后受身。","Works best when they stand tall with their weight back, and finishes many combinations.":"当对方站得直、重心在后时特别有效，也是很多组合技的终点。","Minor Inner Reap":"小内刈","Sole hooks the heel":"脚底勾脚跟","Speed and linking":"速度与连接","PUSH BACK · HOOK THE HEEL INSIDE · REAP TO THE TOES":"推后 · 从内侧勾脚跟 · 往脚尖方向刈","Close in and push them back so their weight sits on their lead foot. From between their legs, hook behind that heel with the sole of your foot and reap it towards their toes while both hands drive them back. With the foot gone, they fall backwards.":"靠近对方并往后推，让对方的重量压在前脚上。用脚底从两腿中间勾住对方前脚的脚跟，往对方脚尖的方向刈，同时双手往后推。对方的脚被刈走，往后倒下。","Reaping a foot with no weight on it (it just moves); kicking with the toes instead of hooking with the sole; no push from the upper body; standing too far away.":"刈的时候对方脚上没有重量（刈不动）；用脚尖踢而不是脚底勾；上身没有往后推；身体离太远。","Drill push, hook and reap slowly 10 times each side, then 10 reps linking the minor inner reap into the major outer reap.":"慢速练「推 + 勾 + 刈」各 10 次，再练「小内刈 → 大外刈」连接 10 次。","When they step back to avoid it, they walk straight into the major outer reap or a forward throw.":"对方往后退以防小内刈时，正好让你接大外刈或其他前方摔法。","Major Hip Throw":"大腰","Hip technique":"腰技","Your hip below their belt":"臀部在对方腰带下方","Turning and leg drive":"转身与腿力","PULL FORWARD · TURN IN · HIPS LOW · STRAIGHTEN TO LIFT":"拉往前 · 转身踏进 · 低腰 · 伸腿抬起","Pull the sleeve to bring them forward onto their toes. Turn in so your back is against their chest, bend your knees so your hips are below their belt, and wrap your arm round their waist. Then straighten your legs to lift them on your hip and keep pulling and turning — they roll over your hip and land on their back in front of your feet.":"拉袖让对方往前、重心落在脚尖。转身踏进，背靠对方胸口，双膝弯下，让你的臀部低于对方腰带，同时手臂抱住对方的腰。然后伸直双腿，用臀部把对方抬起，一边拉袖一边转身，对方从你的臀部翻过去，背部着地在你脚前。","Not bending the knees (your hips stay higher than theirs and you cannot lift); pulling with the arms and lifting with the back (hurts your back); not turning far enough, so the hips do not connect; turning in before breaking the balance.":"膝盖没弯（臀部比对方高，抬不起）；只用手拉、用背抬（伤腰）；转身不够，臀部没贴住；没先破势就转身。","Entries (uchikomi): turn in, drop the hips and lift slightly, then stop — 3 × 10 each side; then full throws on mats with your partner breakfalling.":"打入（uchikomi）：转身踏进、低腰、抬起一点就停，左右各 3 × 10 次；之后在垫上完整摔，搭档做受身。","When they push forward or bend over, the hip throw uses that momentum; it is also the base for the other hip throws and shoulder throws.":"对方向前推或向前弯腰时，大腰可以顺势把对方摔过去；它也是学习其他腰技和背负投的基础。","Scarf Hold-Down":"袈裟固","Hold-down":"固技","Your side on their chest":"胸侧压胸口","Ground":"地面","SIT TIGHT · ARM ROUND THE NECK · TRAP THE ARM · LEGS WIDE":"贴身坐 · 抱颈 · 夹臂 · 双腿张开","With them on their back, sit tight against their side, facing their head. Wrap one arm round the back of their neck and trap their near arm under your other armpit. Press your side onto their chest with the legs spread wide, one forward and one back, like a tripod. Under current IJF rules a 10-second hold-down is waza-ari and 20 seconds is ippon.":"对方仰躺时，你紧贴对方身侧坐下，面向对方的头。一手从对方脖子后面绕过，另一手把对方靠近你的手臂夹在腋下。身体侧面压在对方胸口，双腿前后张开，像三脚架一样稳。目前国际柔联规则：压制 10 秒是技有，20 秒是一本。","Sitting too far from them (no pressure); legs together (easy to roll); holding the head without trapping the arm (they pull it out and push you off); letting go in a panic when they bridge.":"坐得离对方太远（压不住）；双腿并拢（一翻就倒）；只抱头不夹手臂（对方手臂抽出来推你）；被翻时慌张放手。","Take turns: one holds for 30 seconds while the other tries to escape by bridging and turning.":"和伙伴轮流：一人压制 30 秒，另一人用挺腰和转身尝试逃脱。","When a throw lands but is not ippon, go straight into the scarf hold and win on the ground.":"摔倒对方但没拿到一本时，马上接袈裟固，可以在地面赢得比赛。","Cross Armlock":"腕挫十字固","Armlock":"关节技","HIPS TO SHOULDER · HUG THE ARM · KNEES IN · LIE BACK":"贴肩坐 · 抱臂 · 夹膝 · 慢慢后躺","Sit with your hips tight against their shoulder and your legs across their chest and head. Hug one of their arms to your chest with their thumb pointing up and squeeze your knees together. Then lie back slowly and lift your hips a little — the pressure goes onto their elbow. The moment they tap or say \"maitta\" (I give up), let go.":"臀部紧贴对方肩膀坐下，双腿压在对方胸口与头上。双手把对方一只手臂抱在胸前，对方拇指朝上，双膝夹紧。然后慢慢往后躺、臀部微微抬起，压力就会落在对方的手肘。对方一拍地或说「参った」（认输），马上放开。","Jerking it on fast (causes injuries); hips too far from the shoulder (they pull the arm out); knees apart; not letting go after the tap.":"猛然用力（会造成受伤）；臀部离肩膀太远（对方抽手）；双膝打开；对方拍地后还不放。","Under a coach, partners practise the position with very light pressure, 5 times each, and both practise tapping. Armlocks are usually taught only to older students.":"在教练指导下，伙伴之间只做「位置 + 极轻施压」各 5 次，双方都要练习拍地。关节技通常只教给较年长的学员。","A submission is ippon and wins the match outright.":"让对方认输是一本，直接获胜。","Start and end with a bow":"以礼开始、以礼结束","Grip first, then break the balance":"先抓好，再破坏平衡","Judo's first lesson":"柔道第一课","Protects the head and back":"保护头部与背部","Timing, not strength":"靠时机，不靠力气","The moment they step":"对方踏步的一瞬间","One of the first throws taught":"初学者最常学的摔法之一","Reap the leg, drive with the chest":"刈腿、胸口往前压","Small move, big effect":"小动作、大效果","A favourite set-up for other throws":"常用来连接其他摔法","The classic hip throw":"经典腰技","Turn in, drop the hips, lift":"转身、低腰、抬起","The first hold-down taught":"柔道第一个学的压制","20 seconds = ippon":"20 秒＝一本","Judo allows locks on the elbow only":"柔道只允许锁手肘","Bow to each other (rei) as a sign of respect":"互相鞠躬（礼），表示尊重","Natural posture (shizentai): feet shoulder-width apart, knees soft, back straight":"自然体（shizentai）：双脚与肩同宽、膝微弯、背挺直","Slide in with small steps, feet close to the mat":"滑步靠近，脚不离地","Grip (kumikata): lead hand on the lapel, rear hand on the sleeve below the elbow":"组手（kumikata）：前手抓衣领，后手抓袖子（肘部下方）","Off-balance them (kuzushi): pull the sleeve and lift the lapel so their weight goes onto their toes":"破势（kuzushi）：拉袖、提领，让对方重心移到脚尖","Back to natural posture, ready to attack":"回到自然体，准备进攻","Stand with the arms forward and the chin slightly tucked":"站立，双手向前，下巴微收","Squat low, chin to chest, eyes on your belt knot":"深蹲，下巴贴胸，眼睛看腰带结","Sit the hips down just behind your heels and roll back with a round back":"臀部坐在脚跟后方，圆背往后滚","Slap the mat with both arms at about 45° from your body; the head never touches the mat":"双手在身体两侧约 45° 拍垫，头不碰地","Sit up, ready to stand":"坐起来，准备站起","Both gripping: lapel and sleeve":"双方互抓：衣领与袖子","As they step forward, pull them on to that foot":"对方往前踏步时，把对方拉到那只脚上","Sweep their ankle with the sole of your foot just before their weight lands":"在对方重心落下前，用脚掌扫对方脚踝","Keep pulling and turning with the hands as their feet leave the mat":"双手继续拉转，对方双脚离地","They land on the back with force and speed — ippon":"有力、快速、背部着地 —— 一本","Both gripping":"双方互抓","Pull the sleeve and push the lapel to put their weight on the heels; plant your support foot beside theirs":"拉袖、推领让对方重心落到脚跟，支撑脚踏到对方脚旁","Swing your reaping leg forward past their leg":"刈脚往前摆过对方的腿","Reap: the back of your thigh hits the back of theirs while your chest drives forward":"大腿后侧刈对方大腿后侧，胸口同时往前压","With the supporting leg gone, they fall backwards":"对方失去支撑脚，往后倒","They land on their back; you stay up and keep hold of the sleeve to protect them":"对方背部着地；你站稳，拉住袖子保护对方","Close in and push them back so their weight sits on the lead foot":"靠近，往后推让对方的前脚承重","Hook behind their lead heel from the inside with the sole of your foot":"用脚底从内侧勾住对方前脚的脚跟","Reap the foot towards their toes while both hands drive them back":"把脚往对方脚尖方向刈，双手同时往后推","Off balance, they fall backwards":"对方失去平衡，往后倒","The minor inner reap often sets up the major outer reap and other throws":"小内刈常常用来接大外刈或其他摔法","Pull the sleeve to bring them forward onto their toes":"拉袖让对方往前，重心落在脚尖","Turn in with your back to them, knees bent so your hips are below their belt, and wrap your arm round their waist":"转身踏进，背贴对方，膝弯下让臀部低于对方腰带，手臂抱住对方的腰","Straighten the legs to lift them on your hip while you pull the sleeve":"伸直双腿，用臀部把对方抬起，同时拉袖","They roll over your hip":"对方从你的臀部上翻过去","They land on their back in front of your feet; you keep hold of the sleeve":"对方背部着地在你脚前，你拉住袖子","They are on their back; sit tight against their side, facing their head":"对方仰躺；你紧贴对方身侧坐下，面向对方的头","Wrap one arm round their neck and trap their near arm under your other armpit":"一手绕过对方脖子，另一手把对方的手臂夹在腋下","Hold it: 10 seconds is waza-ari, 20 seconds is ippon":"压住：10 秒是技有，20 秒是一本","If they bridge, spread your legs wider and keep your weight on their chest":"对方挺腰想翻时，双腿再张开，把重量留在对方胸口","Sit with your hips tight to their shoulder and your legs across their chest and head":"臀部紧贴对方肩膀坐下，双腿压在对方胸口与头上","Hug their arm to your chest, thumb pointing up, and squeeze your knees together":"双手把对方的手臂抱在胸前，拇指朝上，双膝夹紧","Lie back slowly and lift your hips a little — the pressure goes on their elbow":"慢慢往后躺、臀部微微抬起，压力在对方的手肘","Posture":"姿势","Etiquette":"礼仪","Drive":"推进","Kuzushi":"Kuzushi","Turning":"转身","Flexibility":"柔软度","Technique {n} of 10 · {type}":"第 {n} 个技术 · {type}","What is Lethwei?":"什么是缅甸拳？","Lethwei is Myanmar's traditional combat sport, known as the \"art of nine limbs\". Fighters wear no gloves — only gauze and tape on the hands — and may strike with fists, elbows, knees, feet and the head, while throws and sweeps are also allowed, which makes it one of the most intense stand-up fighting sports in the world.":"缅甸拳（Lethwei）是缅甸的传统格斗运动，被称为“九肢艺术”。选手不戴拳套，只用纱布和胶带缠手，可以用拳、肘、膝、脚和头攻击，摔和扫也被允许，因此被视为世界上最激烈的站立格斗之一。","How is it different from Muay Thai?":"缅甸拳和泰拳有什么不同？","Lethwei":"缅甸拳","Muay Thai":"泰拳","Gloves":"拳套","None — gauze and tape":"无，纱布与胶带缠手","Yes":"有","Headbutts":"头撞","Allowed":"允许","Not allowed":"不允许","Weapons":"攻击部位","Throws & sweeps":"摔与扫","Part of the game":"是比赛的一部分","Limited":"有限制","Rules vary between events — always check the rules of the event you are watching or entering.":"规则会因赛事而不同，参加比赛前请确认该赛事的规则。","The ten techniques at a glance":"十个技术一览","Build the basics first — stance, straight punches, kicks and checks from boxing and Muay Thai.":"先打好拳击与泰拳的基本功：站架、直拳、踢腿与挡踢。","Learn to wrap your hands properly, and still wear gloves for most pad and bag work.":"裸拳训练前学会正确缠手，打手靶或沙袋时仍要戴拳套。","Practise headbutts and elbows only on pads or protective gear, under a coach.":"头撞与肘击只在教练监督下、在护具或手靶上练。","Stop and see a doctor after any blow to the head that causes dizziness, headache or nausea.":"头部受击后若有头晕、头痛、恶心，立即停止并就医。","Related: <a href=\"../muay-thai/\">Muay Thai basics</a> and <a href=\"../boxing/\">boxing basics</a>.":"相关课程：<a href=\"../muay-thai/\">泰拳入门</a>、<a href=\"../boxing/\">拳击入门</a>。","Why \"the art of nine limbs\"?":"为什么叫“九肢艺术”？","It adds the headbutt to Muay Thai's eight limbs of fists, elbows, knees and shins.":"在泰拳的八肢（拳、肘、膝、胫）之外，再加上头撞。","Do Lethwei fighters wear gloves?":"缅甸拳选手戴拳套吗？","No — the hands are wrapped only in gauze and tape.":"不戴。比赛时双手只用纱布和胶带缠好。","Can beginners learn headbutts?":"初学者可以学头撞吗？","Only from a qualified coach, following their progression and with protective equipment — never on your own or with friends.":"只能在合格教练指导下、按照课程进度学习，并使用护具；绝对不要自己或和朋友尝试。","FIGHTING SPORTS · MYANMAR'S ART OF NINE LIMBS":"格斗运动 · 缅甸的「九肢艺术」","Lethwei Basics: Bare Knuckles and the Art of Nine Limbs":"缅甸拳入门：裸拳与头撞的九肢格斗","Lethwei is fought without gloves — just gauze and tape on the hands — and adds the head to Muay Thai's weapons: fists, elbows, knees, feet and the headbutt make nine, and throws and sweeps are allowed. The grey figure is the opponent; the red ring marks the point of contact.":"缅甸拳（Lethwei）不戴拳套，只用纱布和胶带缠手，攻击部位比泰拳多了头部——拳、肘、膝、脚加上头撞，共九种武器，摔与扫也被允许。灰色人形是对手，红圈标示接触点。","Fists (bare)":"拳（裸拳）","Elbows":"肘","Knees":"膝","Feet & shins":"脚与胫","Head":"头","Safety: ":"安全提醒：","Lethwei is one of the most dangerous combat sports. Headbutts, bare-knuckle punches and elbows must only be trained under a qualified coach, on pads and with protective equipment — never try a headbutt on a partner or anyone else. These animations are for understanding only.":"缅甸拳是最危险的格斗运动之一。头撞、裸拳与肘击只能在合格教练指导下、在手靶或护具上练习，绝对不要对同伴或任何人尝试头撞。本页动画仅供理解。","Fists · elbows · knees · feet · head":"双拳 · 双肘 · 双膝 · 双脚 · 头","Contact point, this technique":"本技术的接触点","Hands wrapped in gauze and tape only":"仅用纱布和胶带缠手","Pick a technique":"选择技术查看细节","For education only; the animations are simplified. Lethwei is a high-risk contact sport — train only under a qualified coach with proper protective equipment.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，动画为简化示意。缅甸拳是高风险接触性运动，请只在合格教练指导下、使用适当护具训练。","Lethwei Basics: Burmese Bare-Knuckle Boxing, the Art of Nine Limbs | KungfuTutor":"Lethwei基础：缅甸裸拳拳击，九肢之术 | KungfuTutor","An animated introduction to Lethwei, Myanmar's bare-knuckle art of nine limbs: stance, bare-knuckle punches, the headbutt, rising elbow, flying knee, kicks, catch-and-sweep and the high cover — with safety notes.":"以动画介绍Lethwei，即缅甸的裸拳九肢之术：站姿、裸拳拳法、头击、上挑肘、飞膝、踢法、抓握与扫腿，以及高位防守，并附安全提示。","Lethwei Basics — The Art of Nine Limbs, Step by Step":"Lethwei基础——九肢之术，循序渐进","Why is Lethwei called the art of nine limbs?":"为什么Lethwei被称为九肢之术？","Because it adds the head to the eight weapons of Muay Thai: two fists, two elbows, two knees, two shins or feet, and headbutts.":"因为它在泰拳的八种武器之外加上了头部：两拳、两肘、两膝、两胫或两脚，以及头击。","No. Lethwei is fought bare-knuckle, with the hands wrapped in gauze and tape.":"不需要。Lethwei以裸拳进行，双手缠绕纱布和胶带。","What is the difference between Lethwei and Muay Thai?":"Lethwei和泰拳有什么区别？","Lethwei is bare-knuckle and allows headbutts, and throws and sweeps are part of the game; Muay Thai is fought in gloves and does not allow headbutts.":"Lethwei采用裸拳，允许头击，投摔和扫腿也是比赛的一部分；泰拳则戴拳套比赛，不允许头击。","HANDS HIGH · ELBOWS TIGHT · CHIN DOWN":"手高 · 肘紧 · 下巴收","Stand with feet staggered about shoulder-width, weight slightly back, knees soft. With bare fists there is no padding to hide behind, so hold the hands higher and closer to the head and use the forearms as shields; keep the elbows in and the chin tucked. Watch their chest — and their head, because headbutts are legal in Lethwei.":"双脚前后站立、约与肩同宽，重心略偏后，膝盖微屈。因为是裸拳，双手要举得比戴拳套时更高、更贴近头部，前臂可以当作盾牌；手肘收紧护住身体，下巴收。眼睛看对方胸口，同时留意头部——缅甸拳允许头撞。","Hiding behind the hands as if wearing gloves (bare fists don't cover enough); chin up; poking the head forward (an easy headbutt target); weight on the front foot.":"用戴拳套的习惯「躲在手后」（裸拳挡不住）；下巴抬起；头往前伸（容易被头撞）；重心在前脚。","Hold and move in your stance in a mirror, 3 × 1 minute, checking hands, elbows and chin.":"对镜保持站架并轻轻移动 3 × 1 分钟，检查手、肘、下巴的位置。","Lethwei has the most weapons of any striking art, so the stance must defend fists, elbows, knees, feet and the head.":"缅甸拳攻击方式最多，站架必须同时防拳、肘、膝、脚和头。","Bare-knuckle Straight Punch":"裸拳直拳","Punch":"拳","First two knuckles":"食指与中指指节","Fist structure":"拳头结构","PIVOT & TURN · FIRST TWO KNUCKLES · STRAIGHT WRIST":"转脚转髋 · 前两个指节 · 手腕直","Throw it like a boxing cross — pivot and turn the hips — but with no glove you must land on the first two knuckles with the wrist and forearm in one straight line and the fist tightly closed. Snap it straight back to guard.":"和拳击直拳一样转脚、转髋出拳，但因为没有拳套，要特别注意用食指与中指的指节击中，手腕和前臂保持一直线，拳头握紧。打完立刻收回护头。","Landing on the little-finger knuckles (a common fracture); a bent wrist; a loose fist; punching hard skull bone.":"用小指那侧的指节打（容易骨折）；手腕弯曲；拳头没握紧；打硬的头骨。","With wraps and gauze, slow reps on pads, 3 × 10, feeling the first two knuckles connect.":"缠好手带与纱布后，对手靶慢速练习 3 × 10，感受前两个指节接触。","Bare-knuckle punches cut and concentrate force — but hands break easily, so where you hit matters.":"裸拳的伤害集中，但手也容易受伤，所以选择打击的位置很重要。","ELBOW LEVEL · TURN · STRAIGHT WRIST":"手肘抬平 · 转身 · 手腕直","Shift a little weight to the lead foot, pivot and turn the hips with the arm bent about 90° and the elbow level with the fist, hooking across into the side of the jaw. With bare fists keep the wrist straight to avoid spraining it. (In the side view the fist travels into the screen.)":"重心稍移到前脚，转脚转胯，手臂弯成约 90°、手肘与拳同高，拳头横向勾入下巴侧面。裸拳时手腕要保持直，避免扭伤。（侧面动画中拳头往画面内移动。）","A wide, telegraphed swing; dropping the elbow; bending the wrist; the other hand leaving the face.":"幅度大、预告明显的甩拳；手肘下垂；手腕弯曲；另一只手离开脸部。","Hooks on pads, 3 × 10, then chain them after the straight punch.":"对手靶练勾拳 3 × 10，再接在直拳之后。","Hooks come from outside the line of sight and are a common knockout punch up close.":"勾拳从视线之外打来，是近身战中常见的击倒拳。","Headbutt":"头撞","Forehead near the hairline":"前额（发际线附近）","Close-range control":"近距离控制","GRIP THE NECK · DRIVE FROM THE LEGS · USE THE FOREHEAD":"扣住后颈 · 腿部发力 · 用前额","The headbutt is what sets Lethwei apart from other stand-up fighting. At very close range a fighter often grips the back of the opponent's neck to control the distance, then drives from the legs to strike with the hard part of the forehead near the hairline — not the face or the top of the head. This animation is only here so you understand the rule and the movement: headbutts are extremely dangerous and must only be learned under a qualified coach with suitable equipment. Never try one on a training partner or anyone else.":"头撞是缅甸拳与其他站立格斗最大的不同。在极近距离时，选手常先扣住对方后颈控制距离，再由腿部蹬地带动身体，用前额发际线附近较坚硬的部位往前撞向对方脸部，而不是用脸或头顶。动画只是让你理解这条规则与动作——头撞非常危险，只能在专业教练指导、使用合适护具的环境下学习，绝对不要对同伴或在任何其他情况下尝试。","Hitting with the face or the top of the head (you get hurt); charging in head-down and blind; lunging from out of range.":"用脸或头顶去撞（自己会受伤）；低头盲目冲撞；从超出距离的地方突进。","This page gives no headbutt drill — learn it only from a qualified Lethwei coach.":"本页不提供头撞练习方法；请只在合格的缅甸拳教练指导下学习。","Headbutts make close range far more dangerous — and are why Lethwei fighters guard their head so carefully.":"头撞让近距离缠斗更危险，也是缅甸拳选手必须特别注意防守头部的原因。","Rising Elbow":"上挑肘","Elbow":"肘","Point of the elbow":"手肘前端","Close-range explosiveness":"近距离爆发力","DIP · DRIVE UP · ELBOW SPEARS UP":"膝盖微蹲 · 蹬地 · 手肘往上顶","At close range, dip the knees and drop the rear elbow, then drive up through the legs so the elbow spears upward into the chin, with your hand finishing near your own ear. The other hand guards your head; return to stance.":"在近距离时，膝盖微蹲、后手手肘放低，接着双腿蹬地，让手肘由下往上顶向对方下巴，手掌靠近自己耳朵。另一手护头，打完回到站架。","Throwing from too far; lifting the arm without the legs; flaring the elbow out; leaving an opening afterwards.":"距离太远就出手；只抬手臂不用腿；手肘往外甩；打完留下空档。","Slow reps on pads, 3 × 8, then add it after a hook.":"对手靶慢速练习，3 × 8，之后接在勾拳后面。","When an opponent ducks and charges in, the rising elbow meets them on the way.":"当对手低头冲进来时，上挑肘正好迎上去。","Flying Knee":"飞膝","Knee":"膝","Point of the knee":"膝盖前端","Chest, chin":"胸口、下巴","STEP & JUMP · REAR KNEE UP & FORWARD · LAND GUARDED":"踏步起跳 · 后膝向前上方 · 落地护头","Step in with the lead foot to take off and jump forward and up, driving the rear knee up and forward into the chest or chin, with the hands reaching out for balance or control. Land balanced and get straight back into your guard.":"用前脚踏步作为起跳脚，向前上方跳起，同时后腿膝盖向前上方顶向对方胸口或下巴，双手往前保持平衡或控制对方。击中后落地站稳，立刻回到护头。","Jumping from too far; pausing before take-off (telegraphing); landing off balance; getting countered after a miss.":"距离太远就跳；起跳前停顿（预告动作）；落地时失去平衡；落空后被反击。","Practise jumping knee lifts on the spot, 10 reps, then 3 × 5 on the bag, focusing on a balanced landing.":"先原地练习「提膝跳」10 次，再对沙袋练习 3 × 5，着重落地平衡。","The flying knee is a classic finisher in Lethwei and Muay Thai — but costly if it misses.":"飞膝是缅甸拳和泰拳中经典的收尾技，但若落空代价很大。","Roundhouse Kick":"中段踢","Kick":"脚","Shin":"小腿胫骨","Side of the body":"身体侧面","Explosive hip turn":"转髋爆发","PIVOT · TURN THE HIP · SHIN · ARM SWINGS BACK":"转前脚 · 转髋 · 胫骨 · 手往后摆","Turn the lead foot out, swing the rear leg up and turn the hip over, landing the shin on the side of the body. The arm on the kicking side swings down and back while the other hand guards the head. Recover to stance.":"前脚脚尖往外转，后腿往前上甩起并把髋部转过去，用胫骨踢中身体侧面，同侧手往下往后摆帮助转身，另一手护头。踢完收回站架。","Not pivoting; kicking with the foot; dropping both hands.":"前脚不转；用脚背踢；两手都掉下。","10 slow pivots holding a wall, then 3 × 10 per leg on the bag.":"扶墙练转脚转髋 10 次，再到沙袋每脚 3 × 10。","Body kicks add up and draw the hands down, opening the head.":"中段踢累积伤害，也能让对方放低手而露出头部。","Push Kick":"前推踢","Sole of the foot":"脚掌","Stomach, hips":"腹部、髋部","KNEE UP · PUSH THE HIPS · SOLE":"先提膝 · 推髋 · 脚掌","Lift the lead knee, push the hips forward and drive the sole of the foot into them, leaning back slightly with the hands up; re-chamber before putting the foot down.":"前腿提膝，髋部往前推，用脚掌把对方推开，上身稍往后、双手护头，推完收回提膝再落地。","Swinging without the knee lift; no hip push; dropping the hands.":"没提膝直接甩；只用腿不推髋；手掉下来。","3 × 10 per leg on the bag.":"对沙袋每脚 3 × 10。","When they try to close in for headbutts or the clinch, the push kick restores the distance.":"当对方想近身头撞或抱颈时，前推踢把距离推回来。","Catch Kick & Sweep":"接腿扫倒","Lead arm traps the leg":"前手夹腿","Their standing leg":"对方的支撑脚","Timing and control":"时机与控制","STEP IN · TRAP THE LEG · SWEEP THE STANDING LEG":"迎上去 · 夹住腿 · 扫支撑脚","As the body kick comes, step into it to take the sting out and scoop the leg up under your lead arm. Then sweep their standing leg with your rear leg so they lose balance, and reset to your stance.":"对方中段踢过来时，身体往前迎上去减少冲击，前手从下方把对方的腿夹在腋下。接着用后腿扫对方的支撑脚，让对方失去平衡倒地，自己回到站架。","Catching while backing away (you take the full kick); grabbing with the hand instead of trapping; losing your own balance on the sweep.":"往后退接腿（会被踢个正着）；只用手抓不夹紧；扫腿时自己失去平衡。","Partner throws slow, light kicks while you step in and trap, 10 reps; then add the sweep, on mats only.":"伙伴慢速轻踢，你练习迎上去夹腿 10 次；熟练后再在软垫上加上扫脚。","Catching and sweeping makes a kicker think twice.":"接腿扫倒让喜欢踢腿的对手不敢乱踢。","High Cover & Counter":"护头挡击","Forearm and elbow":"前臂与手肘","Block the hook":"挡住勾拳","Reaction and structure":"反应与结构","ARM TIGHT TO THE HEAD · CHIN DOWN · COUNTER":"手臂贴头 · 下巴收 · 挡完反击","As a hook comes in, raise the arm on that side tight against the side of your head so the forearm and elbow take the blow, chin down and leaning in slightly. Fire back immediately with a straight punch from the other hand.":"对方勾拳打来时，同侧手臂抬起紧贴头侧，用前臂和手肘挡住，下巴收、身体微向前，让冲击落在手臂上。挡完立刻用另一手直拳反击。","Holding the arm away from the head (the punch drives through); closing your eyes and turning away; blocking without countering.":"手臂离头太远（被打穿）；闭眼转头；只挡不反击。","Partner swings slowly from both sides with pads; block and counter, 3 × 1 minute.":"伙伴用手靶慢速从两侧挥打，你练挡＋反击 3 × 1 分钟。","Without gloves only the structure of the arm can absorb a heavy shot, so this cover is vital.":"没有拳套时，只有手臂结构能挡住重拳，所以这个防守特别重要。","Defending without gloves":"没有拳套的防守","Hands higher and tighter":"手更高、更紧","No gloves — structure matters more":"没有拳套，结构更重要","A straight wrist":"手腕一直线","Driven by the body turn":"转身带动","Lethwei's signature ninth weapon":"缅甸拳的招牌：第九种武器","For understanding only — never practise on a person":"仅供理解，切勿对人练习","Upward at close range":"近距离由下往上","Punishes a ducking opponent":"对付低头冲进的人","High risk, high reward":"高风险、高威力","When the opponent dips":"对方低头时使用","The same hip-turning kick as Muay Thai":"和泰拳相同的转髋踢","Lands with the shin":"胫骨踢击","Controls distance":"控制距离","Stops a rush":"打断对方冲进","Turns their kick into your chance":"把对方的踢变成机会","Lethwei allows throws and sweeps":"缅甸拳允许摔与扫","Key bare-knuckle defence":"裸拳的防守重点","Block, then counter at once":"挡完立刻反击","Feet staggered, weight a little back, knees soft":"双脚前后站，重心偏后，膝盖微弯","Hands high and tight with the chin tucked — there are no gloves to hide behind":"双手高举护头，下巴收紧——没有拳套可以躲","Elbows in to cover the body; eyes on their chest":"手肘收紧护住身体，眼睛看对方胸口","Pivot and turn the hips; land on the first two knuckles":"转脚转髋，用食指与中指的指节击中","Keep the wrist straight and snap it back":"手腕保持一直线，立刻收回","Stance at close range":"近距离站架","Turn the body and hook the fist across into the side of the jaw":"转身带动，拳头横向勾入下巴侧面","The opponent is very close":"对方在很近的距离","Grip behind their neck and sway back slightly":"双手扣住对方后颈，身体略往后","Drive from the legs and strike with the forehead near the hairline":"腿部蹬地，用前额（发际线附近）往前撞","Release and return to the guard":"放开、回到护头","Close-range stance":"近距离站架","Dip the knees and drop the rear elbow":"膝盖微蹲、后手手肘放低","Drive up and spear the elbow upward under the chin":"蹬地，手肘由下往上顶向下巴","Stance; the opponent dips or comes forward":"站架，对方低头或往前","Step in with the lead foot to take off":"前脚踏出，准备起跳","Jump and drive the rear knee up and forward, hands reaching out":"起跳，后膝往前上方顶，双手往前","Land balanced and get the hands up":"落地站稳，立刻护头","Pivot the lead foot and swing the rear leg up":"转前脚，后腿往前上甩","Turn the hip over and land the shin on the body":"转髋，用胫骨踢中身体","Recover the leg":"收腿","Back to stance":"回到站架","Stance; the opponent steps in":"站架，对方逼近","Lift the lead knee":"前脚提膝","Push the hips and drive the sole into them":"推髋，用脚掌把对方推开","Re-chamber":"收腿","They throw a body kick":"对方起腿中段踢","Step into the kick and scoop the leg under your lead arm":"身体迎上去，前手从下方把腿夹住","Sweep their standing leg with your rear leg":"后腿扫对方的支撑脚","They lose their balance; you reset to stance":"对方失去平衡，你回到站架","Arm tight to the side of the head, forearm takes it, chin down, lean in a little":"手臂贴头侧，前臂挡住，下巴收、身体微前倾","Counter straight away with the rear hand":"挡完立刻用后手反击","Awareness":"观察","Wrist stability":"手腕稳定","Close control":"近距离控制","Head defence":"头部防守","Hip drive":"髋部推送","One-leg balance":"单脚平衡","Commitment":"勇气","What is MMA?":"什么是 MMA？","Mixed martial arts (MMA) is a combat sport that allows striking, clinching, takedowns and ground fighting; fighters usually blend boxing, Muay Thai, wrestling and Brazilian jiu-jitsu. Bouts take place in a cage or ring and are won by knockout, submission (the opponent taps out) or the judges' decision.":"综合格斗（MMA）是允许站立打击、缠抱、摔与地面技术的格斗运动，选手通常结合拳击、泰拳、摔跤和巴西柔术。比赛在八角笼或擂台中进行，可以用击倒、降服（让对方拍地认输）或裁判判定获胜。","The eight techniques at a glance":"八个技巧一览","How do striking and wrestling connect?":"打击和摔怎么连在一起？","MMA's key idea is that strikes set up takedowns and the threat of takedowns sets up strikes: when they raise their hands to block punches, the double-leg gets easier; when they drop low to stop takedowns, the overhand and knees land more easily. That is why the stance must handle both threats at once.":"MMA 最大的特点是“打击掩护摔、摔逼出打击”：对方抬手护头时，双腿抱摔更容易成功；对方怕被摔而压低重心时，过顶拳和膝击更容易打中。所以站架要能同时应对两种威胁。","Learn a boxing stance, basic wrestling and how to fall safely (breakfalls) first.":"先分别学好拳击站架、基本摔与受身（安全倒地）。","Practise takedowns and ground work only on mats, with a coach.":"摔与地面技术只在软垫上、在教练指导下练习。","Spar with MMA or boxing gloves and a mouthguard, starting with light technical sparring.":"对打时戴 MMA 手套或拳套、护齿，初期以技术对打为主。","Tap early when caught in a choke or joint lock — never fight through it.":"被勒或关节被锁时，早点拍地认输，不要硬撑。","Related: <a href=\"../boxing/\">boxing basics</a> and <a href=\"../muay-thai/\">Muay Thai basics</a>.":"相关课程：<a href=\"../boxing/\">拳击入门</a>、<a href=\"../muay-thai/\">泰拳入门</a>。","What should an MMA beginner learn first?":"MMA 初学者应该先学什么？","The stance, basic punches, the sprawl and getting up safely — they keep you safe in sparring.":"站架、基本拳、防摔下压和安全起身。这些能让你在对打中保护自己。","What is a sprawl?":"什么是下压（Sprawl）？","A takedown defence: throw your legs back and drop your hips onto their back as they shoot.":"对方抱腿时把双脚往后甩、髋部压在对方背上的防摔动作。","Can I learn MMA without a wrestling background?":"没有摔跤背景可以学 MMA 吗？","Yes — most MMA classes teach the stance, breakfalls and basic takedowns from scratch.":"可以。大部分 MMA 课程会从最基本的站架、受身和摔开始教。","MMA":"综合格斗","FIGHTING SPORTS · MIXED MARTIAL ARTS FOR BEGINNERS":"格斗技 · 综合格斗入门","MMA Basics: Striking, Takedowns and the Ground in 8 Lessons":"综合格斗（MMA）入门：打击、摔与地面 8 课","MMA joins boxing, Muay Thai, wrestling and jiu-jitsu. These 8 lessons start with the stance, then basic strikes, a takedown and how to stop one, control on the ground and getting back up safely. The grey figure is the opponent; the red ring marks the point of contact.":"MMA 把拳击、泰拳、摔跤和柔术结合在一起。这 8 课从站架开始，学基本打击、抱摔与防摔，再到地面控制与安全起身。灰色人形是对手，红圈标示接触点。","Striking":"站立打击","Punches and kicks":"拳与腿","Takedowns and the sprawl":"抱摔与下压","Control and getting up":"控制与起身","Phases of a fight":"比赛阶段","Standing · clinch and takedowns · ground":"站立 · 缠抱与摔 · 地面","Pro bout":"职业赛制","3 rounds × 5 minutes (title fights 5 rounds)":"3 回合 × 5 分钟（冠军赛 5 回合）","For education only; the animations are simplified. MMA is a high-impact contact sport: train under a qualified coach on mats, with gloves and a mouthguard for sparring. Practise takedowns and ground work only on mats with a coach.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，动画为简化示意。MMA 是高冲击的接触性运动：请在合格教练指导下、在软垫上训练，对打时戴拳套、护齿等护具。摔与地面技术只在有教练的软垫上练习。","MMA Basics: Stance, Striking, Takedowns, Sprawl & Ground Game — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"MMA基础：站姿、打击、摔倒、防摔与地面技术 — 互动指南 | KungfuTutor","Learn 8 mixed martial arts fundamentals with animated demos against an opponent: MMA stance, jab-cross, overhand, low kick, double-leg takedown, sprawl, ground and pound from mount and the technical stand-up.":"通过与对手对练的动画示范，学习8项综合格斗基础：MMA站姿、刺拳接直拳、过顶拳、低踢、双腿抱摔、sprawl防摔、骑乘位地面重拳打击，以及技术起身。","MMA Basics — Striking and Grappling, Step by Step":"MMA基础——打击与摔跤，循序渐进","What are the basics of MMA?":"MMA的基本是什么？","A stance that defends both strikes and takedowns, basic punches and kicks, a takedown such as the double-leg, takedown defence such as the sprawl, and control on the ground, plus getting back to your feet safely.":"一种同时防御打击和摔法的站姿，基本拳法与腿法，双腿摔等摔法，sprawl防摔等摔法防御，以及地面控制，还有如何安全地重新站起来。","What is a sprawl in MMA?":"MMA中的sprawl是什么？","A takedown defence: as the opponent shoots for your legs, you throw your legs back and drop your hips onto their upper back so they cannot reach your legs, then get back up.":"一种防摔动作：当对手扑向你的双腿时，你将双腿向后蹬出，臀部下沉压在对手上背，使其无法抓到你的腿，然后再站起来。","What is a technical stand-up?":"什么是技术起身？","A safe way to get up from the floor: post one hand behind you, plant the opposite foot, lift the hips, swing the straight leg back underneath you and stand up at a distance, eyes on the opponent.":"一种从地面安全起身的方法：一手撑在身后，另一侧脚踩稳，抬起臀部，将伸直的腿向后摆到身下，然后与对手保持距离站起，眼睛始终盯着对手。","MMA Stance":"MMA 站架","Balance and all-round defence":"平衡与全面防守","MORE KNEE BEND · HIPS LOW · HANDS UP":"膝更弯 · 重心低 · 手护脸","The MMA stance sits between boxing and wrestling: feet a little wider than in boxing, knees more bent and hips lower, so you can react when someone shoots for your legs. Hands guard the face but sit slightly lower than in boxing, elbows close, so they can block punches and fight off grips. Keep your weight fairly even and the lead leg light against low kicks.":"MMA 站架介于拳击与摔跤之间：双脚比拳击稍宽，膝盖更弯、重心更低，这样对方抱腿时你能及时下压。双手护脸但比拳击略低、手肘靠近身体，可以挡拳也可以挡对方抓腿。重心大致平均，前脚不要太重，以免被低踢。","Standing tall like a boxer (easy to take down); head too low like a wrestler (open to knees); dropping the hands; too much weight on the lead leg.":"像拳击一样站得太高（容易被抱摔）；像摔跤一样头太低（容易吃膝击）；双手垂下；前脚太重。","Move in all directions in your stance for 3 × 1 minute, dropping your level every time a partner calls it.":"在站架中前后左右移动 3 × 1 分钟，每听到口令就做一次降低重心。","An MMA fighter faces punches, kicks, knees, elbows and takedowns at once — the stance is where every exchange starts.":"MMA 选手要同时面对拳、踢、膝、肘和摔，站架是所有攻防的起点。","Jab–Cross (1-2)":"一二连击","Knuckles":"拳面","Speed and rhythm":"速度与节奏","JAB OPENS · CROSS TURNS THE HIPS · MOVE AFTER":"前手开路 · 后手转髋 · 打完移动","Find range with the jab and, as it returns, pivot the back foot and turn the hips to fire the cross. MMA gloves are much smaller than boxing gloves, so keep the hands working hard to protect your face. Move straight after, or chain into a kick or takedown.":"先用前手直拳量距离，收回的同时转后脚、转髋打出后手直拳。MMA 的小手套比拳击手套小，双手要更积极护脸。打完立刻移动脚步或接摔、接踢。","Standing still afterwards; both hands away from the face; no body turn; falling forward and giving them a takedown.":"打完停在原地；两手同时离开脸；只用手不转身；身体往前倒，给对方抱摔机会。","3 × 3-minute rounds of shadowboxing or bag work, moving in a new direction after every 1-2.":"空击或沙袋 3 回合 × 3 分钟，每个 1-2 后换一个方向移动。","The 1-2 is the base of MMA striking and often hides a takedown.":"1-2 是 MMA 站立打击的基础，也常用来掩护抱摔。","Overhand":"过顶拳","Arcing power and head movement":"弧线力量与闪避","HEAD OFF LINE · LOOP UP AND OVER · OVER THEIR GUARD":"头往前侧闪 · 拳由上画弧 · 越过对方的手","Dip your head forward and off the centre line while the rear hand loops up and over the top of their lead hand onto the side of the head. Pivot and turn the hips so your weight follows, with the other hand guarding your face. It is often thrown just as they jab.":"头稍微向前并移出中线，同时后手由上方画出弧线，越过对方的前手，打在头侧。转脚转髋让体重跟上，另一手保持护脸。过顶拳常在对方出前手拳时同时打出。","A huge, obvious loop; leaving the head on the centre line; losing balance on a miss; dropping the other hand.":"弧线太大、预告明显；头留在中线上；打空后失去平衡；另一手掉下。","Partner throws slow jabs while you slip and counter with the overhand, 3 × 10.":"伙伴慢速出刺拳，你练「闪 + 过顶拳」反击 3 × 10。","With small gloves and the threat of takedowns, guards sit lower in MMA — which is why the overhand lands so often.":"因为小手套和摔的威胁，对手的护脸较低，过顶拳特别容易打中。","Low Kick":"低踢","Hip turn and accuracy":"转髋与准确度","PIVOT · SHIN · HANDS UP AFTER":"转前脚 · 胫骨 · 踢完护头","Turn the lead foot out, swing the rear leg and turn the hip to land the shin on the outside of their thigh or calf. In MMA a high kick can be caught for a takedown, so the low kick is one of the safest, most used kicks. Recover the leg with the hands up.":"前脚脚尖外转，后腿甩起并转髋，用胫骨踢对方大腿外侧或小腿。在 MMA 中踢得太高容易被抓腿摔倒，所以低踢是最安全常用的腿法之一。踢完收腿、双手护头。","Throwing it when they are set (checked or caught); kicking with the foot; dropping the hands afterwards.":"在对方准备好时直接踢（被挡或被抓）；用脚背踢；踢完手掉下。","1-2 plus low kick on the bag, 3 × 3-minute rounds.":"组合「1-2 + 低踢」在沙袋上 3 回合 × 3 分钟。","Steady low kicks hurt the legs, slow the opponent down and make them wary of stepping in.":"持续低踢会让对方腿部受伤、移动变慢，也让对方不敢轻易进攻。","Double-Leg Takedown":"双腿抱摔","Takedown":"摔","Hands behind both thighs":"双手抱大腿后侧","LEVEL CHANGE · PENETRATE · HEAD TIGHT · DRIVE":"降重心 · 前膝穿透 · 头贴身侧 · 往前推","First change levels — bend the knees with a straight back and eyes forward — then step deep between their feet, dropping the lead knee to the mat with your head tight to their side and both hands wrapping behind their thighs. Bring the back foot up and drive forward off your legs until they fall, and land on top. It works best straight after punches, when their hands come up to guard the head.":"先降低重心（弯膝、背挺直、眼睛看前方），接着前脚大步踏到对方双脚之间，前膝跪地，头贴在对方身侧，双手抱住对方大腿后侧。后脚跟上，用腿往前推，让对方失去平衡倒地，你落在上方。常接在拳之后，让对方的手往上护头。","Bending at the waist instead of the knees (easy to sprawl on); shooting from too far; looking at the floor; grabbing the legs and stopping instead of driving.":"弯腰而不是弯膝（容易被压头）；距离太远才冲；低头看地；抱住后停住不推。","On mats, drill the level change and penetration step 10 times each, then slow full reps with a partner — only on mats with a coach.":"在软垫上练“降重心 → 穿透步”各 10 次，再和伙伴慢速完整练习。只在有教练的软垫上进行。","Good wrestlers decide whether the fight stays standing or goes to the ground; the double-leg is the basic takedown.":"摔角好的选手可以决定比赛在站立还是地面进行，双腿抱摔是最基本的摔法。","Sprawl":"防摔下压","Takedown defence":"防摔","Hips and body weight":"髋部与体重","Reaction and hip strength":"反应与髋部力量","LEGS BACK · HIPS DOWN · HANDS ON HEAD AND SHOULDERS":"脚往后甩 · 髋压下 · 手压头肩","The moment they shoot for your legs, throw both legs back and drive your hips down onto their upper back, putting your whole weight on them, with your hands pushing on their head and shoulders so they can't reach your legs. Once they stall, get back up to your stance.":"对方低身冲向你的脚时，双脚马上往后甩，髋部往下压到对方的上背，用全身体重压住对方，双手压住对方的头和肩膀，让对方碰不到你的腿。稳住后再站起来回到站架。","Reacting late; bending forward without throwing the legs back; landing on your knees (they can still reach); staying down instead of getting up.":"反应太慢；只弯腰不把脚往后甩；膝盖跪地（对方仍抓得到）；压住后忘了站起来。","On mats, sprawl and pop back up on command, 3 × 10; then have a partner shoot slowly.":"在软垫上听口令练下压再站起 3 × 10，熟练后由伙伴慢速出抱摔。","The sprawl lets a striker keep the fight standing.":"下压让擅长打击的选手可以把比赛留在站立。","Ground and Pound (Mount)":"骑乘位地面打击","Fists":"拳头","KNEES TIGHT · WEIGHT LOW · SHORT STRIKES":"双膝夹紧 · 重心压低 · 短打","In the mount you sit on an opponent lying on their back, knees tight to their sides and the tops of the feet on the mat. Get your weight low and balanced first, then posture up a little and throw short, fast strikes downward, bringing the hands back each time and staying balanced so they can't roll you. Many amateur events and most training sessions restrict or ban strikes to the head on the ground.":"骑乘位是坐在仰卧对手身上，双膝紧贴他身体两侧，脚背贴地。先压低重心、保持平衡，再坐直一点，用短而快的拳向下打，每次打完收回手并保持平衡，避免对方翻身。许多业余赛事和大多数训练课中，地面打头会被限制或禁止。","Sitting too tall (easy to roll); big swings that lose balance; striking without control; knees spread wide.":"坐得太直、太高（容易被翻）；挥大拳失去平衡；只打不控制；膝盖张开。","On mats with a grappling dummy or a padded partner: hold the mount for 30 seconds while tapping light strikes.":"在软垫上用打击假人或伙伴戴护具，练「维持骑乘位 30 秒 + 轻触打击」。","The mount is one of the best positions in MMA, and many fights end there.":"骑乘位是 MMA 中最有利的地面位置之一，很多比赛在这里结束。","Technical Stand-up":"技术性起身","Ground → standing":"地面 → 站立","Coordination and safety":"协调与安全","POST · LIFT THE HIPS · LEG BACK · STAND AT DISTANCE":"撑手 · 抬臀 · 脚往后收 · 站起保持距离","Sitting on the floor, post one hand on the mat behind you with that leg straight, plant the other foot and guard your face with the free hand. Push off the posted hand and planted foot to lift your hips, swing the straight leg back underneath you and plant it, then rise into your stance at a safe distance. Keep your eyes on the opponent the whole time.":"坐在地上时，一手撑在身后地面，同侧的腿伸直，另一脚踩地，空着的手护脸。撑地的手和踩地的脚一起推，把臀部抬离地面，伸直的腿从身体下方往后收并踩稳，然后站起进入站架，与对方保持安全距离。全程眼睛注视对方。","Turning your back to crawl up; standing up head-first (easy to kick); ending up too close; posting the hand in front instead of behind.":"转身背对对方爬起来；头往前低着站起（容易被踢）；起身后站太近；撑地的手放在身体前方。","10 reps each side; once smooth, try it with a partner calling the side.":"左右两边各练 10 次，熟练后闭眼练习，确保动作自然流畅。","Getting up safely after going down matters in MMA and in self-defence alike.":"被摔倒后安全地站起来，是 MMA 和自我防卫都很重要的技巧。","Defends strikes and takedowns":"同时防打与防摔","Lower and wider than boxing":"比拳击更低、更宽","The basic punching combination":"最基本的拳法组合","Punch, then move":"打完就移动","One of MMA's most common power punches":"MMA 最常见的重拳之一","The head moves off line as you throw":"出拳时头同时移出中线","Slows the opponent's movement":"削弱对方的移动","Thigh or calf":"踢大腿或小腿","Takes the fight to the ground":"把比赛带到地面","Level change → penetrate → drive":"降重心 → 穿透 → 推","The basic takedown defence":"最基本的防摔","Legs back, hips down":"腿往后伸、髋往下沉","A dominant ground position":"地面上的优势位置","Control first, then strike":"先控制，再打击","Getting up safely from the floor":"从地上安全站起来","Useful in self-defence too":"自我防卫也适用","Feet a little wider than boxing, knees more bent, hips lower":"双脚比拳击稍宽、膝盖更弯，重心较低","Hands guard the face but sit a little lower, ready to stop takedowns":"双手护脸但稍低，随时可以挡摔","Ready for punches, kicks and takedowns at once":"同时防拳、防踢、防摔","Cross — pivot the back foot and turn the hips":"后手直拳，转脚转髋","Hands back up, ready to move":"双手回防，准备移动","Dip the head forward and off the centre line":"头向前下沉并移出中线","The rear hand loops up and over":"后手由上方绕弧打出","Come down over their guard onto the side of the head":"从对方手上方落下，打在头侧","Pivot the lead foot and swing the rear leg":"转前脚、后腿往前甩","Land the shin on their thigh or calf":"用胫骨踢中对方大腿或小腿","Recover the leg, hands up":"收回腿，双手护头","Stance, at punching range":"站架，对方在出拳距离","Level change: bend the knees, back straight, eyes forward":"降低重心：屈膝、背挺直、眼睛向前","Penetration step: drop the lead knee between their feet, head tight to their side":"穿透步：前膝落在对方双脚之间，头紧贴对方身侧","Grab behind both thighs and drive forward off your feet":"双手抱住大腿后侧，用双脚蹬地向前推","They go down; you land on top in control":"对方倒地，你在上方控制","Stance; watch their hips":"站架，看对方的髋部","They shoot low for your legs":"对方低身冲向你的腿","Throw the legs back and drop the hips, putting your weight on their back":"双腿往后甩、髋部压下，用体重压在对方背上","Hands push down on their head and shoulders so they can't reach your legs":"双手压住对方的头和肩，让对方够不到你的腿","Get back up to your stance":"站起来回到站架","Mount: knees either side of their body, weight low":"骑乘位：双膝在对方身体两侧，重心压低","Posture up a little and raise the rear hand":"坐直一点，后手举起","Short, fast strikes downward, then bring the hand back":"短而快地向下打，打完收回","Stay balanced so they can't roll you":"保持平衡，不要被翻过去","Sitting: one hand posted behind, that leg straight, the other foot planted, front hand guarding the face":"坐在地上：一手撑地在后，同侧腿伸直，另一脚踩地，前手护脸","Push off the posted hand and planted foot to lift the hips":"用撑地的手和踩地的脚一起推，把臀部抬离地面","Swing the straight leg back under you and plant it behind":"把伸直的腿从身体下方往后收，踩在后方","Stand up into your stance at a safe distance":"站起成站架，与对方保持安全距离","Takedown readiness":"摔法防守准备","Arcing power":"弧线力量","Head movement":"头部移动","Hip strength":"髋部力量","Conditioning":"体能","Hip pressure":"髋部压力","Accurate strikes":"打击精准","What is Muay Thai?":"什么是泰拳？","Muay Thai is Thailand's national sport, known as the \"art of eight limbs\" because it strikes with eight points — two fists, two elbows, two knees and two shins — plus its own stand-up clinch. Before a fight, boxers perform the traditional Wai Kru Ram Muay to honour their teachers and tradition. Today it is one of the world's most popular stand-up combat sports and a key striking base for MMA.":"泰拳是泰国的国技，被称为“八肢艺术”，因为它用双拳、双肘、双膝和双小腿共八个部位攻击，还有独特的近身抱颈。比赛前，选手会表演传统的拜师舞 Wai Kru Ram Muay，向老师和传统致敬。如今，泰拳是全球最受欢迎的站立格斗运动之一，也是综合格斗（MMA）站立技术的重要基础。","How is the stance different from boxing?":"泰拳和拳击站架有什么不同？","Boxers only defend punches, so they stand more side-on with even weight. In Muay Thai you also face kicks, knees and elbows, so the stance is squarer, taller and weighted to the back leg, keeping the lead foot light to check kicks or teep.":"拳击手只需防拳，因此身体较侧、重心平均；泰拳还要防踢、膝和肘，所以身体更正面、站得更高、重心偏后，前脚保持轻盈，随时可以提膝挡踢或前蹬。","Warm up with 5–10 minutes of skipping or jogging, then mobilise hips, ankles and shoulders.":"先跳绳或慢跑热身5–10分钟，再做髋部、脚踝和肩部的活动。","Get each technique right in the air or on the bag before adding speed and power.":"在加入速度和力量之前，先在空中或沙袋上把每个动作做对。","Spar in gloves, a mouthguard and shin guards; throw elbows and knees only on pads or bags.":"对练时戴拳套、护齿和护胫；肘和膝只能在手靶或沙袋上练习。","Shins toughen gradually with normal training — never strike hard objects to \"condition\" them.":"胫骨会随着正常训练逐渐变得耐打，千万不要用硬物敲打来“锻炼”它们。","Want stronger basic strikes? See <a href=\"../../kungfu/strikes/\">basic punches &amp; kicks</a>; for conditioning, try <a href=\"../../fitness/gym/\">the 10 gym basics</a>.":"想加强基本拳法和腿法？请参阅 <a href=\"../../kungfu/strikes/\">基本拳法与腿法</a>；想锻炼体能，可以试试 <a href=\"../../fitness/gym/\">健身房 10 个基本动作</a>。","Why \"the art of eight limbs\"?":"为什么叫“八肢艺术”？","Because it strikes with eight points: two fists, two elbows, two knees and two shins.":"因为泰拳用双拳、双肘、双膝和双小腿共八个部位攻击。","Do you kick with the foot or the shin?":"泰拳踢腿用脚背还是胫骨？","The roundhouse and low kick land with the shin — far tougher than the foot and more powerful when the hip turns over.":"中段踢和低踢都用小腿胫骨，比脚背耐打得多，配合转髋力量也更大。","When can a beginner start sparring?":"初学者多久可以对打？","Usually after a few months of technique, pads and bag work, when your coach is happy you can control power and defend yourself — starting with light technical sparring.":"通常先练几个月的基本动作、手靶与沙袋，等教练认为你能控制力道与防守，再从轻度技术对打开始。","FIGHTING SPORTS · THAILAND'S ART OF EIGHT LIMBS":"格斗技 · 泰国的「八肢艺术」","Muay Thai Basics: 10 Core Techniques, Step by Step":"泰拳入门：10 个基本技术互动解析","Muay Thai strikes with eight limbs — fists, elbows, knees and shins — plus the clinch up close. Every technique is animated against a grey opponent, with a red ring at the point of contact. Click a step to freeze it; southpaws press SOUTHPAW.":"泰拳用拳、肘、膝、胫骨八个部位攻击，再加上近身箍颈。每个技术都有动画，灰色人形代表对手，红圈标示接触点。点选步骤可定格查看，左撇子请按「反架」。","Fists — jab and cross":"拳 · 前手与后手","Elbows — close range":"肘 · 近距离","Knees — from the clinch":"膝 · 箍颈中","Shins — kick and check":"胫骨 · 踢与挡","Striking limbs":"攻击部位","Fists · elbows · knees · shins":"双拳 · 双肘 · 双膝 · 双胫","Pro bout format":"职业赛制","5 rounds × 3 minutes (varies by event)":"5 回合 × 3 分钟（各赛事略有不同）","For education only; the animations are simplified. Muay Thai is a high-impact contact sport: train under a qualified coach and wear gloves, a mouthguard and shin guards for sparring; throw elbows and knees only on pads or bags.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，动画为简化示意。泰拳是高冲击的接触性运动：请在合格教练指导下训练，对打时使用拳套、护齿、护胫等护具；肘与膝只打手靶或沙袋。","Muay Thai Basics: Stance, Teep, Roundhouse, Elbow, Knee & Clinch — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"泰拳基础：站姿、前踢、摆踢、肘击、膝击与缠抱，互动指南 | KungfuTutor","Learn 10 Muay Thai fundamentals with animated demos against an opponent: stance, jab, cross, teep, roundhouse kick, low kick, elbow, clinch, knee and shin check — with common mistakes and drills.":"通过与对手的动画示范，学习10项泰拳基本功：站姿、直拳、摆拳、前踢、摆踢、低扫踢、肘击、缠抱、膝击和护胫——包括常见错误与练习方法。","Muay Thai Basics — The Art of Eight Limbs, Step by Step":"泰拳基础——八肢之术，逐步学习","Why is Muay Thai called the art of eight limbs?":"为什么泰拳被称为八肢之术？","Because it strikes with eight points of contact: two fists, two elbows, two knees and two shins, plus clinch work to control the opponent.":"因为它用八个接触点进行攻击：两只拳、两个肘、两个膝和两个胫骨，并配合缠抱来控制对手。","What is a teep in Muay Thai?":"泰拳中的前踢是什么？","A push kick: lift the knee, then push the hips forward and drive the ball of the foot into the opponent's stomach or hips to stop them and restore distance.":"一种推踢：提膝，然后向前顶髋，用脚掌前部蹬向对手的腹部或髋部，以阻止对方并恢复距离。","Do you kick with the foot or the shin in Muay Thai?":"在泰拳中，你是用脚还是用胫骨踢？","The roundhouse and low kick land with the shin, which is far tougher than the foot and carries more power when the hip turns over.":"摆踢和低扫踢用胫骨命中，它比脚更坚硬，并且在髋部转动时能产生更大的力量。","WEIGHT BACK · LIGHT LEAD FOOT · HANDS AT THE BROWS":"重心偏后 · 前脚轻 · 手在眉前","Stand with feet about shoulder-width, one foot ahead of the other (left foot forward for right-handers), facing the opponent more squarely than in boxing. Keep roughly 60–70% of your weight on the back leg so the lead foot is light and ready to check kicks or teep. Hold your hands up at brow height, elbows tight to the body, chin tucked, eyes on their chest and hips.":"双脚约与肩同宽，一脚在前一脚在后（右撇子左脚在前），身体比拳击更正面朝向对方。重心大约 60–70% 在后脚，前脚轻，随时可以提起来挡踢或前蹬。双手举在眉毛前方，手肘收紧护住身体，下巴微收，眼睛看着对方的胸口与髋部。","Weight on the front foot (hard to check low kicks); dropping the hands; feet on one line so you lose balance; standing too side-on so the legs are easy targets.":"重心在前脚（难以挡低踢）；双手放低；双脚站成一直线而失去平衡；身体太侧（腿容易被踢）。","Hold your stance in a mirror for a minute, then bounce lightly forward and back without dropping the hands — 3 rounds.":"对镜保持站架 1 分钟，再在原地轻轻前后弹动，保持手不掉下来，3 回合。","A Muay Thai stance has to deal with punches, kicks, elbows and knees, so it is squarer and more weighted to the back than a boxing stance.":"泰拳的站架要应对拳、踢、肘、膝，因此比拳击的站架更正面，重心更偏后。","Knuckles, lead hand":"拳面（前手）","Speed and distance":"速度与距离感","STRAIGHT OUT · STRAIGHT BACK · SHOULDER COVERS CHIN":"直线出 · 直线回 · 肩护下巴","From your stance, shoot the lead hand straight out, turning it palm-down as it lands, with the lead shoulder raised to cover your chin and the other hand by your face. Snap it straight back to guard. A small step with the lead foot adds reach.":"从站架出发，前手直线打出，出拳落点时手转成拳心朝下，前肩抬起护住下巴，另一只手留在脸旁。打完立即沿原路收回护脸。可以配合前脚小步上前增加距离。","Pulling back before punching (telegraphing); dropping the hand afterwards; the rear hand leaving the face; leaning forward.":"出拳前先拉回（预告动作）；打完手掉下来；另一手离开脸；身体往前倒。","3 × 2-minute rounds of jabs on a bag or in a mirror — fast out, fast back.":"对镜或沙袋打单一前手 3 回合 × 2 分钟，重点是快出快收。","The jab measures distance, blinds the opponent and sets up the cross or a kick.":"前手直拳用来量距离、干扰对方视线，并带出后手拳或踢腿。","Knuckles, rear hand":"拳面（后手）","PIVOT THE BACK HEEL · TURN THE HIPS · LEAD HAND GUARDS":"后脚跟转 · 转髋 · 前手护脸","From your stance, turn the back heel out so the hips and shoulders rotate forward, and drive the rear hand straight out — power travels from the floor through the hips to the fist. The lead hand stays by your face. Return along the same line to your stance.":"从站架开始，把后脚跟向外转，带动髋部和肩膀往前转，后手沿直线打出——力量从地面经髋部传到拳头。前手一直留在脸旁。沿原路收回到站架。","Arm-only punching; not turning the back heel; dropping the lead hand; leaving your weight out front.":"只用手臂出拳；不转后脚跟；前手放下；重心留在前面。","Jab–cross combinations on the bag, 3 × 2-minute rounds.":"在沙袋上练习「前手直拳＋后手直拳」组合，3 回合 × 2 分钟。","The cross is the most common power punch and often leads straight into a rear kick.":"后手直拳是最常见的重拳，也常直接接后腿踢。","Teep (Push Kick)":"前蹬","Ball of the foot":"前脚掌","KNEE UP FIRST · PUSH THE HIPS · BALL OF THE FOOT":"先提膝 · 推髋 · 前脚掌","From your stance, lift the lead knee to waist height, then push the hips forward and straighten the leg, driving the ball of the foot into their stomach or hips. Lean back slightly and keep the hands up. Re-chamber the knee before setting the foot down.":"从站架开始，把前腿提膝到腰的高度，然后髋部往前推并伸直腿，用前脚掌推向对方的腹部或髋部。上身稍微后仰，双手保持护头。推完先收回提膝，再把脚放下。","Swinging the leg without lifting the knee (like kicking a ball); no hip push; dropping the hands; slow recovery.":"不提膝、直接甩腿（像踢球）；没有推髋；双手放下；收腿太慢。","On a bag or pad, 3 × 10 per leg, feeling the hips push.":"在沙袋或踢靶上，每条腿 3 组 × 10 次，感受髋部推送。","The teep stops the opponent coming forward, restores distance and breaks balance — Muay Thai's key defensive and offensive kick.":"前蹬用来阻止对方前进、拉开距离、破坏平衡，是泰拳最重要的防守兼攻击腿法。","Explosive hip rotation":"转髋爆发力","PIVOT · TURN THE HIP OVER · LAND THE SHIN · ARM SWINGS BACK":"转前脚 · 翻转髋部 · 用胫骨踢中 · 手臂往后摆","Turn the lead foot out onto the ball of the foot and swing the rear leg up and across while turning the hip right over, landing with the shin on the side of their body. The arm on the kicking side swings down and back to help you turn while the other hand guards your head. Let the leg return to your stance.":"前脚脚尖向外转、踮起，后腿从地面向前上方甩起，同时把髋部完全翻转过去，用小腿胫骨踢中对方身体侧面。踢腿同侧的手往下往后摆，帮助转身，另一手护头。踢完顺势收回站架。","Not pivoting the lead foot (no power, strains the knee); kicking with the top of the foot (easy to injure); not turning the hip over; dropping both hands.":"前脚不转（伤膝、没力）；用脚背踢（易受伤）；髋部没有转过去；两手都掉下来。","Slow pivots and hip turns holding a wall, 10 reps, then 3 × 10 per leg on the bag.":"扶着墙慢速练转脚转髋 10 次，再到沙袋每脚 3 组 × 10 下。","The Muay Thai roundhouse lands with the shin and carries huge power — a main scoring weapon in fights.":"泰拳的中段踢以胫骨踢击、力量极大，是比赛得分的主要武器。","Outside of the thigh":"大腿外侧","PIVOT · CHOP DOWN · OUTSIDE OF THE THIGH":"转前脚 · 往下斜 · 打大腿外侧","Pivot and turn the hip just like the roundhouse, but angle the kick slightly downward and chop the lower shin into the outside of their thigh. It works best straight after punches, while their attention is up high.":"和中段踢一样转前脚、转髋，但踢的角度稍微往下斜，用胫骨下半段砍向对方大腿外侧。常接在拳之后，让对方的注意力在上面。","Throwing it when they are set to check; kicking with the foot or ankle; losing balance afterwards.":"在对方准备好时直接踢（容易被挡）；用脚背或脚踝踢；踢完站不稳。","Jab–cross–low kick combinations, 3 × 2-minute rounds.":"打「前手＋后手＋低踢」组合，3 回合 × 2 分钟。","Low kicks add up — heavy legs and lost balance — a key way to wear an opponent down.":"低踢累积起来会让对方腿部沉重、站不稳，是泰拳消耗对手的重要武器。","Horizontal Elbow":"横肘","Side of the face, brow":"脸侧、眉骨","ARM FOLDED · ELBOW LEVEL · TURN THE HIPS":"手臂折紧 · 手肘水平 · 转髋","At closer than punching range, fold the arm tight with the hand near your own head, turn the hips and shoulders, and slice the elbow level across the side of their face or brow. The other hand guards your head. Return to the guard immediately.":"在比拳更近的距离，手臂折紧、手掌靠近自己的头，转髋转肩，让手肘水平划过对方脸侧或眉骨。另一手护头。打完立刻回到护头。","Throwing from too far (it falls short); not folding the arm; swinging the arm without turning the body; not returning to guard.":"距离太远（打不到）；手臂没折紧；只甩手臂不转身；打完手不回来。","Slow horizontal elbows on pads, 10 each side; later chain them after hooks or from the clinch.":"对手靶慢速练左右横肘各 10 次，熟练后接在勾拳或箍颈之后。","Elbows cut easily and can end fights up close; many amateur events ban or restrict them.":"肘击容易造成割伤，是泰拳近身战的决胜武器。业余赛事常禁止或限制肘击。","The Clinch (Plum)":"箍颈（Plum）","Clinch":"纏抱","Hands behind the head":"双手扣后脑","Head control":"控制头部","HANDS INSIDE · ONE OVER THE OTHER · ELBOWS SQUEEZE":"手从内侧 · 双手交叠 · 手肘夹紧","When chest to chest, bring both hands up the inside of their arms and cup them one over the other behind their head (don't interlace the fingers). Squeeze the elbows together onto their collarbones and pull the head down so they lose posture and balance.":"贴身时，双手从对方手臂内侧往上，交叠扣在对方后脑（不要十指交扣）。手肘往内夹紧，压在对方锁骨上，把头往下拉，让对方失去姿势与平衡。","Interlacing the fingers (they get hurt); flaring the elbows so they slip out; pulling with the arms only; letting your posture drop below theirs.":"十指交扣（手指容易受伤）；手肘张开让对方钻出；只用手拉不用身体；姿势比对方低。","With a partner, take turns: enter the clinch → pull down → release, slowly and gently, a minute at a time.":"与夥伴轮流练“进箍颈 → 拉低 → 放开”，慢速、温和，每次 1 分钟。","The clinch controls the opponent up close and sets up knees and off-balancing sweeps.":"箍颈让你在近距离控制对方，并带出膝击与摔倒。","Straight Knee":"直膝","Stomach, ribs":"腹部、肋骨","PULL THE HEAD DOWN · HIPS FORWARD · KNEE UP AND IN":"拉头往下 · 髋往前 · 膝往上顶","In the clinch, pull their head down while drawing the rear leg back to load, then drive the hips forward and the knee up and in to their stomach or ribs, toes pointing down. Lean back slightly for balance and keep controlling the head with both hands.":"在箍颈中把对方的头往下拉，同时后腿往后拉开蓄力，接着髋部往前推、膝盖往前上方顶入对方腹部或肋骨，脚尖向下。上身略后仰保持平衡，双手一直控制头部。","Lifting the leg without pushing the hips; leaning forward into a head clash; letting go of the head; an unstable support leg.":"只抬腿、髋部不推；身体前倾撞头；放开头部控制；支撑脚站不稳。","3 × 10 knees per leg on a bag or knee pad, then light touch knees with a partner in the clinch.":"对沙袋或膝靶，每条腿 3 组 × 10 次膝撞；再与搭档在箍颈中轻触练习。","Straight knees are short and powerful; many Muay Thai fights are won with them in the clinch.":"直膝距离短但威力大；许多泰拳比赛都靠它在箍颈中取胜。","Check (Shin Block)":"提膝挡踢","Shin, lead leg":"前腿胫骨","Block their kick":"挡住对方的踢","Reaction and balance":"反应与平衡","KNEE UP · TURN IT OUT · HANDS STAY UP":"提膝 · 膝盖外翻 · 手保持护头","As soon as you see their hip turn for a kick, lift the knee on that side and turn it slightly outward so your shin meets their kick. Keep the support leg slightly bent and both hands up. Plant the foot and fire back straight away.":"看到对方髋部转动、起腿，马上把被踢那侧的膝盖提起并稍微外翻，让小腿胫骨挡住对方的腿。支撑腿微屈站稳，双手保持护头。挡完立刻落脚反击。","Watching the foot instead of the hips (too slow); a low knee so the thigh gets hit; dropping the hands; losing balance after the block.":"只看脚不看髋（太慢）；膝盖提得太低，被踢到大腿；手放下来；挡完站不稳。","Your partner throws slow, light kicks while you check, 10 each side; then add a counter after each check.":"搭档慢速轻踢，你练习提膝挡，左右各 10 次；熟练后加上挡完反击。","Checking protects your legs and hurts the kicker's shin, making them think twice.":"挡踢保护你的腿，也会让踢你的人小腿痛，让对方不敢乱踢。","Where every technique starts":"所有技术的起点","High guard · weight back":"高护手 · 重心偏后","The fastest, most-used punch":"最快、最常用的拳","Measures distance, sets things up":"量距离、开路","The power straight punch":"最有力的直拳","Turn foot, hip and shoulder":"转脚、转髋、转肩","Muay Thai's \"jab with the leg\"":"泰拳的「前手拳」","Pushes distance, breaks rhythm":"推开距离、打乱节奏","The signature Muay Thai kick":"泰拳的招牌踢法","Shin, not the foot":"用胫骨不是脚背","Breaks down the legs":"削弱對方的腿","Chops downward":"往下斜砍","The sharpest close-range weapon":"近距离最锋利的武器","Driven by the hips":"转髋带动","Muay Thai's unique stand-up grappling":"泰拳独有的缠抱技术","Control the head, control the body":"控制头就控制身体","The main attack from the clinch":"箍颈中的主要攻击","Drive the hips forward":"髋部往前推","The standard defence to leg kicks":"挡低踢的标准方法","Shin meets shin":"胫骨对胫骨","Feet about shoulder-width, one in front of the other, weight mostly on the back leg":"双脚约与肩同宽前后站，重心偏后脚","The lead foot stays light, ready to lift for a check or a teep":"前脚轻点地，随时可提起来防守或前蹬","Hands up by the brows, elbows tight, chin tucked":"双手护在眉前、手肘收紧、下巴微收","Snap the lead hand straight out, shoulder up to protect the chin":"前手直线打出，肩膀护住下巴","Bring it straight back to guard the face":"原路收回护脸","Turn the back heel, hips and shoulders and drive the rear hand straight out":"后脚跟转起、转髋转肩，后手直拳打出","Return — the lead hand guards the face the whole time":"收回，前手一直护脸","Push the hips forward and drive the ball of the foot into their stomach":"髋部前推，用前脚掌把对方推开","Re-chamber the knee":"收腿回提膝","Back to stance with the distance restored":"落回站架，距离拉开了","Pivot on the lead foot (toes turn out) and swing the rear leg up":"前脚脚尖外转，后腿往前上方甩起","Turn the hip over and land with the shin on the body; the rear arm swings down and back":"转髋，用小腿胫骨踢中对方身体；后手往下往后摆","Let the leg come back":"顺势收回","Back to stance, hands up":"回到站架，双手护头","Chop down with the shin into the outside of their thigh":"用胫骨往下斜踢对方大腿外侧","Close range — the opponent is inside punching distance":"近距离，对方在手臂范围内","Draw the lead elbow back and load the hips":"前手手肘往后收、准备转身","Turn the hips and slice the elbow level across the side of the face":"转髋，手肘水平划过对方脸侧","The opponent is chest to chest":"对方靠得很近","Slide both hands up the inside and cup them, one over the other, behind their head":"双手从内侧伸上去，交叠扣在对方后脑","Squeeze the elbows together on their collarbones and pull the head down":"手肘夹紧对方锁骨，把头往下拉","Hold the control — they lose their posture and balance":"保持控制，对方失去平衡","Control the head in the clinch":"在箍颈中控制对方的头","Draw the rear leg back to load":"后腿往后拉开、准备","Drive the hips forward and the knee up and in to the stomach":"髋部往前推，膝盖向前上方顶入腹部","Return the leg, keep the clinch":"收腿，保持箍颈","They start a low kick":"对方起腿低踢","Lift the lead knee, turn it out and block with the shin":"前脚提膝外翻，用胫骨挡住","Hands stay up the whole time":"双手保持护头","Plant the foot, ready to fire back":"落脚，准备反击","Distance":"距离感","Shoulders":"肩部","Setting it up":"组合时机","Grip & squeeze":"握力与夹力","Shin structure":"胫骨结构","What is sambo?":"什么是桑搏？","Sambo is a martial art developed in the Soviet Union in the 1920s and 1930s; the name is a Russian short form of \"self-defence without weapons\". It draws on judo and many folk wrestling styles. Fighters wear a jacket (the kurtka), shorts and wrestling shoes, and win with throws, hold-downs and joint locks.":"桑搏（Sambo）是 1920 至 1930 年代在苏联发展出来的格斗术，名称是俄文「不用武器的自卫」的缩写。它吸收了柔道和多种民族摔跤的技术。选手穿外套（kurtka）、短裤和摔跤鞋，用摔、压制和关节技取胜。","Sport sambo and combat sambo":"运动桑搏与格斗桑搏","Sport sambo is jacket wrestling: throws, hold-downs and arm and leg locks are allowed, but chokes are not. Throwing the opponent flat on their back while you stay standing wins the match outright (a \"total victory\"). Combat sambo adds punches, kicks, knees, elbows and chokes; it was built for military and police self-defence and is fought with gloves and protective gear.":"运动桑搏是穿衣摔跤：可以摔、压制、锁手臂和腿部关节，但不允许勒颈。把对方摔到背部着地而自己保持站立，可以直接获胜（称为「完全胜利」）。格斗桑搏再加上拳、踢、膝、肘和勒颈，原本是为军队与警察的自卫而设计，比赛时戴拳套和护具。","Apply leg locks slowly — let go the moment your partner taps or says stop.":"腿锁要慢慢施压：对方一拍地或说「停」，马上放开。","Tap early when you are caught in a lock — never fight through it.":"被锁时早点拍地认输，不要硬撑。","Related: <a href=\"../mma/\">MMA basics</a> and <a href=\"../../self-defence/basics/\">self-defence basics</a>.":"相关课程：<a href=\"../mma/\">MMA 入门</a>、<a href=\"../../self-defence/basics/\">自我防卫基础</a>。","How is sambo different from judo?":"桑搏和柔道有什么不同？","Both throw in a jacket, but sambo allows direct leg grabs and leg locks, while judo allows chokes and its modern rules ban grabbing the legs directly.":"两者都穿外套摔人，但桑搏允许直接抱腿和腿部关节技，柔道则有勒颈而现代规则禁止直接抱腿。","Breakfalls, the stance and grips, then simple foot sweeps and trips.":"受身、站姿与抓握，然后是简单的扫腿和绊摔。","How do you win a sambo match?":"怎样才能赢得桑搏比赛？","A clean throw onto the back while you stay standing, a submission, or points from throws and hold-downs — 10 seconds of hold-down scores 2 points, 20 seconds scores 4.":"干净利落地把对手摔到背部着地，而你保持站立；或让对手认输；或通过摔投和压制得分。压制 10 秒得 2 分，20 秒得 4 分。","FIGHTING SPORTS · SAMBO FOR BEGINNERS":"格斗运动 · 桑搏入门","Sambo Basics: Throws, Hold-Downs and Leg Locks in 8 Lessons":"桑搏基础：8 节课学会摔法、压制与腿部关节技","Sambo is a jacket-wrestling sport and self-defence system from the Soviet Union. These 8 lessons start with grips and falling safely, then three throws, a hold-down on the ground and sambo's famous ankle lock, and finish with how combat sambo links strikes to a throw. Red jacket is you, blue is your partner; the red ring marks the point of contact.":"桑搏是源自苏联的穿着外衣摔跤运动，也是一种自卫体系。这 8 节课从抓握和安全倒地开始，然后学习三种摔法、地面压制，以及桑搏著名的踝关节锁，最后讲解格斗桑搏如何把打击与摔投连接起来。红色外衣代表你，蓝色代表你的搭档；红圈标示接触点。","Throws":"摔","Sweeps, trips and leg grabs":"扫、绊与抱腿","Hold-downs and leg locks":"压制与腿部关节技","Combat sambo":"格斗桑搏","Strikes into throws":"打击接摔投","Two kinds of sambo":"两种桑搏","Sport sambo · combat sambo":"运动桑搏 · 格斗桑搏","Hold-down points":"压制得分","10 seconds scores 2 points, 20 seconds scores 4":"压制 10 秒得 2 分，20 秒得 4 分","SIDE · RED = YOU · BLUE = PARTNER":"侧面 · 红＝你 · 蓝＝搭档","For education only; the animations are simplified. Learn to breakfall first, and practise throws and locks only on mats with a qualified coach; apply locks slowly and let go the moment your partner taps. Combat sambo sparring needs gloves, a mouthguard and headgear.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，动画为简化示意。请先学会受身；摔法和关节技只能在有合格教练指导的垫子上练习；关节技要慢慢施加压力，对方一拍地就立即松开。格斗桑搏对打须佩戴拳套、护齿和头盔等护具。","Sambo Basics: Grips, Breakfalls, Throws, Hold-Downs & Leg Locks — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"Sambo 基础：握法、倒地保护、投技、压制与腿部关节技 — 互动指南 | KungfuTutor","Learn 8 sambo fundamentals with animated demos against a partner: stance and jacket grips, the back breakfall, forward foot sweep, back trip, single-leg pick-up, side hold-down, straight ankle lock and a combat sambo strike-to-throw.":"通过与搭档进行的动画演示，学习 8 项 Sambo 基本功：站姿与上衣握法、后倒保护、前脚扫、后绊摔、单腿抱起、侧压制、直腿踝关节锁，以及实战 Sambo 的打击转投技。","Sambo Basics — Throws, Hold-Downs and Leg Locks, Step by Step":"Sambo 基础 — 投技、压制与腿部关节技，循序渐进","A grappling martial art and sport developed in the Soviet Union in the 1920s and 1930s. The name is a Russian short form of 'self-defence without weapons'. Fighters wear a jacket and win with throws, hold-downs and joint locks.":"一种摔跤式格斗技击与运动，1920 年代至 1930 年代在苏联发展起来。其名称是俄语「不用武器的自卫」的简称。选手穿着上衣，以投技、压制和关节技取胜。","What is the difference between sport sambo and combat sambo?":"Sport sambo（体育 Sambo）与 combat sambo（实战 Sambo）有什么区别？","Sport sambo is a jacket-wrestling sport with throws, hold-downs and arm and leg locks but no chokes. Combat sambo adds punches, kicks, knees, elbows and chokes, and was built for military and police self-defence.":"Sport sambo 是一项穿上衣的摔跤运动，包括投技、压制以及手臂和腿部关节技，但不允许勒颈。Combat sambo 则加入拳击、踢击、膝击、肘击和勒颈，原为军队与警察的自卫而设计。","By a clean throw that lands the opponent on their back while you stay standing, by a submission, or on points from throws and hold-downs. A 10-second hold-down scores 2 points and a 20-second hold-down scores 4.":"通过干净利落的投技将对手摔倒在背上而你仍站立，或通过关节技降服，或以投技和压制得分取胜。10 秒的压制得 2 分，20 秒的压制得 4 分。","Stance and Jacket Grips":"站姿与抓握","SOFT KNEES · STRAIGHT BACK · LAPEL · SLEEVE":"膝微弯 · 背挺直 · 前手领 · 后手袖","Stand with the feet a little wider than the shoulders, knees soft and back straight, weight between both feet. The lead hand grips their lapel and the rear hand grips the sleeve near the elbow. Once you hold both, pull the sleeve and push or lift the lapel to move their weight onto their toes or heels — breaking the balance, the set-up for every throw.":"双脚比肩稍宽、膝盖微弯、背挺直，重心放在两脚中间。前手抓对方的衣领，后手抓对方肘部附近的袖子。抓好之后用「拉袖、推或提领」让对方的重心移到脚尖或脚跟，这叫破坏平衡，是所有摔法的准备。","Bending at the waist with the head forward (easy to pull down); feet in one line; holding on without moving; stiff, locked-straight arms.":"弯腰把头伸向前（容易被拉倒）；双脚站成一直线；只抓不动；手臂完全伸直、僵硬。","Sambo is fought in a jacket (the kurtka), so the grip fight decides who gets to throw first.":"桑搏比赛穿外套（kurtka），抓握决定谁能先发动摔法。","From standing, squat down with the chin on your chest and eyes on your belt. Sit the hips down just behind your heels and roll back with a rounded back. As your back meets the mat, slap it with both whole arms at about 45° from your body to spread the impact. Your head never touches the mat.":"从站立深蹲下去，下巴贴胸、眼睛看自己的腰带。臀部坐在脚跟后方，背部弓圆往后滚。背部着地的同时，双臂在身体两侧约45°用整只手臂拍垫，把冲击分散掉。头始终不碰地。","In any throwing sport you will be thrown a lot; a good breakfall is what lets you train safely for years.":"在任何摔投类运动中你都会经常被摔；正确的受身让你能安全地练习多年。","Forward Foot Sweep":"前扫脚","Throw":"摔","Grip the lapel and sleeve and move with them. As they step forward and the foot is about to land — before their weight is on it — sweep the sole of your foot against their ankle while your hands pull and turn their upper body. With the foot swept away, they fall.":"抓住衣领和袖子，跟着对方移动。当对方向前踏步、脚快要落地但重心还没放上去时，用你的脚掌贴着对方脚踝向前扫，同时双手拉转对方的上身。脚被扫走后，对方就会摔倒。","Foot sweeps are fast and cheap on energy and leave you standing — a textbook clean throw.":"扫脚快、省力，而且让你保持站立，是干净摔法的典型例子。","Back Trip":"后绊摔","Your leg behind theirs":"腿挡在对方腿后","Drive and timing":"推进与时机","STEP BEHIND · BLOCK · DRIVE BACK":"前脚踏到对方腿后 · 挡住 · 双手往后推","With the lapel and sleeve gripped, step your lead leg deep behind their lead leg so your leg blocks theirs. Stay close and drive your hands towards their back. As they step back they trip over your leg and land on their back, while you stay on your feet.":"抓住衣领和袖子，前脚大步踏到对方前脚的后方，让你的腿挡在对方腿后。身体贴近，双手朝对方的后方推。对方往后退时会被你的腿绊住而背部着地。整个过程你保持站稳。","Not stepping deep enough (the block misses); staying too far away and pushing with the arms only; falling with them; pushing down instead of back.":"踏得不够深（腿挡不住）；身体离太远，只用手推；自己跟着倒下；推的方向往下而不是往后。","Drill the step and block slowly 10 times each side, then full reps on mats with your partner breakfalling.":"慢速练习踏步和挡住，每边各 10 次，然后在软垫上与伙伴完整练习，伙伴做受身。","Works best when they push into you — their own pressure helps trip them.":"当对方往前压时特别好用：对方的力量让自己更容易被绊倒。","Single-Leg Pick-Up":"抱单腿摔","Hands behind the knee":"双手抱膝后","Explosiveness and level change":"爆发力与降重心","DROP THE LEVEL · BEHIND THE KNEE · LIFT · DRIVE":"屈膝降低 · 抱膝后 · 抬腿 · 往前推","Bend the knees to drop your level with a straight back, step in and wrap both hands behind their lead knee. Lift that leg high while your body drives forward. Standing on one leg, they cannot balance and land on their back. Unlike modern judo, sambo allows grabbing the legs directly.":"屈膝降低重心（背部挺直），上前一步，双手环抱对方前腿膝盖的后方。把那条腿抬高的同时，身体向前推进。对方单腿站立无法保持平衡，会背部着地。与现代柔道不同，桑搏允许直接抓腿。","Bending at the waist with the head down (easy to stuff); shooting from too far; grabbing the ankle instead of behind the knee (hard to lift); catching the leg but not driving.":"弯腰低头（容易被压住）；离得太远才冲；抱住脚踝而不是膝后（不好抬）；抱到腿后不推。","On mats, drill the level drop and knee catch 10 times, then slow full reps with a partner — only on mats with a coach.":"在软垫上练「降重心 + 抱膝」10 次，再与伙伴慢速完整练习。只在有教练的软垫上进行。","When they stand tall and grip hard, a leg pick goes around the upper-body grip fight.":"当对方站得很直、抓得很紧时，抱腿可以绕过上身的抓握。","Side Hold-Down":"侧压制","Chest on chest":"胸口压胸口","CHEST ON CHEST · CONTROL HEAD AND ARM · WIDE BASE":"胸压胸 · 控头控手 · 底盘宽","With them on their back, kneel at their side and put your chest on their chest. One arm goes round behind their head, the other controls their near arm. Keep the legs spread and knees on the mat, with your weight on them. In sport sambo a 10-second hold-down scores 2 points and a 20-second hold-down scores 4, and a fighter can score with a hold-down only once per match.":"对方仰躺时，你跪在对方身侧，胸口压在对方胸口上。一手从对方头后绕过，另一手控制对方靠近你的手臂。双脚张开、膝盖撑地，把体重压在对方身上。运动桑搏中，压制 10 秒得 2 分，压制 20 秒得 4 分，每场只能用压制得分一次。","Kneeling too tall (no chest pressure); legs together (easy to roll); holding the head but not the arm; letting go in a panic when they bridge.":"跪得太高（胸口没压住）；双脚并拢（一翻就倒）；只抱头不控手；被翻时慌张放手。","Sport sambo has no chokes, so the hold-down is one of the main ways to score on the ground.":"桑搏没有勒颈（运动桑搏），所以压制是地面上主要的得分方式之一。","Straight Ankle Lock":"直脚踝锁","Forearm on the Achilles":"前臂压阿基里斯腱","FOOT TRAPPED · LEAN BACK SLOWLY · RELEASE ON TAP":"脚夹腋下 · 慢慢后仰 · 拍地即放","Sit in front of their foot and trap it under your armpit, with your legs over their thigh. Put the bony edge of your forearm just above their heel (the Achilles tendon) and lock your hands. Then lean back slowly and lift the chest so the pressure goes into their ankle. The moment they tap or say stop, let go.":"坐在对方脚前，把对方的脚夹在你的腋下，你的双腿压住对方的大腿。前臂的骨头卡在对方脚跟上方（阿基里斯腱），双手扣紧。然后慢慢往后仰、挺胸，压力会集中在对方脚踝。对方一拍地或说「停」，马上放开。","Jerking it on fast (causes injuries); putting the forearm on the foot instead of the Achilles; legs not controlling the thigh (they pull the foot out); not letting go after the tap.":"猛然用力（会造成受伤）；前臂放在脚掌而不是跟腱；双腿没压住对方（对方可以抽脚）；对方拍地后还不放。","Under a coach, partners practise the position with very light pressure, 5 times each, and both practise tapping.":"在教练指导下，伙伴之间只做「位置 + 极轻施压」各 5 次，双方都要练习拍地。","Sport sambo allows leg locks, and a submission wins the match outright.":"运动桑搏允许腿部关节技，让对方认输可以直接获胜。","Combat Sambo: Strike, Grip, Trip":"格斗桑搏：打击接摔","Linking strikes to throws":"打击与摔的衔接","1-2 · CLOSE AND GRIP · BACK TRIP · STAY UP":"1-2 · 贴近抓握 · 后绊摔 · 站稳","Combat sambo adds punches, kicks, knees and elbows, and also allows chokes. Throw a jab and cross so their hands come up to cover, then close the gap while their attention is high, take the lapel and sleeve and finish with the back trip. Stay standing afterwards with your guard back up.":"格斗桑搏允许拳、踢、膝、肘，也允许勒颈。先用前手、后手直拳让对方举手护头，趁对方注意上方时贴近，抓住衣领与袖子，再用后绊摔把对方摔倒。摔完保持站立，双手回到防守。","Punching and staying out of range (no grips); closing in with the head down and no guard; waiting too long once you have the grips; falling with them.":"打完停在远距离（抓不到）；贴近时低头不护脸；抓到后犹豫太久；摔完跟着倒。","With gloves and protection, hit pads with a 1-2, then your partner lets you grip and finish the back trip — slowly, 3 × 5 reps.":"戴拳套与护具，对着手靶打 1-2 后，搭档让你抓握并完成后绊摔，慢速 3 × 5 次。","Combat sambo was built for military and police self-defence; linking strikes to throws is its core.":"格斗桑搏原本为军警自卫而设计，打击与摔的衔接是它的核心。","Where every throw starts":"所有摔法的起点","Learn this before any throw":"学摔之前必学","Leg blocks, hands drive":"腿挡、手推","Trips them backwards":"把对方向后绊倒","Leg grabs are allowed in sambo":"桑搏允许抱腿","Drop → catch → lift and drive":"降重心 → 抱腿 → 抬起推","Scores on the ground":"地面得分","10 s = 2 points · 20 s = 4 points":"10 秒 2 分 · 20 秒 4 分","Sambo's trademark leg lock":"桑搏的招牌腿锁","Sambo with strikes":"加入打击的桑搏","Punches set up the grips and throw":"打击为抓握与摔创造机会","Feet a little wider than the shoulders, knees soft, back straight, hands forward ready to grip":"双脚比肩稍宽、膝微弯、背挺直，双手在前准备抓握","Step in with small steps; don't let them grip first":"小步靠近，不要让对方先抓到","Lead hand grips the lapel, rear hand grips the sleeve near the elbow":"前手抓衣领，后手抓袖子（肘部附近）","Pull the sleeve and push or lift the lapel to break their balance":"拉袖、推领，打破对方的平衡","Keep your posture, ready to attack":"保持姿势，随时准备进攻","Squat low, chin to chest, eyes on your belt":"深蹲，下巴贴胸，眼睛看腰带","Sit the hips down just behind your heels and roll back":"臀部坐在脚跟后方，往后滚","Keep pulling and turning with the hands as they leave the floor":"双手继续拉转，让对方在空中翻过","They land on their back while you stay standing — a clean throw like this can win outright":"对方背部着地、你保持站立 —— 干净的摔可以直接获胜","Step your lead leg deep behind their lead leg":"前脚大步踏到对方前脚的后方","Your leg blocks behind theirs while your hands drive them backwards":"你的腿挡住对方的腿，双手往后推","They trip over your leg and fall backwards":"对方绊到你的腿往后倒","They land on their back; you stay on your feet":"对方背部着地，你站稳不跟着倒","Stance, with their lead leg in front of you":"站姿，对方的前脚在你前方","Bend the knees to drop your level, back straight":"弯膝降低重心，背保持挺直","Wrap both hands behind their lead knee":"双手抱住对方前脚的膝后","Lift the leg high and drive forward with your body":"把腿抬高，同时用身体往前推","On one leg they cannot balance and land on their back":"对方单脚站不稳，背部着地","They are on their back; you kneel close to their side":"对方仰躺，你跪在对方身侧","Chest on their chest, one arm round the head and one controlling the arm":"胸口压在对方胸口，一手绕过头、一手控制手臂","Hold it: 10 seconds scores 2 points, 20 seconds scores 4":"保持压制：10 秒得 2 分，20 秒得 4 分","If they bridge, spread your legs for a wider base and stay heavy":"对方挺腰想翻时，张开双脚加宽底盘，保持重量压下","Sit down with their foot trapped under your armpit and your legs over their thigh":"坐下，对方的脚夹在你腋下，你的双腿压住对方的大腿","Put the bony edge of your forearm just above their heel (the Achilles tendon) and lock your hands":"前臂骨头卡在对方脚跟上方（阿基里斯腱），双手扣紧","Lean back slowly and lift the chest — the pressure goes on their ankle":"慢慢往后仰、挺胸，压力在对方的脚踝","Combat sambo: gloves on, hands guarding the face":"格斗桑博：戴拳套，双手护脸","Cross — their hands come up to cover":"后手直拳，让对方举手护头","Close the gap behind the punches and take the grips":"趁机贴近，抓住衣领与袖子","Leg behind theirs and drive back — the back trip":"腿踏到对方腿后，往后推 —— 后绊摔","They go down; you stay standing with your guard ready":"对方倒地，你保持站立、做好防守","Level change":"降重心","Squat":"深蹲","Legs · push":"下肢 · 推","Quads, glutes, core":"股四头肌、臀大肌、核心","Barbell (beginner: bodyweight to a box)":"杠铃（初学：徒手坐箱）","3–5 sets × 5–10 reps":"3–5 组 × 5–10 次","FLAT BACK · KNEES OVER TOES · WHOLE-FOOT DRIVE":"背部平直 · 膝朝脚尖 · 全脚掌发力","Stand with feet about shoulder-width, toes turned slightly out, and the bar resting on your upper back. Breathe in and brace your core, then sit the hips back and down while pushing the knees out over the toes until your thighs are at least parallel to the floor. Keep your back flat and heels down, then drive up through the whole foot as you breathe out. The bar should stay over the middle of your foot.":"双脚约与肩同宽、脚尖微向外。杠铃放在上背（斜方肌上），双手握紧。吸气、收紧核心，臀部往后往下坐，膝盖朝脚尖方向推出，直到大腿至少与地面平行。全程背部平直、脚跟不离地，再用整个脚掌踩地站起并呼气。杠铃应该一直在脚掌中间的正上方。","Knees caving in; heels lifting; rounding the back or cranking the head up; half-depth reps; hips shooting up first so it turns into a good-morning.":"膝盖往内夹；脚跟离地；圆背或抬头过度；只蹲一半；起身时臀部先起、变成弯腰。","Start with bodyweight squats to a box, 3 × 10; once steady, learn with an empty bar (20 kg) and add weight in small steps.":"先用徒手坐箱练习 3 组 × 10 次，动作稳定后再用空杠（20 公斤）学习，每次只加一点重量。","Squats build leg and core strength and underpin everyday movements like sitting, standing and lifting.":"深蹲训练腿部与核心力量，也是坐下、站起、搬东西等日常动作的基础。","Deadlift":"硬举","Posterior chain · pull":"后侧链 · 拉","Glutes, hamstrings, back":"臀大肌、腿后肌、背部","Barbell":"杠铃","3–5 sets × 3–6 reps":"3–5 组 × 3–6 次","BAR OVER MID-FOOT · FLAT BACK · BAR STAYS CLOSE":"杠在脚掌上 · 背平 · 杠贴腿","Stand with feet hip-width and the bar over the middle of your feet. Hinge and bend the knees to grip the bar with shins touching it, back flat and shoulders just in front of the bar. Brace and stand up as if pushing the floor away, keeping the bar against your legs. Once past the knees, drive the hips forward to stand tall. To lower, push the hips back first and follow the same path down.":"双脚与髋同宽，杠铃在脚掌中间正上方。弯腰屈膝握杠，小腿碰到杠，背部平直、肩膀略在杠的前方。吸气收紧，像把地板推开一样站起，杠铃贴着腿往上。过膝后髋部往前推，站直锁定。放下时髋部先往后，沿原路放回。","Rounding the back; letting the bar drift away from the body; hips rising first; leaning back at the top; pulling with the arms.":"弯曲背部；让杠铃离开身体；臀部先抬起；顶端后仰；用手臂拉。","Practise the hip hinge with a broomstick or empty bar, 3 × 10, before adding weight; start every rep from a dead stop.":"加重量前，先用木棍或空杠练习“髋部后推”动作 3 × 10；每一次都从完全静止开始。","The deadlift trains the whole back of the body and is the safe way to pick heavy things off the floor.":"硬举训练整个身体背面，也是安全地从地上搬起重物的正确方法。","Bench Press":"卧推","Upper body · push":"上肢 · 推","Chest, triceps, front shoulders":"胸大肌、三头肌、前三角肌","Barbell, bench (use a spotter)":"杠铃、卧推椅（请找保护者）","BLADES SQUEEZED · ELBOWS ~45° · TOUCH THE LOWER CHEST":"肩胛收紧 · 手肘约 45° · 碰下胸","Lie on the bench with your eyes under the bar and feet planted. Grip a little wider than shoulder-width and squeeze your shoulder blades back and down. Unrack the bar over your shoulders, lower it under control to touch the lower chest with elbows about 45° from your body, then press it back up, drifting slightly towards the shoulders.":"躺在卧推椅上，眼睛在杠铃正下方，双脚稳稳踩地。握距略宽于肩，肩胛骨往后往下收紧。把杠铃推离架子到肩膀上方，慢慢放下碰到下胸，手肘与身体约 45°。再把杠铃推回起点，路线略往肩膀方向。","Flaring elbows to 90° (hard on the shoulders); bouncing the bar off the chest; lifting the hips off the bench; bending the wrists back.":"手肘向外张成 90°（伤肩）；杠铃在胸口弹起；臀部离开椅子；手腕向后折。","Start with an empty bar or dumbbells, 3 × 10; always use a spotter or a rack with safety bars.":"先用空杠或哑铃练 3 × 10，每次都请人在旁保护，或在有安全杠的架子内练习。","The bench press is one of the most effective builders of chest and arm pushing strength.":"卧推是训练胸部与手臂推力最有效的动作之一。","Overhead Press":"站姿肩推","Shoulders, triceps, core":"三角肌、三头肌、核心","Barbell (or dumbbells)":"杠铃（或哑铃）","3–5 sets × 5–8 reps":"3–5 组 × 5–8 次","GLUTES & CORE TIGHT · STRAIGHT BAR PATH · HEAD THROUGH":"臀腹收紧 · 杠走直线 · 头穿过手臂","Stand with feet hip-width, the bar resting on the front of your shoulders and elbows under and slightly in front of it. Squeeze glutes and core, tip your head back slightly to clear a path, and press the bar straight up. Once it passes your forehead, bring your head through between your arms and lock out directly overhead.":"双脚与髋同宽站立，杠铃放在肩膀前方、锁骨上，手肘在杠的下方略前。收紧臀部和腹部，头稍微往后让路，把杠铃直线推过头顶。杠铃过额头后头往前穿过手臂之间，在头顶正上方锁定。","Leaning back and arching the lower back; pressing the bar forward around the face; flared elbows; dipping the knees to cheat.":"腰部过度后仰；杠铃往前推出（绕过脸）；手肘太外开；膝盖弯曲借力。","Start with an empty bar or light dumbbells, 3 × 8, and check side-on in a mirror that the bar travels straight up.":"先用空杠或轻哑铃练 3 × 8，对镜从侧面看杠铃是否走直线。","The press builds shoulder strength and core stability — the same move as lifting a case into an overhead locker.":"肩推训练肩膀与核心稳定，把行李放上置物架就是同样的动作。","Bent-over Row":"俯身划船","Upper body · pull":"上肢 · 拉","Lats, mid-back, biceps":"背阔肌、菱形肌、二头肌","3–4 sets × 8–12 reps":"3–4 组 × 8–12 次","HINGE · FLAT BACK · ELBOWS DRIVE BACK":"髋部前倾 · 背平 · 手肘往后拉","Hold the bar, soften the knees and hinge at the hips until your torso is about 45° with a flat back and the arms hanging. Drive the elbows back and up, squeezing the shoulder blades, until the bar touches your upper stomach, then lower slowly. Your torso angle stays the same throughout.":"双手握杠，膝盖微弯，髋部往后推让上身前倾约 45°，背部平直，手臂自然下垂。手肘往后往上拉，肩胛骨夹紧，让杠铃碰到上腹部，再慢慢放下。全程上身角度不变。","Swinging the body to heave the weight; rounding the back; shrugging the shoulders; cutting the range short.":"用身体甩起来；圆背；耸肩用斜方肌拉；拉到一半就放。","Learn the elbow drive with one-arm dumbbell rows, one hand on a bench, 3 × 10 each side.":"先用单臂哑铃划船（一手撑椅子）学会手肘往后拉的感觉，3 × 10 每边。","Rows balance all the pushing (like the bench press), keeping shoulders healthy and posture upright.":"划船平衡推的动作（如卧推），让肩膀更健康、姿势更挺。","Pull-up":"引体向上","Lats, biceps, grip":"背阔肌、二头肌、握力","Pull-up bar (beginner: box for negatives)":"单杠（初学：箱子做离心）","3–5 sets × as many good reps as you can":"3–5 组 × 尽力次数","SHOULDERS DOWN · ELBOWS DOWN & BACK · CHIN OVER":"先沉肩 · 手肘往下拉 · 下巴过杠","Grip the bar a little wider than your shoulders, palms facing forward, and hang with straight arms. First pull your shoulders down away from your ears, then drive the elbows down and back until your chin clears the bar, and lower under control to straight arms.":"双手略宽于肩、掌心朝前握住单杠，手臂伸直悬吊。先把肩膀往下压离耳朵，再把手肘往下往后拉，直到下巴超过单杠，然后有控制地放下到手臂伸直。","Kicking and swinging for momentum; half reps; dropping down fast; shrugging the shoulders up.":"用腿踢、身体摆荡借力；只拉一半；放下太快；耸肩。","Can't do one yet? Choose Beginner: step up to the top and lower slowly over 3–5 seconds, 3 × 5, or use a resistance band.":"还做不到一下？选“初学”程度：踩箱子到顶点，用 3–5 秒慢慢放下，3 × 5；或用弹力带辅助。","The pull-up is one of the best upper-body pulling exercises and builds a strong grip.":"引体向上是最好的上半身拉力训练之一，也能大幅提升握力。","Push-up":"伏地挺身","Chest, triceps, core":"胸大肌、三头肌、核心","None (beginner: from the knees)":"不需器材（初学：跪姿）","3 sets × 8–20 reps":"3 组 × 8–20 次","HANDS UNDER SHOULDERS · ONE STRAIGHT LINE · ELBOWS 45°":"手在肩下 · 身体一直线 · 手肘 45°","Place your hands just wider than and under your shoulders, with a straight line from head to heels and your stomach and glutes tight. Bend the elbows back at about 45° and lower your whole body together until your chest is just above the floor, then push the floor away to return.":"双手放在肩膀正下方略宽，从头到脚跟成一直线，收紧腹部和臀部。手肘往后约 45° 弯曲，整个身体一起下降到胸口接近地面，再把地面推开回到起点。","Hips sagging or piking up; elbows flared into a T; dipping only the head; not going low enough.":"臀部下垂或翘太高；手肘外开成 T 字；只动头部（点头）；下得不够深。","If full push-ups are too hard, choose Beginner (from the knees) or put your hands on a table edge, 3 × 10.":"做不到标准动作就选“初学”（跪姿），或双手撑在桌边做斜板伏地挺身，3 × 10。","Push-ups train pushing strength and core stability together — the best equipment-free upper-body move.":"伏地挺身同时训练推力和核心稳定，是不需要器材的最佳上半身动作。","Reverse Lunge":"后跨弓箭步","Legs · single-leg":"下肢 · 单脚","Quads, glutes, balance":"股四头肌、臀大肌、平衡","None (dumbbells optional)":"不需器材（可手持啞铃）","3 sets × 8–12 per leg":"3 组 × 每脚 8–12 次","STEP BACK · DROP STRAIGHT DOWN · FRONT KNEE OVER ANKLE":"往后跨 · 垂直下降 · 前膝在脚踝上","Stand with feet hip-width. Take a long step back with one foot and, keeping the front foot planted, drop straight down until the back knee nearly touches the floor and the front thigh is about parallel, front knee over the ankle. Push through the whole front foot to return to standing, then switch legs.":"双脚与髋同宽站立。一脚往后跨一大步，前脚不动，身体垂直往下，直到后膝接近地面、前腿大腿约与地面平行，前膝在脚踝上方。用前脚全脚掌踩地把自己推回站立，再换脚。","Too short a step so the front knee shoots far forward; folding the chest down; front knee caving in; slamming the back knee into the floor.":"步伐太小，前膝超過腳尖太多；上身前倒；前膝往內夾；後膝重重撞地。","Hold a wall or chair for balance, 3 × 8 per leg; once steady, hold dumbbells for extra load.":"扶著牆或椅子練習平衡，每腳 3 × 8；穩定後雙手持啞鈴增加負重。","Single-leg work builds balance and evens out left–right strength — great for running and climbing stairs.":"單腳動作訓練平衡與左右力量差，對跑步和上樓梯都很有幫助。","Plank":"平板支撐","Core · hold":"核心 · 靜態","Abs, glutes, shoulders":"腹肌、臀部、肩膀","Exercise mat":"瑜伽墊","3 sets × 20–60 seconds":"3 組 × 20–60 秒","ELBOWS UNDER SHOULDERS · HEAD TO HEELS IN LINE · BREATHE":"手肘在肩下 · 頭到腳跟一直線 · 正常呼吸","Rest on your forearms with elbows directly under your shoulders, start on your knees, then lift them so head, shoulders, hips and heels form one straight line. Squeeze your stomach and glutes, look at the floor, breathe normally and hold.":"前臂著地、手肘在肩膀正下方，先跪姿準備，再把膝蓋抬離地面，讓頭、肩、臀、腳跟成一直線。收緊腹部和臀部，眼睛看地面，正常呼吸並保持。","Letting the hips sag (hurts the lower back); hips piked up high; holding your breath; lifting or dropping the head.":"臀部下垂（腰會痛）；臀部翹太高；憋氣；頭往上抬或垂下。","Use the timer below starting at 20 seconds and add 5–10 seconds a week; stop when your form slips — quality beats time.":"用下方的計時器從 20 秒開始，每週增加 5–10 秒；姿勢跑掉就停，品質比時間重要。","The plank trains your core to resist movement, which protects the lower back and steadies every other lift.":"平板支撐訓練核心「不動」的能力，能保護下背、幫助所有其他動作更穩定。","Glute Bridge":"臀橋","Glutes · hip extension":"臀部 · 伸髖","Glutes, hamstrings":"臀大肌、腿後肌","3 sets × 12–15 reps":"3 組 × 12–15 次","HEELS DOWN · SHOULDERS TO KNEES IN LINE · NO ARCHING":"腳跟踩地 · 肩到膝一直線 · 不拱腰","Lie on your back with knees bent, feet hip-width and heels close to your seat, arms by your sides. Press through your heels to lift the hips until shoulders, hips and knees form a straight line, squeeze the glutes for 1–2 seconds, then lower slowly.":"仰躺、屈膝，双脚踩地与髋同宽，脚跟靠近臀部，双手放在身体两侧。脚跟踩地把臀部往上推，直到肩膀、髋部、膝盖成一直线，臀部夹紧停 1–2 秒，再慢慢放下。","Arching the lower back instead of using the glutes; pushing through the toes; knees falling out or in; dropping down fast.":"用腰拱起来而不是臀部发力；脚尖踩地；膝盖向外倒或往内夹；放下太快。","3 × 15; once easy, try single-leg bridges or hip thrusts with your shoulders on a bench.":"3 × 15，熟练后改成单腿臀桥，或把肩膀靠在椅子上做臀推。","Long sitting \"switches off\" the glutes; bridges wake them up and take strain off the lower back and knees.":"久坐容易让臀部“沉睡”；臀桥能唤醒臀肌、减轻下背和膝盖的负担。","The king of lifts":"动作之王","Hips back, knees over toes":"臀往后坐、膝朝脚尖","Lifting a weight off the floor":"从地上拿起重物","A flat back comes first":"背部平直是第一要务","The classic upper-body press":"最经典的上半身推","Shoulder blades back, elbows 45°":"肩胛收紧、手肘 45°","Pressing a weight overhead standing":"站着把重量推过头","Whole body tight, no leaning back":"全身收紧、不后仰","The basic back builder":"背部厚度的基本动作","Torso angle stays fixed":"身体角度不动","The bodyweight pulling king":"自身体重的拉力王","Shoulders down first, then pull":"先沉肩、再拉","Do it anywhere":"随时随地都能做","Body like a plank":"身体像一块木板","Easier on the knees than a forward lunge":"比前跨更护膝","Drop straight down":"垂直下降","The basic core exercise":"最基本的核心训练","Use the hold timer below":"用下方计时器练习","A beginner glute activator":"唤醒臀部的入门动作","Squeeze and pause at the top":"顶点夹紧停 1–2 秒","Feet shoulder-width, toes slightly out, arms forward":"双脚与肩同宽，脚尖微向外，手向前伸","Bar on the upper back; breathe in and brace":"杠铃放在上背，吸气、核心收紧","Sit the hips back and down; knees track over the toes":"臀部往后往下坐，膝盖朝脚尖方向","Lightly touch the box, then stand":"坐到箱子上轻碰即起","Thighs at least parallel; back stays flat":"大腿至少与地面平行，背部保持平直","Drive up through the whole foot; breathe out":"脚掌全掌踩地发力站起，吐气","Bar over mid-foot; flat back, shoulders just in front of the bar":"杠铃在脚掌中间上方，背部平直、肩膀在杠前","Brace and \"push the floor away\"":"吸气收紧，把地板「推开」","Bar slides up the shins; past the knees, drive the hips forward":"杠铃贴着小腿往上，过膝后髋部向前","Stand tall and lock out — don't lean back":"站直锁定，不要后仰","Hips back first, lower along the same path":"髋部先往后，沿原路放下","Feet planted, shoulder blades squeezed, arms straight":"双脚踩地、肩胛骨收紧，手臂伸直","Lower under control, elbows about 45° — not flared out":"慢慢放下，手肘约 45° 而非向外张开","Touch the lower chest":"轻触下胸","Press back up, slightly towards the shoulders":"推回起点，杠铃略往肩膀方向","Bar on the front of the shoulders, elbows under and slightly ahead":"杠铃在锁骨前，手肘在杠下略前","Squeeze the glutes and brace":"臀部与核心收紧","Tip the head back so the bar travels straight up":"头稍微后仰让杠铃直线通过","Lock out overhead, head through between the arms":"推到头顶锁定，头穿过手臂之间","Lower back to the shoulders under control":"有控制地放回肩上","Hinge to about 45°, flat back, arms hanging":"髋部后推前倾约 45°，背部平直，手臂垂直","Drive the elbows back and squeeze the shoulder blades":"手肘往后拉，肩胛骨夹紧","Bar touches the upper stomach; torso angle doesn't change":"杠铃碰到上腹，身体角度不变","Lower slowly to straight arms":"慢慢放回，手臂完全伸直","Jump or step up to the top, chin over the bar":"从箱子跳或站到顶点，下巴过杠","Lower yourself slowly over 3–5 seconds":"用 3–5 秒慢慢放下（离心）","At the bottom, step back up and repeat":"到底后再站回去，重复","Hands just wider than shoulders, palms forward, hang with straight arms":"双手略宽于肩，掌心朝前，手臂伸直悬吊","First pull the shoulders down away from the ears":"先把肩膀往下压（肩胛下沉）","Drive the elbows down and back until the chin clears the bar":"手肘往下往后拉，直到下巴过杠","Lower under control to straight arms":"有控制地放下到手臂伸直","Knees down; a straight line from knees to head":"膝盖着地，从膝到头成一直线","Hands under the shoulders; a straight line from head to heels":"双手在肩膀下方，从头到脚跟成一直线","Elbows back at about 45°; the whole body lowers as one":"手肘往后约 45°，身体整条一起下降","Chest just above the floor":"胸口接近地面","Push the floor away; hips don't sag":"推地回到起点，臀部不下垂","Stand with feet hip-width":"双脚与髋同宽站立","Take a long step backwards":"一脚往后跨一大步","Drop straight down: back knee near the floor, front knee over the ankle":"垂直往下，后膝接近地面，前膝在脚踝上方","Push through the front foot to stand back up":"前脚踩地推回站立","Forearms down, elbows under the shoulders, start on the knees":"前臂着地，手肘在肩膀正下方，先跪姿","Lift the knees: head to heels in one line, squeeze stomach and glutes":"抬起膝盖：头到脚跟成一直线，收紧腹部与臀部","Breathe normally and hold the position":"正常呼吸，保持姿势","Lie on your back, knees bent, heels close to the seat":"仰躺屈膝，脚跟靠近臀部","Press through the heels and lift the hips":"脚跟踩地，臀部往上推","Shoulders to knees in one line; squeeze the glutes for 1–2 seconds":"肩膀到膝盖成一直线，臀部夹紧 1–2 秒","Lower slowly":"慢慢放下","GREEN LINE = HEAD TO HEELS IN ONE LINE":"绿线＝头到脚跟一直线","DASHED LINE = MID-FOOT (KEEP THE BAR OVER IT)":"虚线＝脚掌中间（杠铃保持在上方）","Quadriceps":"股四头肌","Glutes":"臀大肌","Hip & ankle mobility":"髋踝活动度","Hamstrings":"腿后肌","Lower back":"竖脊肌","Grip":"握力","Chest":"胸大肌","Triceps":"三头肌","Front shoulders":"前三角肌","Shoulder-blade control":"肩胛稳定","Core stability":"核心稳定","Upper back":"上背","Lats":"背阔肌","Mid-back":"中背","Biceps":"二头肌","Lower-back hold":"下背稳定","Hip stability":"髋部稳定","Abs":"腹肌","Shoulder stability":"肩膀稳定","Breathing control":"呼吸控制","Hip extension":"髋部伸展","Current level: ":"目前程度：","Beginner version":"初学版本","Standard":"标准动作","Exercise {n} of 10 · {type}":"第 {n} 个动作 · {type}"," · beginner version":"· 初学版本","The ten exercises at a glance":"十个动作一览","Exercise":"动作","Pattern":"类型","Main muscles":"主要肌群","Sets × reps":"组数 × 次数","A simple beginner week":"初学者的一周范例","Train 2–3 days a week with a rest day between, full body each time:":"每周练 2–3 天、中间休息一天，每次做全身：","Day A: ":"A 日：","Squat, bench press (or push-up), row, plank":"深蹲、卧推（或俯卧撑）、划船、平板支撑","Day B: ":"B 日：","Deadlift (or glute bridge), overhead press, pull-up (or negatives), lunge":"硬举（或臀桥）、过顶推举、引体向上（或离心下放）、弓步","Alternate A and B. Do 2–4 sets of each with a weight you can lift with good form and 1–2 reps to spare; when it feels easy, add a little weight or a rep next time.":"A、B 日轮流做。每个动作 2–4 组，选一个姿势正确、做完还能多做 1–2 下的重量；能轻松完成时，下次再加一点点重量或次数。","Breathing and bracing":"呼吸与核心收紧","For standing barbell lifts like the squat, deadlift and press, take a deep breath into your belly before the rep and brace as if someone were about to poke your stomach; hold it on the way down and breathe out after the hard part. For light, high-rep work just breathe normally — don't hold your breath. If you have high blood pressure or heart problems, ask your doctor first.":"做深蹲、硬举、肩推这类站姿杠铃动作时，动作前先深吸一口气到腹部、像要被打肚子一样收紧核心，下降时保持，用力完成后再吐气。轻重量、高次数的动作则保持正常呼吸，不要憋气。有高血压或心脏问题的人请先咨询医生。","Warm up for 5–10 minutes, then do 1–2 light sets with an empty bar or light weight.":"先热身 5–10 分钟，再用空杠或轻重量做 1–2 组热身组。","Bench and squat inside a rack with safety bars, or with a spotter.":"卧推和深蹲请在有安全杠的架子内练习，或请人保护。","Stop when your form breaks down — form always comes before weight.":"姿势跑掉就停，重量永远排在姿势后面。","Stop for joint pain (not muscle burn) and get it checked by a doctor or physio if needed.":"关节疼痛（不是肌肉酸）就停止，必要时请医师或物理治疗师检查。","Want to put your strength to the test? See <a href=\"../../hyrox/\">the 8 HYROX stations</a>.":"想把力量用在比赛上？看看 <a href=\"../../hyrox/\">HYROX 8 大关卡</a>。","How many days a week should a beginner train?":"初学者每周要练几天？","Two or three full-body sessions with rest days between is plenty. Consistency matters more than frequency.":"2–3 天全身训练就足够，中间让肌肉休息恢复。规律比次数多更重要。","Should I train to failure?":"做到力竭比较好吗？","Beginners don't need to. Leaving 1–2 reps in reserve keeps form clean and injury risk low, and progress is just as fast.":"初学者不需要。每组保留 1–2 下的余力，姿势会比较好、受伤风险也低，进步一样快。","Why keep the bar over mid-foot?":"为什么杠铃要在脚掌中间上方？","In standing barbell lifts mid-foot is your balance point; keeping the bar over it stops the weight pulling you forwards or backwards and makes the lift most efficient.":"站姿杠铃动作中，脚掌中间是身体的平衡点；杠铃保持在它正上方，你就不会被重量往前或往后拉，动作也最省力。","Gym basics":"健身房基本动作","FITNESS · STRENGTH TRAINING FOR BEGINNERS":"体能训练 · 健身入门","10 Essential Gym Exercises, With Correct Form":"健身房 10 个基本动作：正确姿势动画教学","Squat, deadlift, bench press, overhead press, row, pull-up, push-up, lunge, plank and glute bridge — every basic pattern: push, pull, squat, hinge, single-leg and core. The green trail shows the bar path and the dashed line marks mid-foot; choose Beginner to see easier versions.":"深蹲、硬拉、卧推、肩推、划船、引体向上、俯卧撑、弓步、平板支撑、臀桥——涵盖推、拉、蹲、髋铰链、单腿与核心。绿色轨迹显示杠铃路线，虚线是脚掌中间；选“初学”可看更简单的版本。","Key exercises":"基本动作","Push · pull · squat · hinge · single-leg · core":"推 · 拉 · 蹲 · 髋 · 单脚 · 核心","Main muscles, this exercise":"目前动作主要肌群","Suggested sets × reps":"建议组数次数","A weight you can lift with 1–2 reps to spare":"姿势正确、还能多做 1–2 下的重量","Exercises you have mastered":"动作掌握进度","Mark each exercise as mastered below":"可在下方标记为“已熟悉”","Choose your level (squat, pull-up and push-up have beginner versions)":"选择程度（深蹲、引体向上、俯卧撑有初学版本）","Pick an exercise":"选择动作查看细节","Equipment":"器材","How to start":"怎么开始","Why do it":"为什么要练","SIDE 90°":"侧面 90°","Muscles worked":"主要训练肌群","Relative involvement":"相对参与度","For education only; the animations are simplified. Check with a doctor before starting strength training if you have health concerns; beginners should get coaching from a qualified trainer, and always use a spotter or safety bars for heavy lifts.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，动画为简化示意。开始重量训练前若有健康问题请先咨询医师；初学者建议请合格教练指导，大重量训练请使用保护者或安全杠。","Gym Exercises for Beginners: 10 Key Movements with Correct Form | KungfuTutor":"初学者健身房训练：10个关键动作及正确姿势 | KungfuTutor","Learn correct form for 10 essential gym exercises with step-by-step animation: squat, deadlift, bench press, overhead press, bent-over row, pull-up, push-up, reverse lunge, plank and glute bridge — with beginner versions, common mistakes, sets and reps.":"通过分步动画学习10个基础健身房动作的正确姿势：深蹲、硬拉、卧推、肩上推举、俯身划船、引体向上、俯卧撑、反向弓步、平板支撑和臀桥。内容包括初学者版本、常见错误、组数和次数。","Gym Basics — 10 Exercises with Correct Form, Animated":"健身房基础：10个动作，正确姿势，动画演示","What are the best gym exercises for beginners?":"初学者最好的健身房动作有哪些？","A balanced beginner plan covers a squat, a hip hinge such as the deadlift or glute bridge, a horizontal push (bench press or push-up), a vertical push (overhead press), a pull (row or pull-up), a single-leg move (lunge) and a core exercise (plank).":"均衡的初学者计划包括：深蹲；髋部铰链动作，如硬拉或臀桥；水平推举，如卧推或俯卧撑；垂直推举，如肩上推举；拉的动作，如划船或引体向上；单腿动作，如弓步；以及核心训练，如平板支撑。","How many sets and reps should a beginner do?":"初学者应该做多少组和次数？","Two to four sets of about 8 to 12 reps with a weight you can lift with good form, leaving one or two reps in reserve, two or three times a week.":"每周两到三次，每组大约8到12次，使用你能以良好姿势举起的重量，每组保留一到两次余力，做两到四组。","Should the bar stay over the middle of the foot?":"蹲起、硬拉和肩上推举等站立杠铃动作中，杠铃是否应保持在中足上方？","In standing barbell lifts like the squat, deadlift and overhead press, keeping the bar roughly over mid-foot keeps you balanced and the lift efficient.":"在深蹲、硬拉和肩上推举等站立杠铃动作中，让杠铃大致保持在中足上方，可以帮助你保持平衡并提高动作效率。","Women Open":"女子公开","the most popular entry division":"最多人参加的入门组别","Women Pro":"女子精英","high-intensity competitive division":"高强度女子竞技组别","Men Open":"男子公开","Men Pro":"男子精英","Doubles":"双人组","run together, split every station as you like":"两人一起跑，每站工作量自由分配","Women":"女子","Men":"男子","Mixed":"混合","Relay":"四人接力","each of 4 runs 2 × 1 km and does 2 stations":"四人各跑 2 × 1 km、各完成 2 站","Mixed (F / M)":"混合（女 / 男）","SkiErg":"SkiErg","Lats and core power":"背阔肌与核心爆发","Stand on the SkiErg base, grab the handles overhead and drive them down while you hinge at the hips and soften the knees, dropping your bodyweight into the pull. Finish with the hands beside the thighs, then ride back up tall. The power comes from the hip hinge, not just the arms.":"双脚站在滑雪机底座，双手由头顶握住把手向下拉，同时屈髋、微屈膝，把身体重量“压”进把手；拉到大腿两侧后，手臂与身体回到顶端再重复。力量主要来自髋部折叠，不是只靠手臂。","A judge resets the monitor first. Both feet must stay on the base the whole time — heels may hang off but must not touch the floor; jumping is fine if you land back on the base. After 1,000 m, keep both feet on the base and raise a hand until the judge confirms. Infringements: a warning first, then +15 s each.":"开始前由裁判重设显示器。全程双脚须留在底座上，脚跟可悬空但不可碰地；可以做跳跃式动作，但落地须回到底座。完成 1,000 m 后须双脚仍在底座并举手示意，等裁判确认后才可离开。违规：第一次警告，之后每次加罚 15 秒。","Use 4 × 250 m intervals to find a pace you can hold; drill the hip-hinge-plus-pull timing; don't sprint the first station — save legs for the runs.":"以 4 × 250 m 间歇找出稳定配速；练习“髋部折叠＋手臂下拉”同步；第一站不要冲太快，保留跑步能量。","Sled Push":"推雪橇","Quads and calf drive":"股四头肌与小腿推蹬力","Grip the upright poles with straight or slightly bent arms, lean about 45° and drive with short, quick steps on the balls of your feet like a sprint start. Keep the back flat and the core braced, and keep the sled moving — restarting a stopped sled costs the most energy.":"双手握住雪橇直立杆，手臂打直或微弯，身体前倾约 45°，像短跑起步一样用前脚掌小步、快速地推蹬。背部保持平直、核心收紧，让雪橇持续移动，避免停下再起动。","Use the lane the judge assigns; sled and athlete start fully inside the Racers Box; it is 4 × 12.5 m and the whole sled must cross each end line before changing direction; never interfere with the next lane. Infringements: a warning, then +15 s each.":"使用裁判指定的赛道；开始前雪橇和选手都须完全在 Racers Box 内；共 4 × 12.5 m，雪橇须整个越过每段终点线才可换方向；不可干扰隔壁赛道。违规：警告后每次加罚 15 秒。","Build with back squats and Bulgarian split squats; drill low, short steps; carpet friction varies by venue, so train heavier than race weight.":"重训做后蹲举、保加利亚分腿蹲；练习低姿势小步推蹬；不同场地地毯摩擦力不同，练习时可用比比赛更重的负荷。","Sled Pull":"拉雪橇","Grip, back and posterior chain":"握力、背肌与后侧链","Stand in the Racers Box, lean back slightly with a solid stance and pull the rope hand over hand so the sled slides to you. Step back to use your bodyweight and legs, and keep the slack rope tidy behind you. When the sled crosses the line, run to the other end and pull it back.":"站在 Racers Box 内，身体略为后倾、双脚稳稳站开，双手交替把绳索往后拉，让雪橇滑向自己；可以后退一步借用体重与腿部力量，把拉过的绳索整理在身后。雪橇过线后，跑到赛道另一端再拉回来。","Stay standing — no sitting or kneeling pulls; while holding the rope don't step on the front or back line of the Racers Box; keep the rope in your lane (it may run out of the back); the whole sled must pass the 12.5 m line, 4 times. Infringements: a warning, then +15 s each.":"全程须站立，不可坐着或跪着拉；手持绳索时不可踩到 Racers Box 前后的实线；绳索须留在自己赛道（可延伸到赛道后方）；雪橇须整个越过 12.5 m 线才算完成一段，共 4 段。违规：警告后每次加罚 15 秒。","Rows, pull-ups and dead hangs for grip; sit back and pull with legs and bodyweight, not arms alone; practise stacking the rope behind you so you don't trip.":"划船、引体向上与死悬垂练握力；用“坐后”的姿势以腿和体重拉，而不是只靠手臂；练习把绳索整理在身后，避免绊倒。","Burpee Broad Jumps":"波比跳远","Full-body power and stamina":"全身爆发与心肺耐力","Hands down, lower until your chest touches the floor, jump or step the feet back in, then broad-jump forward taking off and landing on both feet together. Land straight into the next burpee. Rhythm matters more than distance — a medium jump you can repeat beats a huge one.":"双手撑地、身体俯卧让胸口贴地，再跳（或踏）回蹲姿，接着双脚同时起跳向前跳远，落地后直接进入下一下波比。重点是保持节奏，跳远距离适中即可，不必每次跳最远。","Chest must clearly touch the floor every rep; take off and land with both feet together (max 5 cm stagger), no extra steps; hands go down within 30 cm of your front toes; when you come out of the burpee your feet may not pass your fingertips; finish by jumping fully over the line. Using a knee to get up is allowed.":"每次波比胸口须明确触地（乳头线碰地）；起跳和落地须双脚同时，两脚前后差不可超过 5 cm，不可多踏小步；下一个波比双手须放在前脚脚尖前 30 cm 内；从波比起身时脚不可超过指尖；最后须双脚完全跳过终点线。可以用膝盖辅助起身。","Practise steady EMOM sets; find your most economical jump length; rehearse 1 km run straight into burpee broad jumps.":"用EMOM（每分钟固定次数）练习稳定节奏；找出自己最省力的跳远距离；演练跑完 1 km 后直接接波比跳远，习惯疲劳下的动作。","Rowing":"划船机","Leg drive, back pull, stamina":"腿推、背拉与心肺耐力","The stroke goes legs → body → arms: push the footplate, swing from a forward lean to a slight lean back, then draw the handle to the lower ribs. Recover in reverse: arms → body → legs. Most of the power comes from the legs.":"划桨顺序是「腿 → 身体 → 手」：脚先用力推踏板，身体由前倾摆到略为后仰，最后把把手拉到下胸。回程反过来「手 → 身体 → 腿」。大部分力量来自双腿。","A judge resets the monitor; stay seated until 1,000 m is done; you may stop and rest with the handle in its holder, but don't stand or leave the seat until the judge confirms. Damper is preset to 6 and footplates to position 4 — both adjustable.":"开始前由裁判重设显示器；必须坐在划船机上直到完成 1,000 m；可以停下并把把手放回架上休息，但在裁判确认完成前不可站起或离开座位。阻力预设 6、脚踏板预设第 4 格，可自行调整。","Use 500 m intervals to learn your sustainable split; aim for about 26–30 strokes per minute; use this station to reset your breathing before the carry.":"以 500 m 间歇找出可维持的配速；桨频约每分钟 26–30 下；利用这站调整呼吸，为后面的农夫走路做准备。","Farmers Carry":"农夫走路","Grip and core stability":"握力与核心稳定","One kettlebell in each hand, arms hanging by your sides, chest up, shoulders down, core tight, and move with short quick steps. Eyes forward and keep the bells off your thighs. Fast walking or a light jog both work.":"双手各提一个壶铃，手臂自然垂在身侧，挺胸、肩膀下沉、收紧核心，用小而快的步伐前进。眼睛看前方，不要让壶铃撞到大腿。可以快走或小跑。","Take and return the bells from the marked box by the station; carry both bells at all times with arms straight by your sides; you may put them down to rest but not move them forward; return them upright in the right box or take a 30 s penalty; using the wrong weight means redoing the station or disqualification.":"由工作站旁的标示框取出并归还壶铃；移动时须同时提着两个壶铃，手臂伸直在身侧；可放下休息，但放下时壶铃不可往前移；完成后壶铃须放回正确的框并把手朝上，否则罚 30 秒；用错重量须重做整站，否则取消资格。","Dead hangs and heavy carries for grip; try to go unbroken on race day; short quick steps reduce swing.":"用死悬挂和重物行走练握力；比赛时尽量一次走完不放下；用短而快的步伐减少晃动。","Sandbag Lunges":"负重弓箭步","Quad and glute endurance":"下肢股四头与臀肌耐力","Rest the sandbag across the back of both shoulders (on the upper traps), hold it steady, and step forward into alternating lunges, dropping straight down until the back knee touches the floor. Stand up tall and keep moving for 100 m.":"把指定重量的沙袋扛在双肩后方（上背斜方肌处），双手抓稳两侧，交替向前跨出弓箭步，垂直下蹲到后膝轻触地面，再站直推进，连续完成 100 公尺。","The back knee must clearly touch the floor each rep; finish each rep standing tall (knees and hips straight); alternate legs; no extra steps between reps; the bag stays on both shoulders — never rested on the floor or anything else (+15 s each time); the front foot must fully cross the finish line and the bag goes back to its area or +30 s.":"每一下后膝须明确触地；每下结束须站直（膝与髋完全伸直）；左右脚须交替；两下之间不可多踏小步；沙袋须全程由双肩承托，不可放在地上或其他地方卸重（每次罚 15 秒）；最后前脚须完全越过终点线，沙袋须放回指定区，否则罚 30 秒。","Build to 50 m of unbroken walking lunges; stay upright with an even stride; this is the leg-endurance gate before the final station.":"练习 50 m 行走弓箭步不休息；保持上身直立、步幅一致；这是最后一站前的大腿耐力关键。","Wall Balls":"药球投掷","Coordination and willpower":"全身协调与意志力","Stand tall holding the ball at your chest, squat until the hips are below the knees, then drive up with the legs and throw the ball to the target above. Catch it and flow straight into the next squat.":"双手抱球在胸前站直，深蹲到髋部低于膝盖，然后用双腿发力站起，顺势把球抛向上方目标。接住球后直接进入下一下深蹲。","Start each set standing tall with the ball — no scooping it off the floor straight into a throw; hips must go below the knees; hit your own target (women 2.70 m, men 3.00 m); catch and go, or let it drop and stand tall before the next rep — no catching off the bounce. Any fault is a no-rep.":"开始时须站直抱球，不可从地上捡起就直接抛；深蹲时髋部须低于膝盖；球须击中自己的目标（女子 2.70 m、男子 3.00 m）；接住球后再开始下一下，或让球落地后重新站直再开始；不可接弹地球直接续做。违规该下不计（No-rep）。","Break it up — 4 × 25 or 5 × 20 with short rests; train squat endurance and breathing rhythm; watch your depth when tired to avoid no-reps.":"拆组完成，例如 4 × 25 或 5 × 20，组间休息要短；练习深蹲耐力与呼吸节奏；疲劳时特别注意深蹲深度，避免 No-rep。","Base move: double-pole pull":"基础动作：双臂下拉 (Double Pole)","Upper-body pull · coordination":"上肢拉力 · 全身协调","Base move: leaning drive":"基础动作：前倾推进 (Drive)","Leg power · heaviest station":"下肢爆发 · 最重关卡","Base move: hand-over-hand pull":"基础动作：双手交替拉绳","Grip · posterior chain":"握力 · 后侧链","Base move: burpee + broad jump":"基础动作：波比＋立定跳远","Full-body power · cardio test":"全身爆发 · 心肺试炼","Base move: legs → body → arms":"基础动作：腿 → 身体 → 手","Full-body pull · breathing reset":"全身拉力 · 呼吸调节","Base move: loaded walk":"基础动作：负重行走","Grip · core stability":"握力 · 核心稳定","Base move: walking lunge":"基础动作：弓箭步 (Lunge)","Alternating legs · endurance test":"双腿交替 · 肌耐力试炼","Base move: squat + throw":"基础动作：深蹲＋上抛","Coordination · final push":"全身协调 · 最后冲刺","no added load":"无负重限制","Damper 6 (adjustable)":"阻力 6（可自行调整）","Lats / upper back":"背阔肌／上背","Cardio":"心肺"," incl. sled":"（含雪橇）","Quads":"股四头肌","Calves":"小腿","Grip / forearms":"握力／前臂","Hamstrings & glutes":"腿后肌与臀","bodyweight":"徒手自身体重","Bodyweight":"自身体重","Quads / glutes":"股四头／臀肌","Chest & triceps":"胸与三头肌","Damper 6 · footplate 4":"阻力 6 · 脚踏板第 4 格"," kettlebells":"壶铃","Traps / upper back":"斜方肌／上背","sandbag":"沙袋"," sandbag":"沙袋","Glute endurance":"臀大肌耐力","Balance & core":"平衡与核心","Mental grit":"意志抗压","reps":"次"," ball · target ":"药球 · 目标","BOTH FEET STAY ON THE BASE":"双脚始终踩在底座上","STAY IN YOUR LANE · 4 × 12.5 m":"留在自己的跑道内 · 4 × 12.5 m","STAND UP · STAY INSIDE THE BOX":"站起来 · 留在方框内","CHEST MUST TOUCH THE GROUND":"胸部必须触地","STAY SEATED UNTIL 1,000 m":"坐好直到 1,000 m","ARMS STRAIGHT BY YOUR SIDES":"手臂伸直贴于身体两侧","KNEE MUST TOUCH GROUND":"膝盖必须触地","HIPS BELOW KNEES · HIT THE TARGET":"臀部低于膝盖 · 击中目标","Current division: ":"目前组别：","Each of 4 teammates runs 2 × 1,000 m":"四位队员各跑 2 段 × 1,000 m","8 × 1,000 m, one before each station":"8 段 × 1,000m 穿插于每站前","; sled push ":"；雪橇推进",", wall ball ":"、药球","after 1 km":"1km 跑后","Comes after run {n} of 8 (1,000 m), via the RoxZone":"前置赛段：第 {n} 段 1,000m 跑步后进入 RoxZone","100 reps":"100 次"," — load":"规格／负重"," — movement demo":"动作与距离示意","Division":"组别","Sled push":"推雪橇","Sled pull":"拉雪橇","Farmers carry":"农夫走路","Lunge bag":"弓箭步沙袋","Wall ball":"药球","What is HYROX?":"HYROX 是什么？","HYROX is an indoor fitness race. Everyone, everywhere, does the same format: run 1 km, complete one functional workout station, and repeat eight times. Because distances, movements and loads are standardised worldwide, a time set in one city compares directly with any other.":"HYROX 是一项室内「健身竞速赛」：所有选手在世界各地都完成同一套流程——跑 1 公里，接着完成一个功能性训练站，重复 8 次。因为距离、动作和负重全球统一，你在任何一个城市的成绩都可以直接和其他人比较。","The transition area between the running track and each station is called the RoxZone. It is easy to ignore, but a few seconds lost finding equipment on each of eight visits can add up to minutes.":"跑步与站点之间的转换区叫做 RoxZone。很多人忽略了这里：从跑道进站、找器材、出站，每次只差几秒，8 次累积下来就可能是好几分钟。","Loads for every division":"各组别负重一览","Sled weights include the sled. All divisions: SkiErg 1,000 m, sled push and pull 50 m each (4 × 12.5 m), burpee broad jumps 80 m, row 1,000 m, farmers carry 200 m, lunges 100 m, 100 wall balls. Women's and men's Doubles/Relay use Women Open / Men Open loads. Source: official HYROX website and the 2026/27 rulebook.":"雪橇重量已包含雪橇本身。所有组别：滑雪机 1,000 m、推／拉雪橇各 50 m（4 × 12.5 m）、波比跳远 80 m、划船 1,000 m、农夫走路 200 m、弓箭步 100 m、药球 100 次。双人组与接力的「女子／男子」分组分别使用女子公开／男子公开重量。资料来源：HYROX 官方网站及 2026/27 规则书。","Pacing: running is half the race":"配速策略：跑步占了比赛的一半","The 8 km of running is roughly half your finishing time. The classic mistake is going out too fast on run 1 and arriving at the sled push with empty legs. Run the first four laps at a pace where you can still speak in short sentences, note your lap times, and only push in the second half. The sled push, sled pull and lunges hit the legs hardest, so leave room for them.":"8 公里跑步大约占完赛时间的一半。最常见的错误是第一段跑太快，在推雪橇前就把腿用光。建议以「可以说短句」的强度跑前 4 段，记录每段时间；后半段如果还有余力再加速。站点中，推雪橇、拉雪橇和弓箭步最伤腿，跑步配速要预留空间。","Singles, Doubles or Relay?":"单人、双人还是接力？","For a first race, Doubles is a friendly option: you both run the full 8 km but split each station however you like. In the Relay, four teammates each run 2 × 1 km and complete 2 stations — a good fit for friends or workplace teams who want the race atmosphere.":"第一次参赛可以考虑双人组：两人一起跑完全部 8 公里，但每一站的工作量可以自由分配。接力则由四人组队，每人跑 2 段 1 公里并完成 2 个站点，适合想体验比赛气氛的朋友或公司团队。","What are the 8 HYROX stations in order?":"HYROX 8 站的顺序是什么？","SkiErg → Sled Push → Sled Pull → Burpee Broad Jumps → Rowing → Farmers Carry → Sandbag Lunges → Wall Balls, each after a 1 km run.":"滑雪机 → 推雪橇 → 拉雪橇 → 波比跳远 → 划船 → 农夫走路 → 负重弓箭步 → 药球投掷，每站之前都要先跑 1 公里。","What if I can't finish a station?":"没做完一站会怎样？","Under the rulebook, failing to complete any station in full is a disqualification. You may rest within the station, but you have to finish it.":"依规则书，任何一站没有完整完成都会被取消资格。可以在站内休息，但必须做完。","How high is the wall ball target?":"药球目标有多高？","Women (Open and Pro) 2.70 m; men (Open and Pro) 3.00 m.":"女子（公开与精英）2.70 m，男子（公开与精英）3.00 m。","Are these animations official demos?":"这些动画是官方示范吗？","No. The animations are drawn by KungfuTutor to illustrate the key points of each movement; the official HYROX rulebook is the final word on standards.":"不是。动画由 KungfuTutor 自行绘制，用来说明动作重点；正式规则请以 HYROX 官方规则书为准。","HYROX · THE WORLD SERIES OF FITNESS RACING · 2026/27 SEASON STANDARDS":"HYROX 全球统一室内混合健身竞赛 · 2026/27 赛季标准","HYROX: The 8 Functional Stations, Explained Interactively":"HYROX 8 大功能性训练关卡互动解析","Every race is 8 × 1 km runs, each followed by one of 8 functional stations in a fixed order. Pick any station below to see an animated demo, the load for your division, the judging standards and how to train for it.":"每场比赛由“8 次 1 公里跑步”交替穿插“8 个固定顺序功能性站点”组成。点选下方任一关卡，即可切换查看动画示范、各组别通关负重规则与备赛训练重点。","Total running (about 50% of race time)":"总跑步距离（约占完赛时间 50%）","Workout stations (fixed order worldwide)":"训练站（全球固定顺序）","Push, pull, squat, lunge, carry and jump":"涵盖推、拉、蹲、弓步、搬运与跳跃","Reference finish time, this division":"目前检视组别参考完赛时间","Stations you have mastered":"备赛关卡掌握进度","Mark each station as mastered below":"可在下方将各关卡标记为“已熟悉”","Choose your division (loads and standards update instantly)":"切换参赛组别（即时更新负重与通关标准）","Pick a station (in fixed race order)":"选择关卡查看细节（依比赛固定顺序排列）","Distance / reps":"距离／规定次数","Main demand":"主要考验能力","How to move":"动作说明","Judging rules":"通关规则","How to train":"备赛重点","Load profile of this station":"此关卡体能负荷分布","Relative demand":"相对需求指数","KungfuTutor.com is an independent education site and is not affiliated with HYROX World GmbH; HYROX is a trademark of its owner. Loads and rules are summarised from the official 2026/27 rulebook — always check the latest official rules before racing. Check your health before training and consult a doctor or qualified coach where needed.":"KungfuTutor.com 为独立教育网站，与 HYROX World GmbH 无任何关系；HYROX 为其所有者的商标。重量与规则依官方 2026/27 规则书整理，比赛以官方最新公告为准。运动前请评估自身健康状况，必要时咨询医师或合格教练。","HYROX 8 Stations Explained — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"HYROX 8 个站点详解 — 互动指南 | KungfuTutor","Interactive HYROX guide: all 8 stations in race order with animated movement demos, official weights for every division (Open, Pro, Doubles, Relay), judging standards and training tips.":"HYROX 互动指南：按比赛顺序介绍全部 8 个站点，附动画动作示范，列出每个组别（Open、Pro、Doubles、Relay）的官方重量、评判标准和训练建议。","HYROX 8 Stations — Interactive Movement Guide":"HYROX 8 个站点：互动动作指南","SkiErg 1,000 m, Sled Push 50 m, Sled Pull 50 m, Burpee Broad Jumps 80 m, Rowing 1,000 m, Farmers Carry 200 m, Sandbag Lunges 100 m and 100 Wall Balls, each after a 1 km run.":"SkiErg 1,000 m、Sled Push 50 m、Sled Pull 50 m、Burpee Broad Jumps 80 m、Rowing 1,000 m、Farmers Carry 200 m、Sandbag Lunges 100 m，以及 100 Wall Balls，每项之前都先跑 1 km。","How heavy is the HYROX sled push?":"HYROX 的雪橇推重有多重？","Including the sled: 102 kg for Women Open, 152 kg for Women Pro and Men Open, and 202 kg for Men Pro.":"包括雪橇在内：女子 Open 为 102 kg，女子 Pro 和男子 Open 为 152 kg，男子 Pro 为 202 kg。","How high is the HYROX wall ball target?":"HYROX 的 wall ball 目标高度是多少？","2.70 m for women and 3.00 m for men, in both Open and Pro.":"女子组（Open 和 Pro 均适用）为 2.70 m，男子组（Open 和 Pro 均适用）为 3.00 m。","Five Stances":"五大步型","KUNG FU FOUNDATIONS · THE FIVE BASIC STANCES (WU BU)":"传统功夫基本功 · 长拳五大步型（五步）","The 5 Basic Kung Fu Stances, Explained Interactively":"功夫五大步型互动解析：马、弓、虚、仆、歇","Stances are the foundation of kung fu: a stable base is what gives punches and kicks their power. Pick a stance to watch it from the front or side, see exactly where the feet go and how the weight is shared, then practise with the built-in stance timer.":"步型是功夫的地基：站得稳，拳脚才有力量。点选下方任一步型，可以从正面或侧面看动画、检视脚的位置与重心分配，并用站桩计时器开始练习。","Basic stances (Changquan system)":"基本步型（长拳体系）","Horse · Bow · Empty · Drop · Cross":"马步 · 弓步 · 虚步 · 仆步 · 歇步","Weight split, this stance (front / back)":"目前步型重心分配（前 / 后）","Varies by school — common training values":"不同门派略有差异，此为常见训练值","Suggested hold for beginners":"初学者建议站桩时间","3 sets per stance, building to 1–2 min":"每式 3 组，逐步加到 1–2 分钟","Stances you have mastered":"步型掌握进度","Mark each stance as mastered below":"可在下方标记为「已熟悉」","Choose your level (animation depth updates instantly)":"选择程度（动画深度即时改变）","Beginner · higher":"初学 · 站高一点","Standard · full depth":"标准 · 完整深度","Pick a stance (in traditional teaching order)":"选择步型检视细节（依传统教学顺序）","Weight (front / back)":"重心分配（前／后）","Foot distance":"脚距","Main benefit":"主要训练效果","How to stand":"动作要领","How to practise":"练习方法","Where it's used":"应用","FRONT 0°":"正面 0°","Foot placement & weight (top view)":"脚位与重心（俯视图）","↑ facing forward":"↑ 面向前方","What this stance trains":"此步型训练重点分布","For education only. Stance details vary between schools — follow your own teacher. Stop if you feel knee or hip pain and seek professional advice.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，各门派的步型细节略有不同，请以你的老师指导为准。练习时如膝盖或髋部疼痛，请立即停止并咨询专业人士。","5 Basic Kung Fu Stances: Horse, Bow, Empty, Drop & Cross — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"5种基本功夫步型：马步、弓步、虚步、仆步与交叉步——互动指南 | KungfuTutor","Learn the five basic kung fu stances — Ma Bu (horse), Gong Bu (bow), Xu Bu (empty), Pu Bu (drop) and Xie Bu (cross) — with animated front and side views, foot placement, weight distribution, common mistakes and a stance timer.":"学习五种基本功夫步型——Ma Bu（马步）、Gong Bu（弓步）、Xu Bu（虚步）、Pu Bu（仆步）和Xie Bu（交叉步）——包括动画正面与侧面视图、脚位、重心分配、常见错误以及步型计时器。","The 5 Basic Kung Fu Stances — Interactive Guide":"5种基本功夫步型——互动指南","What are the five basic kung fu stances?":"功夫的五大步型是哪五个？","Horse stance (Ma Bu), bow stance (Gong Bu), empty stance (Xu Bu), drop stance (Pu Bu) and cross stance (Xie Bu).":"马步（Ma Bu）、弓步（Gong Bu）、虚步（Xu Bu）、仆步（Pu Bu）和丁字步（Xie Bu）。","How long should a beginner hold horse stance?":"初学者马步要站多久？","Start with three sets of about 30 seconds with good form and build gradually towards two minutes. Stand higher rather than letting the knees cave in.":"从三组约30秒开始，动作姿势要正确，然后逐步增加到两分钟。站高一些，不要让膝盖内扣。","Is horse stance bad for your knees?":"马步对膝盖有害吗？","With knees tracking over the toes and a depth you can control, it is a common strength exercise. Pain is a signal to stand higher or stop and seek advice from an instructor or doctor.":"膝盖与脚尖方向一致，并且下蹲深度在自己可控制的范围内，这是一种常见的力量训练。疼痛是一个信号，代表应该站高一点，或停止并向教练或医生请教。","Horse Stance":"马步","about 3 foot lengths, parallel":"约 3 脚长，平行","Thigh and hip endurance":"大腿与臀部肌耐力","THIGHS NEAR LEVEL · KNEES OVER TOES":"大腿接近水平 · 膝盖对脚尖","Feet parallel about three foot lengths apart, toes forward. Bend the knees and sink until the thighs are close to level, pressing the knees out over the toes. Keep the back upright, chin tucked, shoulders relaxed and fists at the waist. Weight sits evenly between both feet.":"两脚平行分开约三个脚掌长，脚尖朝前。屈膝下蹲，大腿接近水平，膝盖向外撑、对准脚尖方向。上身挺直、收下巴、沉肩，双拳抱于腰侧。重心平均落在两脚之间。","Knees caving inward; leaning forward and sticking the hips out; toes turned out; holding the breath or shrugging. Beginners should stand higher rather than give up good form.":"膝盖内扣（膝盖往中间倒）；上身前倾、翘臀；脚尖外八；憋气耸肩。初学者宁可站高一点，也不要牺牲姿势。","Start with 3 × 30 seconds a day and build to 2 minutes. Breathe naturally and check knee direction in a mirror.":"每天从 3 × 30 秒开始，逐步增加到 2 分钟。保持自然呼吸，可以对着镜子检查膝盖的方向。","Almost every kung fu style builds on the horse stance: it trains leg strength and a stable base, and it is the starting point for punches and blocks.":"马步是几乎所有功夫流派的基础：练腿力、稳定下盘，也是冲拳、架打等动作的起点。","Bow Stance":"弓步","about 4–5 foot lengths long":"长约 4–5 脚长","Front-leg support and back-leg drive":"前腿支撑与后腿蹬地力","FRONT KNEE OVER ANKLE · BACK LEG STRAIGHT":"前膝不超过脚踝 · 后腿伸直","Step forward about four to five foot lengths with the front toes turned in slightly. Bend the front knee until the thigh is near level, with the knee above the instep. Straighten the back leg and press it into the floor, back foot turned in to point about 45° forward, and flat. Keep the torso upright and facing forward.":"向前跨出约四到五个脚长，前脚尖朝前或微向内扣；屈前膝，大腿接近水平，膝盖垂直于脚背上方。后腿伸直蹬地，后脚尖向内扣、斜向前约 45°，全脚掌着地。上身正直、面向前方。","Front knee past the toes; back heel lifting or back knee bending; both feet on one line like a tightrope, which kills balance; leaning the torso forward.":"前膝超过脚尖；后脚跟离地或后膝弯曲；两脚站在同一直线上，像走钢索一样不稳；上身前倾。","Hold each side for 30–60 seconds, then add the bow-stance punch: drive the back leg straight and turn the waist as you punch.":"左右式各站 30–60 秒；之后练习弓步冲拳：出拳时后腿蹬直、转腰送拳。","The bow stance is the classic attacking stance: it sends bodyweight forward behind punches and palm strikes.":"弓步是最常见的进攻步型，让身体重量往前推送，配合冲拳、推掌使用。","Empty Stance (Cat Stance)":"虚步","about 1–1.5 foot lengths":"前后约 1–1.5 脚长","Single-leg strength and balance":"单腿支撑力与平衡","FRONT FOOT: TOES ONLY, NO WEIGHT":"前脚只用脚尖轻点地","Turn the back foot out about 45°, bend the knee and put almost all your weight on the back leg. Place the front foot about one foot length ahead, knee slightly bent, touching down lightly with the ball or toes, heel raised. Keep the body upright — don't sit back and lean.":"后脚尖斜向外约 45°，屈膝下蹲，几乎全部体重放在后腿。前脚向前约一个脚长，膝盖微屈，只用前脚掌或脚尖轻点地面，脚跟提起。上身正直，不要往后坐倒。","Sneaking weight onto the front foot (you should be able to lift it any time); support knee caving in; leaning back; reaching the front foot too far so it becomes a bow stance.":"重心偷偷放到前脚（前脚应能随时提起）；支撑腿膝盖内扣；身体后仰；前脚伸太远变成弓步。","Start with a hand on a wall, 20–30 seconds each side. Test: lift the front foot — if your body doesn't move, your weight was right.":"先扶墙练习，每边 20–30 秒；可测试：站好后把前脚提起，身体不晃就是正确。","Keeping the front leg \"empty\" lets you kick or change step instantly; it appears in both northern and southern styles as a guard and kicking set-up.":"前脚保持「空着」，可以随时踢腿或转换步法，常见于南北各派的防守与起腿准备。","Drop Stance":"仆步","about 4–5 foot lengths wide":"左右约 4–5 脚长","Hip flexibility and bent-leg strength":"髋部柔韧性与屈腿力量","BOTH FEET FLAT · STRAIGHT-LEG TOES TURNED IN":"两脚全脚掌着地 · 伸直腿脚尖内扣","Spread the feet wide to the sides. Sink fully into one leg, hips near that heel, knee tracking the toes. Stretch the other leg straight along the floor with the toes turned in. Keep both feet flat and the chest as upright as you can — don't fold forward.":"两脚左右大幅分开。一腿全蹲，臀部接近脚跟，膝盖与脚尖同方向；另一腿向侧伸直贴近地面，脚尖内扣。两脚全脚掌着地，上身尽量正直，不要弯腰低头。","Heel or outer edge of the straight-leg foot lifting; the bent-leg heel coming up; rounding the back; forcing depth until the knee hurts — stay higher until your flexibility allows.":"伸直腿的脚跟或脚掌外侧离地；屈腿脚跟抬起；弯腰低头；勉强压低造成膝盖疼痛——柔软度不够时先站高一点。","Warm up the hips and inner thighs first; hold 20–30 seconds each side, or shift slowly from side to side.":"先做髋与内收肌伸展；左右换边各 20–30 秒，或左右慢慢移动重心来回转换。","The drop stance is used for low evasions and threading-palm techniques, and is excellent hip-mobility training.":"仆步常用于低身闪躲与穿掌等动作，也是很好的髋部柔软度训练。","Cross Stance (Resting Stance)":"歇步","legs crossed, back foot behind the front foot":"两腿交叉，后脚在前脚斜后方","Low balance and hip rotation":"低位平衡与髋部旋转","FRONT FOOT TURNED OUT · BACK HEEL UP":"前脚外展全脚着地 · 后脚跟提起","Cross the legs and sink: the front foot turns out and stays flat; the back foot sits diagonally behind it on the ball of the foot with the heel raised, back knee tucked close against the outside of the front calf. Sit down towards the back calf and keep the chest upright, slightly forward.":"两腿交叉下蹲：前脚脚尖外展、全脚掌着地；后脚在前脚斜后方，以前脚掌着地、脚跟提起，后膝贴近前腿小腿外侧。臀部坐在后腿小腿附近，上身挺直、略向前。","Leaving a gap between the legs; not turning the front foot out so the knee twists; tilting or rounding the body; forcing the sit and straining the knee.":"两腿没有夹紧、中间留空；前脚没有外展导致膝盖扭转；身体歪斜或弯腰；蹲不下去就硬坐，伤到膝盖。","Hold onto support at first, 15–30 seconds each side; later practise flowing from bow stance into cross stance.":"先扶物练习，每边 15–30 秒；熟练后练习由弓步转歇步的转换。","The cross stance appears in turns, low counters after evasions, and as a finishing posture in forms.":"歇步常用于转身、闪避后的低位反击，也常见于套路的收势与定势。","Foundation stance: your root":"基础步型：下盘根基","Static hold · leg strength":"静态站桩 · 腿力","Foundation stance: bend front, drive back":"基础步型：前弓后蹬","Attacking stance · forward drive":"进攻步型 · 推送力量","Foundation stance: empty vs full":"基础步型：虚实分明","Balance · quick change":"平衡 · 灵活转换","Foundation stance: low and long":"基础步型：低身伸展","Flexibility · low transitions":"柔韧度 · 低位转换","Foundation stance: crossed and seated":"基础步型：交叉坐盘","Turning · low stability":"转身 · 低位稳定","FRONT VIEW":"正面视角","KNEE":"膝角","Inner thighs":"内收肌","FRONT KNEE":"前膝","BACK KNEE":"后膝","Quads (front leg)":"股四头肌（前腿）","Calf stretch (back leg)":"小腿伸展（后腿）","SUPPORT KNEE":"支撑膝","Quads (support leg)":"股四头肌（支撑腿）","Ankle stability":"踝关节稳定","Inner-thigh stretch":"内收肌伸展","Quads (bent leg)":"股四头肌（屈腿）","Ankle mobility":"踝关节柔韧度","Hip rotation / mobility":"髋部旋转／柔韧","Knee & ankle control":"膝踝控制","FRONT":"前","Beginner":"初学","Weight ":"重心","Stance {n} of 5 · Pinyin {py}":"第 {n} 式 · 拼音 {py}","Why learn stances first?":"为什么要先练步型？","An old kung fu saying tells beginners to \"stand in stance for three years\". Power starts at the ground and travels through the legs and waist to the hands and feet — without a stable base, even fast techniques lack force. The five stances are the foundation of Changquan and most northern styles, and the building blocks of forms such as Wu Bu Quan (Five Stance Fist).":"功夫有句老话：「入门先站三年桩」。拳脚的力量来自地面，经过腿、腰再传到手脚；如果下盘不稳，动作再快也没有力。五大步型是长拳与多数北派功夫的基本功，也是套路（例如五步拳）的组成单位。","The five stances at a glance":"五大步型一览","Weight splits and distances are common training values; northern, southern and individual schools differ — follow your own teacher.":"重心比例与脚距是常见的训练参考值；南派、北派及各家门派的要求不完全相同，请以你的老师指导为准。","Three rules for safe practice":"安全练习的三个原则","Knees always track the direction of the toes — never cave in or twist.":"膝盖永远对准脚尖方向，不要内扣或扭转。","Choose a depth you can control: correct shape matters more than going low.":"深度依能力调整：姿势正确比蹲得低更重要。","Warm up hips, knees and ankles first; stop if anything hurts.":"先热身髋、膝、踝；疼痛就停，不要硬撑。","Horse (Ma Bu), bow (Gong Bu), empty (Xu Bu), drop (Pu Bu) and cross (Xie Bu).":"马步、弓步、虚步、仆步、歇步。","Start with about 30 seconds × 3 sets with good form, then build slowly towards 1–2 minutes.":"建议从每组约 30 秒、做 3 组开始，姿势正确后再慢慢延长到 1–2 分钟。","Is horse stance bad for the knees?":"站马步会伤膝盖吗？","With knees over the toes and a depth you control, it is a common strength exercise. If it hurts, stand higher or stop, and ask an instructor or doctor.":"只要膝盖对准脚尖、深度在可控制范围内，马步是常见的力量训练；如出现疼痛，请站高一点或停止，并请教教练或医师。","Who made these animations?":"这些动画是谁做的？","They are drawn by KungfuTutor to show the key points, not an official demonstration of any particular school.":"动画由 KungfuTutor 自行绘制，用来说明姿势重点，并非任何门派的官方示范。","Beginner (low kicks)":"初学（低踢）","Standard height":"标准高度","Strikes with: ":"力点：","Technique {n} of 6 · {type} · Pinyin {py}":"第 {n} 式 · {type} · 拼音 {py}","First, make a proper fist":"先学会握拳","Roll the four fingers tightly into the palm and fold the thumb across the middle sections of the index and middle fingers — never tuck it inside. Keep the wrist straight so the knuckles line up with the forearm; a bent wrist is the most common beginner injury.":"四指并拢用力卷入掌心，拇指横扣在食指与中指的第二节上，不要包在四指里面。手腕要直，让拳面与前臂成一直线——手腕弯曲是初学者最常见的受伤原因。","The six techniques at a glance":"六个技巧一览","Striking point":"力点","Height":"高度","Bend-and-extend kicks vs straight-leg swings":"屈伸性腿法 vs 直摆性腿法","The snap kick, heel thrust and side kick are bend-and-extend kicks: chamber the knee, then extend to strike — the line and striking point are what matter. The front stretch kick is a straight-leg swing: the leg stays straight all the way up, building flexibility and hip strength for higher kicks later.":"弹腿、蹬腿、侧踹属于「屈伸性腿法」：先提膝，再把腿伸出击打，重点是路线与力点。正踢腿属于「直摆性腿法」：腿全程伸直往上摆，主要用来练柔软度与髋部力量，是学高踢腿的基础。","Warm up hips, knees, ankles and shoulders; never swing hard kicks when cold.":"先热身髋、膝、踝与肩，身体未热时不要用力甩腿。","Don't snap joints into a hard lock — keep a little give and control the return.":"出拳出腿时不要把关节猛力锁死，保留一点弯度，并控制收回的动作。","Use pads and train under an instructor when hitting targets or working with a partner.":"对靶或与人练习时，请使用护具，并在教练指导下进行。","New to stances? Start with <a href=\"../stances/\">the five basic stances</a> — the punch and palm strike are both done in bow stance.":"还没练过步型？建议先看 <a href=\"../stances/\">功夫五大步型</a>，冲拳与推掌都是在弓步上完成的。","Snap kick vs heel thrust — what's the difference?":"弹腿和蹬腿有什么不同？","The snap kick points the toes and whips the lower leg out, striking with the tip of the foot; the heel thrust pulls the toes back and pushes the heel out in a straight line.":"弹腿脚面绷直、小腿快速弹出，用脚尖击打；蹬腿脚尖勾起，把脚跟沿直线推出，用脚跟击打。","Why does the fist turn palm-down?":"出拳时拳心为什么要转向下？","Starting palm-up at the waist and finishing palm-down lines the knuckles up with the target and locks the arm into a strong structure — the standard Changquan punch.":"从腰间拳心向上出发、到终点转成拳心向下，可以让拳面对准目标、手臂结构更稳固，也是长拳冲拳的标准要求。","What if I can't kick high?":"踢不高怎么办？","Use the Beginner (low kicks) level and get the line and balance right first; daily front stretch kicks and hamstring stretches will raise your height over time.":"先选择“初学 · 低踢”程度，把路线和平衡做对；每天做正踢腿与腿后肌伸展，高度会慢慢增加。","Punches & Kicks":"拳法与腿法","KUNG FU FOUNDATIONS · BASIC HAND AND LEG TECHNIQUES":"传统功夫基本功 · 基本手法与腿法","Kung Fu Punches & Kicks: 6 Essential Techniques, Step by Step":"功夫基本拳法与腿法：6 个入门技巧互动解析","Two hand techniques and four kicks — the first lessons of Changquan and most northern styles. Each move is broken into steps: click a step to freeze on it, follow the green trail to see the path of the fist or foot, and watch the red dot for the striking point.":"两种手法、四种腿法，是长拳与多数北派功夫的入门课。每个动作都拆成步骤：点选步骤即可定格查看，绿色轨迹显示拳脚的运动路线，红点标示力点。","Basic techniques":"基本技巧","2 hand techniques · 4 kicks":"2 手法 · 4 腿法","Striking point, this technique":"目前技巧力点","Suggested practice":"建议练习量","10 slow reps × 3 sets per side, then speed up":"每边慢动作 10 次 × 3 组，再加快","Choose your level (kick height updates instantly)":"选择程度（腿法高度即时改变）","Beginner · low kicks":"初学 · 低踢","Pick a technique (hands first, then kicks)":"选择技巧查看细节（先手法、后腿法）","Target height":"攻击高度","For education only. Details vary between schools — follow your own teacher. Warm up first; when practising with a partner, use pads and train under a qualified instructor.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，各门派细节略有不同，请以你的老师指导为准。练习前请充分热身；与他人练习时请使用护具并在合格教练指导下进行。","Basic Kung Fu Punches & Kicks: 6 Essential Techniques — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"功夫基础拳法与腿法：6 项必学技术——互动指南 | KungfuTutor","Learn six basic kung fu techniques — straight punch, palm strike, snap kick, heel thrust kick, side kick and front stretch kick — with step-by-step animation, striking points, common mistakes and practice tips.":"学习六种基础功夫技术——直拳、掌击、弹踢、蹬踢、侧踢和前伸踢——配有分步动画、击打部位、常见错误和练习建议。","Kung Fu Punches & Kicks — Interactive Step-by-Step Guide":"功夫拳法与腿法——互动分步指南","What is the difference between a snap kick and a heel thrust kick?":"弹踢和蹬踢有什么区别？","A snap kick (Tan Tui) whips the lower leg out from a lifted knee with the toes pointed and strikes with the tip of the foot. A heel thrust kick (Deng Tui) pulls the toes back and pushes the heel out in a straight line.":"弹踢（弹腿）从提起的膝盖处将小腿甩出，脚尖绷直，用脚尖端击打。蹬踢（蹬腿）将脚趾勾回，沿直线把脚跟推出。","How do you make a correct kung fu fist?":"怎样做出正确的功夫拳？","Curl the four fingers tightly into the palm and fold the thumb across the middle of the index and middle fingers. Keep the wrist straight so the knuckles and forearm form one line.":"四指紧紧卷入掌心，拇指横扣在食指和中指的中段。手腕保持挺直，使指节与前臂成一条直线。","Should I warm up before practising kicks?":"练习腿法前需要热身吗？","Yes. Warm up the hips, knees and ankles and do light stretches first; never swing kicks hard when cold.":"需要。先热身髋、膝和踝关节，并做轻度拉伸；身体冷的时候切勿用力甩腿。","Straight Punch":"直拳","Knuckles (fist face)":"拳面","Chest to shoulder height":"胸口至肩高","Waist rotation and straight-line arm drive":"腰胯转动与手臂直线出力","STRAIGHT LINE · SHOULDER DOWN · ELBOW IN":"拳走直线 · 肩不耸 · 肘不外翻","Set a bow stance with both fists at the waist, palms up. Push off the back leg, turn the waist and let the shoulder follow as the fist drives straight out from the waist, twisting palm-down on the way. Power lands on the knuckles as the arm straightens; the other fist stays at the waist. Return along the same line.":"弓步站稳，双拳抱于腰侧、拳心向上。出拳时后腿蹬地、转腰顺肩，拳从腰间沿直线向前冲出，途中旋转成拳心向下，手臂伸直时力量集中在拳面。另一拳保持在腰间。出完拳沿原路收回。","Arm-only punching with no waist turn; shrugging or flaring the elbow; a curved path; a bent wrist (an injury risk); leaning forward and losing the stance.":"只用手臂、没有转腰；耸肩或肘部向外翻；拳头走弧线；手腕弯曲（容易受伤）；出拳时身体前倾、重心跑掉。","Do 10 slow reps to check the line and the twist, then 20 alternating reps each side. Use a mirror to check the fist stays level with the shoulder.":"先慢动作做 10 次，确认路线与拳心旋转；再左右交替各 20 次。可对镜检查拳是否在肩高直线上。","The straight punch is the most basic strike and the first lesson in \"power from the ground, through the waist, into the hand\".":"直拳是最基本的攻击动作，也是理解「力从地起、经腰传到手」的入门练习。","Palm Strike":"掌击","Palm":"掌法","Heel of the palm":"掌根","Chest to chin height":"胸口至下巴高","Pushing power and wrist structure":"推送力量与手腕结构","WRIST BENT BACK · FINGERS UP · HEEL OF PALM":"坐腕 · 指朝上 · 力达掌根","From a bow stance with fists at the waist, open one hand and push it forward from the waist. As it travels, bend the wrist back so the fingers point up and the palm faces forward. Drive from the back leg and waist so the force lands on the heel of the palm, then close the hand and return to the waist.":"弓步站稳，双拳抱腰。出手时拳变掌，由腰间向前推出，同时坐腕（手腕向后弯）、手指向上成立掌，掌心向前。后腿蹬地、转腰，让力量集中到掌根。完成后变拳收回腰间。","Not bending the wrist back so the fingers do the pushing; locking the elbow hard; shrugging; pushing with the arm without turning the waist.":"手腕没有坐起、用手指推；手肘锁死；耸肩；只推手不转腰。","20 alternating reps each side; push against a wall or pad to feel force travel from the feet to the heel of the palm.":"左右交替各 20 次；可推墙或推靶，感受力量从脚传到掌根。","A palm strike is easier on the hand than a fist; self-defence courses often use it to push an attacker away and create space to escape.":"推掌比拳头更不易伤手，自我防卫教学中常用于推开对方、制造距离以便离开。","Front Snap Kick":"弹腿","Kick (bend & extend)":"腿法（屈伸）","Tip of the foot (toes pointed)":"脚尖（脚面绷直）","Knee to waist height":"膝至腰高","Quad snap and one-leg balance":"股四头肌爆发与单脚平衡","KNEE FIRST · TOES POINTED · SNAP AND RECOIL":"先提膝 · 脚面绷直 · 快弹快收","Stand with feet together, fists at the waist. Keep the support leg firm. Lift the kicking knee until the thigh is near level, then snap the lower leg out from the knee with the toes pointed, power to the tip of the foot. Recoil straight back to the knee lift before putting the foot down.":"并步站立、双拳抱腰。支撑腿站稳微直，踢腿先提膝到大腿接近水平，接着小腿以膝为轴迅速向前弹出，脚面绷直，力量集中到脚尖。弹出后立即收回成提膝，再落地。","Swinging the leg without lifting the knee; snapping the knee into a hard lock (hard on the joint); toes not pointed; leaning far back; slow recoil.":"没有提膝、直接甩腿；弹出时膝盖锁死（伤膝）；脚尖没有绷直；上身后仰太多；收腿太慢。","With a hand on a wall: lift → snap → recoil, 15 per leg. Then practise without support, alternating legs while stepping forward.":"扶墙练习提膝 → 弹出 → 收回，每腿 15 次；熟练后离开墙，左右交替行进练习。","The snap kick is the root of Changquan kicking and gives the Tan Tui forms their name; a low snap kick is fast and compact.":"弹腿是长拳腿法的基础，也是「弹腿」系列套路的名称由来；低弹腿速度快、动作小。","Heel Thrust Kick":"蹬腿","Heel":"脚跟","Waist to chest height":"腰至胸高","Hip & leg thrust, core stability":"臀腿推蹬力与核心稳定","TOES PULLED BACK · POWER TO THE HEEL":"脚尖勾起 · 力达脚跟","From feet together, lift the kicking knee high with the toes pulled back. Extend hip and knee to drive the heel forward in a straight line until the leg is straight, power on the heel. Keep the chest upright, leaning back only slightly, then bend the knee back in and set the foot down.":"并步站立。踢腿屈膝高提，脚尖勾起；接着以髋、膝伸展的力量把脚跟向前直线蹬出，腿伸直，力量集中在脚跟。上身保持正直、略向后，蹬完屈膝收回再落地。","Pointing the toes so it becomes a snap kick; low knee lift so the foot scoops upward; leaning far back; support heel lifting.":"脚尖绷直变成弹腿；提膝不够高，脚往上撩；身体过度后仰；支撑脚跟离地。","Push slowly into a kick shield or thick pad, 10–15 per leg; the key is knee up first, then a straight thrust.":"对着踢靶或厚垫慢慢推蹬，每腿 10–15 次；重点是先提膝再直线蹬出。","The heel thrust pushes distance open, much like the Muay Thai teep; in self-defence it can push away someone closing in so you can leave.":"蹬腿是推开距离的腿法，和泰拳前蹬（Teep）原理相近，在自我防卫中可用来推开逼近的人以便离开。","Side Kick":"侧踹","Heel & outer edge of the foot":"脚跟、脚掌外沿","Waist to shoulder height":"腰至肩高","Hip abductor strength and flexibility":"髋外展力量与柔软度","CHAMBER · OPEN THE HIP · HEEL LEADS":"先提膝 · 展髋 · 脚跟领先","Stand side-on, eyes towards the target. Chamber the kicking knee with the foot turned in; pivot the support foot, open the hip and drive the leg out sideways in a straight line, letting the body tilt the other way for balance. Power lands on the heel and the outer edge of the foot. Re-chamber, then set the foot down.":"侧身站立，目视踢击方向。踢腿屈膝提起，脚掌内扣；支撑脚转动、展开髋部，把腿向侧方直线踹出，上身自然向反方向侧倾保持平衡，力量集中于脚跟与脚掌外沿。踹出后收回提膝，再落地。","Not pivoting the support foot (strains the knee); kicking with the toes; staying upright so the leg can't extend; dropping the leg without re-chambering.":"没有转动支撑脚，造成膝盖扭伤风险；用脚尖踢；身体不倒、腿踢不直；踢完直接放腿没有收回。","Holding a chair back, do slow side kicks, 10 per leg, through the three phases chamber–extend–re-chamber; add hip stretches.":"扶椅背做慢速侧踹，每腿 10 次，练习提膝、展髋、收回三个阶段；配合髋部伸展。","The side kick is among the longest-range, most concentrated kicks, with close relatives in Taekwondo and Karate.":"侧踹是攻击距离最远、力量最集中的腿法之一，在长拳、跆拳道、空手道中都可以看到相近的动作。","Front Stretch Kick":"正踢腿","Kick (straight-leg swing)":"腿法（直摆）","— (flexibility drill)":"—（柔韧训练）","Goal: toes towards the forehead":"目标：脚尖接近前额","Hamstring flexibility and hip-flexor strength":"腿后肌柔韧度与髋屈肌力量","BOTH LEGS STRAIGHT · TOES BACK · CHEST UP":"两腿伸直 · 勾脚尖 · 上身正直","Stand with feet together, hands on hips or arms out to the sides. Keep the support leg straight; swing the kicking leg up straight with the toes pulled back, aiming towards the forehead, then lower it under control. Alternate legs as you walk forward.":"并步站立，双手叉腰或两臂侧平举。支撑腿伸直站稳，踢腿伸直、勾起脚尖，由下向前额方向快速踢起，再有控制地落下。左右腿交替，边走边踢。","Bending the kicking leg; bending forward to fake the height; support heel lifting or knee bending; slamming the leg down and straining the hamstring.":"踢起腿弯曲；为了踢高而弯腰低头；支撑脚跟离地或膝盖弯曲；用力甩下造成拉伤。","Only after a warm-up, 10–20 per leg. Height will come — straight legs and posture matter more. Pair it with daily hamstring stretching.":"热身后再练，每腿 10–20 次。高度不够没关系，伸直和姿势比高度更重要；配合每日腿后肌伸展。","The front stretch kick opens almost every kung fu class as a warm-up and flexibility drill, laying the groundwork for high kicks.":"正踢腿是几乎所有功夫课开头的热身与柔韧训练，为高踢腿打下基础。","Basic hand technique: straight line":"基本拳法：直线出击","Bow-stance punch · waist power":"弓步冲拳 · 转腰发力","Basic palm technique: upright palm":"基本掌法：立掌推出","Bow-stance palm · wrist bent back":"弓步推掌 · 坐腕","Basic kick: bend-and-extend":"基本腿法：屈伸性腿法","Knee lift · snap · fast recoil":"提膝弹击 · 快速收回","Basic kick: toes back, heel out":"基本腿法：勾脚蹬出","Thrusting power · creates distance":"推蹬力量 · 制造距离","Basic kick: open-hip side thrust":"基本腿法：展髋侧踹","Longest-range kick":"最远距离的腿法","Basic kick: straight-leg swing":"基本腿法：直摆性腿法","Flexibility · essential warm-up":"柔韧度 · 热身必练","Bow stance set, fists at the waist":"弓步站稳，双拳抱于腰间","Open the hand and drive it forward from the waist — power to the heel of the palm":"拳变掌，由腰间向前推出，力达掌根","Wrist bent back, fingers up; then return to the waist":"坐腕立掌，再收回腰间","Turn the waist and shoulder; the fist twists palm-down and lands on the knuckles":"转腰顺肩，拳旋转冲出，力达拳面","Pull straight back to the waist along the same line":"沿原路收回腰间","Stand with feet together, fists at the waist":"并步站立，双拳抱腰","Lift the knee until the thigh is level":"提膝，大腿抬平","Snap the lower leg out, toes pointed — power to the tip of the foot":"小腿向前弹出，脚面绷直，力达脚尖","Snap straight back to the knee lift":"迅速弹回成提膝","Lift the knee high and pull the toes back":"屈膝高提，脚尖勾起","Thrust the heel forward until the leg is straight — power to the heel":"脚跟向前蹬出，腿伸直，力达脚跟","Bend and recover the knee, stay balanced":"屈膝收回，保持平衡","Stand side-on, eyes on the target":"侧身站立，目视前方","Chamber: lift the knee, foot turned in":"屈膝提起，脚掌向内扣","Open the hip and drive the leg out sideways, body leaning away — power to the heel and outer edge":"展胯向侧踹出，上身侧倒，力达脚跟及脚掌外沿","Re-chamber the knee, then set the foot down":"收腿回提膝，再落地","Feet together, hands on hips or arms out to the sides":"并步站立，双手叉腰或侧平举","Kick straight up towards the forehead, leg straight, toes pulled back":"腿伸直、勾脚尖，向前额方向踢起","Support leg straight, chest upright — lower the leg under control":"支撑腿伸直，上身正直，控制落下","STRIKING POINT: ":"力点：","Waist rotation":"腰胯转动","Shoulder & arm drive":"肩臂前推","Stance stability":"下盘稳定","Wrist alignment":"手腕稳定","Pushing power":"推送力量","Wrist structure":"手腕结构","Quad snap":"股四头肌爆发","Hip flexors":"髋屈肌","Knee control":"膝关节控制","Glute thrust":"臀大肌推蹬","Hip abductors":"髋外展力量","Hip flexibility":"髋部柔软度","Lateral core":"核心侧向稳定","Hamstring flexibility":"腿后肌柔软度","Hip-flexor strength":"髋屈肌力量","Support balance":"支撑平衡","Core control":"核心控制","Current pace: ":"目前速度：","Beginner (slower)":"初学慢速","Posture {n} of 24 · {group} · Pinyin {py}":"第 {n} 式 · {group} · 拼音 {py}","Where the 24-form comes from":"24 式太极拳的由来","In 1956 China's national sports commission took traditional Yang-style Tai Chi, removed the repetitions and arranged 24 postures from simple to harder — the \"simplified Tai Chi\" form. Because it is short and easy to start, it became the most widely practised Tai Chi routine in the world and a standard for competitions and morning practice in parks.":"1956年，中国国家体育运动委员会以传统杨式太极拳为基础，删去重复动作、整理出由简到难的24个动作，称为“简化太极拳”。因为容易学、时间短，它成为全世界最普及的太极拳套路，也是许多比赛与晨练的标准套路。","All 24 postures":"全部 24 式一览","Name":"名称","Pinyin":"拼音","Group":"组别","English names vary between books and teachers; these are common versions.":"英文名称有多种常见译法，此处采用常见版本。","Learn one group (3–4 postures) at a time before adding the next.":"一次学一组（3–4 式），熟练后再接下一组。","Move slowly and evenly, keeping the same pace throughout.":"动作慢而均匀，速度从头到尾保持一致。","Breathe naturally — usually in as you open, rise or draw in, out as you close, sink or push. Never hold your breath.":"呼吸自然：一般开、起、收时吸气，合、落、推时呼气；不要憋气。","Keep the knees in line with the toes, and only move a foot after the weight has fully shifted off it.":"膝盖对准脚尖，重心转移完成后再移动另一脚。","Health benefits":"太极拳对健康的益处","Research reviews suggest Tai Chi may help older adults improve balance and lower their risk of falls, and may help flexibility, mood and sleep. It is low-to-moderate intensity and suits most ages; if you have heart, joint or balance problems, check with your doctor first.":"多项研究整理显示，太极拳可能有助于改善长者的平衡、降低跌倒风险，并对柔软度、心情与睡眠有帮助。它属于低至中强度运动，适合大多数年龄层；如有心血管、关节或平衡方面的问题，请先咨询医师。","Want stronger foundations first? See <a href=\"../stances/\">the five basic stances</a> — bow, empty and drop stance all appear in the 24-form.":"想先打好下盘基础？可以看 <a href=\"../stances/\">功夫五大步型</a>，弓步、虚步、仆步都会在 24 式中用到。","How long does the whole form take?":"打完 24 式需要多久？","Usually about 4–6 minutes; slower practice can take longer.":"一般约 4–6 分钟，慢练可以更长。","How long does it take to learn?":"学会需要多长时间？","With regular practice many people learn the order in a few weeks to a few months; polishing it takes much longer.":"规律练习的话，很多人几周到几个月可以记住顺序；动作要练得纯熟需要更长时间。","Why do some postures have left and right versions?":"为什么有些动作有“左右”两式？","Postures such as Wild Horse's Mane, Brush Knee, Repulse Monkey, Cloud Hands and the Shuttles repeat on alternate sides. The animation shows one side — use the Left/Right button for the other.":"野马分鬃、搂膝拗步、倒卷肱、云手、穿梭等动作会左右交替重复。动画显示一侧，请用“左式／右式”按钮看另一侧。","Can these animations replace a teacher?":"这些动画可以取代老师吗？","No. They are simplified flat illustrations to help you remember the order and key points; turning directions, hand details and internal energy are best learned from a qualified teacher.":"不能。动画是简化的平面示意，方便记忆顺序与要点；转身方向、细部手形与劲力仍建议跟合格老师学习。","Tai Chi 24-Form":"24 式太极拳","INTERNAL ART · SIMPLIFIED YANG-STYLE TAI CHI · CREATED 1956":"内家拳 · 简化太极拳（杨式）· 1956 年编定","Tai Chi 24-Form: Every Posture, Animated with a Breathing Cue":"24 式太极拳互动解析：逐式动画与呼吸提示","The 24-form is the most widely practised Tai Chi sequence in the world and takes about 4–6 minutes. Pick any posture to see it broken into steps; the circle in the top corner swells and shrinks with the in-breath and out-breath. Switch on Play the whole form to follow along from start to finish.":"24 式太极拳是全世界最多人练习的太极套路，约 4–6 分钟可以打完。点选任一式看分解动作；左上角的圆圈会随“吸气／呼气”胀缩，帮你配合呼吸。开启“连续播放全套”即可从头跟练到尾。","Postures in the form":"套路动作","In 8 groups, performed in one flowing sequence":"分为 8 组，依顺序连贯完成","Current posture":"目前动作","Time for the whole form":"全套时间","Slow and even beats fast":"越慢越均匀越好，不求快","Postures you have mastered":"动作掌握进度","Mark each posture as mastered below":"可在下方标记为“已熟悉”","Pace and playback":"速度与播放方式","Beginner · slower":"初学 · 慢速","Standard pace":"标准速度","▶ Play the whole form (auto-advance)":"▶ 连续播放全套（自动换下一式）","Pick a posture (in form order)":"选择动作（依套路顺序）","Name & imagery":"名称意象","What this posture trains":"此动作训练重点","For education only; the animations are simplified. Tai Chi is low-to-moderate intensity, but if you have heart, joint or balance problems, check with your doctor first and learn with a qualified teacher where possible.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，动画为简化示意。太极拳属低至中强度运动，但如有心血管、关节或平衡方面的问题，练习前请先咨询医师，并尽量在合格老师指导下学习。","Tai Chi 24-Form: All 24 Postures with Animation & Breathing Guide | KungfuTutor":"太极24式：全部24个动作配动画与呼吸指引 | KungfuTutor","Learn the simplified Tai Chi 24-form (Yang style) posture by posture: animated demos of all 24 movements, step-by-step breakdowns, a breathing cue, key points, common mistakes and a play-the-whole-form mode.":"逐式学习简化太极24式（杨式）：24个动作的动画示范、分步拆解、呼吸提示、要点、常见错误，以及整套连续练习模式。","Tai Chi 24-Form — All 24 Postures, Animated":"太极24式——全部24个动作动画演示","What is the Tai Chi 24-form?":"什么是太极24式？","A short sequence of 24 postures based on Yang-style Tai Chi, created in 1956 in China to make Tai Chi easier to learn. It usually takes about 4 to 6 minutes to perform.":"这是一套以杨式太极拳为基础的短套路，由24个动作组成，1956年在中国创编，目的是让太极拳更易学。完整演练通常需要约4至6分钟。","How long does it take to learn the 24-form?":"学会24式需要多久？","Many beginners learn the sequence in a few weeks to a few months of regular practice; refining it takes much longer. Learning one group of postures at a time helps.":"许多初学者经过数周到数月的定期练习即可学会整套动作；要练得精熟则需要更长时间。一次学习一组动作会有所帮助。","Is Tai Chi good for balance?":"太极拳有助于平衡能力吗？","Research reviews suggest Tai Chi may help improve balance and reduce fall risk in older adults. Check with a doctor if you have health concerns.":"研究综述显示，太极拳可能有助于改善老年人的平衡能力并降低跌倒风险。如有健康疑虑，请先咨询医生。","Commencing Form":"起势","Part the Wild Horse's Mane":"左右野马分鬃","White Crane Spreads Its Wings":"白鹤亮翅","Brush Knee and Push":"左右搂膝拗步","Play the Lute (Pipa)":"手挥琵琶","Repulse the Monkey":"左右倒卷肱","Grasp the Bird's Tail — Left":"左揽雀尾","Grasp the Bird's Tail — Right":"右揽雀尾","Single Whip":"单鞭","Cloud Hands":"云手","Single Whip (2)":"单鞭 (2)","High Pat on Horse":"高探马","Right Heel Kick":"右蹬脚","Strike the Ears with Both Fists":"双峰贯耳","Turn and Left Heel Kick":"转身左蹬脚","Lower Body and Stand on One Leg — Left":"左下势独立","Lower Body and Stand on One Leg — Right":"右下势独立","Fair Lady Works the Shuttles":"左右穿梭","Needle at the Sea Bottom":"海底针","Fan Through the Back":"闪通臂","Turn, Deflect, Parry and Punch":"转身搬拦捶","Apparent Close-Up":"如封似闭","Cross Hands":"十字手","Closing Form":"收势","Weight shifting":"重心转移","Relaxed breathing":"放松呼吸","Full vs empty weight":"虚实分明","Focus":"专注","Breath coordination":"呼吸配合","Upright posture":"姿势正直","Side-to-side shifting":"重心左右转移","Waist turning":"腰部转动","Backward balance":"后退平衡","Feet shoulder-width apart, arms hanging naturally":"两脚开立与肩同宽，两臂自然下垂","Slowly raise both arms forward to shoulder height":"两臂慢慢向前平举至肩高","Bend the knees and gently press the palms down in front of the belly":"屈膝下蹲，两掌轻轻下按至腹前","Shoulders and elbows sink; knees stay behind the toes":"沉肩坠肘，屈膝时膝不超过脚尖","Shrugging or raising the arms too high; sticking the hips out or caving the knees as you sink.":"耸肩、手臂举太高；下蹲时翘臀或膝盖内扣。","The opening: settle the mind and let the breath become natural.":"全套的开始：让身心安静、呼吸自然。","Hands \"hold a ball\" in front of the chest, weight on the back leg":"两手在胸前如抱球，重心在后腿","Step into a bow stance; the front hand parts up to eye level, the rear hand presses beside the hip":"上步成弓步，前手向前上方分出至眼高，后手按于胯旁","Parting hands and bowing the leg finish together; body upright":"分手与弓腿同时完成，上身正直","Feet on one line so you wobble; leaning forward; hands arriving before the legs.":"两脚踩在同一直线上而站不稳；身体前倾；手比脚先到。","The hands part like combing a galloping horse's mane; done three times, left and right.":"两手分开，像拨开奔马的鬃毛，左右式共做3次。","Follow-step half a step, hands holding the ball":"跟步半步，两手抱球","Sit back into an empty stance; the upper hand rises beside the forehead, the lower hand presses by the hip":"后坐成虚步，上手提至额前，下手按于胯旁","Front toes just touch; all the weight sits on the back leg":"前脚脚尖点地，重心全在后腿","Putting weight on the front foot; lifting the top hand too high and shrugging; puffing the chest.":"前脚承重；上手举得太高、耸肩；挺胸。","Like a white crane opening its wings — one hand up, one hand down.":"像白鹤展开双翼：一手向上、一手向下。","Turn the waist; one hand circles back by the ear, the other comes in front of the chest":"转腰，一手经耳旁屈收，另一手落于胸前","Step and bow; the lower hand brushes past the knee to the hip as the upper hand pushes forward":"上步弓腿，下手搂过膝前按于胯旁，上手向前推出","Push, bow and waist settle at the same moment":"推掌、弓腿、松腰同时到位","Shrugging and lunging as you push; brushing too far from the knee.":"推掌时耸肩、身体前冲；搂手离膝太远。","One hand brushes the knee while the other pushes; three times, left and right.":"一手搂过膝盖、一手前推，左右共3次。","Bring the back foot in half a step and shift the weight back":"后脚跟进半步，重心后移","Front heel touches down in an empty stance; the hands close as if holding a lute":"前脚跟着地成虚步，两手合抱如抱琵琶","Front hand at nose height, rear hand near the inside of the front elbow":"前手与鼻同高，后手在前手肘内侧","Weighting the front foot; hands too far apart or stiff.":"前脚承重；两手距离太远或太僵。","The shape of someone holding a pipa (Chinese lute), ready to play.":"姿势像怀抱琵琶（中国乐器）准备弹奏。","Turn the waist; the rear hand curls up past the ear":"转腰，后手经耳旁屈肘","Step back; the curled hand pushes forward as the front hand draws back to the waist":"退步，屈肘之手向前推出，前手收回腰旁","When stepping back, the toes land first, then the foot settles":"退步时脚尖先着地，再慢慢踏实","Stepping back too far; feet on one line; leaning back.":"退步太大失去平衡；两脚踩成一直线；身体后仰。","Retreating while pushing away, as if fending off a playful monkey; four times, left and right.":"一边后退、一边推开，像挡开调皮的猴子，左右共4次。","Ward off (peng): bow stance, forearm rounded across the chest":"掤：弓步，前臂横于胸前向前掤出","Roll back (lu): sit back as both hands draw down and back":"捋：重心后坐，两手向后下方捋回","Press (ji): one hand on the other wrist, press forward":"挤：两手相搭向前挤出","Push (an): sit back, draw the palms in, then push forward":"按：后坐收掌，再向前按出","Ward off, roll back, press and push flow without a break":"掤、捋、挤、按4个动作连贯不断","Sticking the hips out or dropping the head when sitting back; lunging on the push.":"后坐时翘臀、低头；前推时身体前冲。","Like gently holding a bird by its tail; it contains Tai Chi's four basic energies: peng, lu, ji, an.":"像轻轻握住小鸟的尾巴，包含太极拳4个基本劲：掤捋挤按。","Turn the body, turn the foot in, hands hold the ball":"转身扣脚，两手抱球","Ward off":"掤","Roll back":"捋","Press, then push":"挤、按","Same as the left side, mirrored (use the left/right button)":"与左揽雀尾相同，方向相反（请按「左右」切换）","Losing balance in the turn; not turning the foot in enough.":"转身时重心不稳、脚没有扣好。","The mirror image of Grasp the Bird's Tail — Left.":"左揽雀尾的对称动作。","Shift back; the rear hand forms a hook and extends behind":"重心后移，后手变勾手向侧后方伸出","Step and bow; the front hand turns and pushes forward":"上步弓腿，前手翻掌向前推出","Hook hand: fingertips together, wrist bent down; push at nose height":"勾手五指撮拢、腕向下；推掌与鼻同高","Arms locked in one stiff straight line; tilting the body.":"两臂成一直线太僵；上身倾斜。","One hand hooked like the tip of a whip, the other pushing — an open, extended posture.":"一手如鞭梢的勾手、一手推出，姿态舒展。","Weight shifts to one side; upper hand in front of the face, lower hand in front of the belly":"重心移向一侧，上手在脸前、下手在腹前","Turn the waist; the hands swap high and low, circling like clouds; side-step":"转腰，两手上下交换，如云般画圆；侧行步","The waist moves the hands; eyes follow the upper hand; toes forward as you side-step":"以腰带手，眼随上手，侧步时脚尖向前","Moving only the arms; bobbing up and down; feet too wide.":"只动手不转腰；侧步时起伏；两脚过宽。","The hands drift continuously like clouds across the sky; three times.":"两手像天上的云一样连绵不断地流动，共三次。","From cloud hands, the rear hand forms a hook":"云手结束，后手变勾","Step, bow and push — the same as posture 9":"上步弓腿推掌，与第 9 式相同","As in posture 9":"同第 9 式单鞭","As in posture 9.":"同第 9 式。","The second Single Whip, leading into the next group.":"第二次单鞭，连接下一组动作。","Bring the back foot in half a step; open the hook hand":"后脚跟半步，勾手变掌","Empty stance; the upper hand pushes forward past the ear, the lower hand rests palm-up by the belly":"成虚步，上手经耳旁向前推出，下手收至腹前掌心向上","Body upright; the pushing hand at eye level":"上身正直，推掌高与眼平","Weighting the front foot; leaning as you push.":"前脚承重；推掌时身体前倾。","Like leaning from the saddle to pat the horse.":"像在马上探身轻拍马背。","Cross the hands in front of the chest and lift the knee":"两手交叉合抱于胸前，提膝","Open the arms to the sides as the heel slowly presses out":"两手向两侧分开，同时以脚跟慢慢蹬出","Support leg slightly bent and steady; toes back; power in the heel":"支撑腿微屈站稳，脚尖勾起，力在脚跟","Bending forward to kick higher; a wobbly support leg; pointed toes.":"为了踢高而弯腰；支撑脚不稳；脚尖绷直。","Arms open, heel kick — a one-leg balance test.":"分手蹬脚，练习单脚平衡。","Draw the leg back to a knee lift; the hands settle above the knee":"收腿提膝，两手落于膝上","Step and bow; both fists circle in from the sides to meet in front at head height":"上步弓腿，两拳从两侧向前上方合击","Fists about a head-width apart; shoulders and elbows sink":"两拳相距约一头宽，沉肩垂肘","Shrugging, fists touching, leaning forward.":"耸肩、两拳碰在一起；身体前倾。","The two fists close in from both sides like twin peaks.":"两拳如双峰从两侧合击。","Turn around, cross the hands, lift the knee":"转身，两手交叉合抱，提膝","Open the arms and press out with the heel (left side — use the mirror button)":"分手并以脚跟蹬出（左式，按「左右」切换）","Settle after the turn before kicking":"转身后先站稳再蹬脚","Kicking before the turn has settled.":"转身未稳就急着蹬脚。","The mirror of the right heel kick, with a turn.":"右蹬脚的对称动作，加上转身。","One hand forms a hook as you sink":"一手变勾，屈膝下蹲","Lower body: drop stance, the front hand threads along the inside of the front leg":"下势：仆步，前手沿前腿内侧穿出","Stand on one leg: rise and lift the knee, elbow above it (\"golden rooster\")":"独立：起身提膝，手肘对膝（金鸡独立）","Both feet flat in the drop; support leg soft when standing on one leg":"仆步时两脚全脚掌着地；独立时支撑腿微屈","Folding forward in the drop; rising too fast and wobbling.":"下势时弯腰低头；起身太快摇晃。","Low then high: from the drop stance up into \"golden rooster stands on one leg\".":"先低后高：由下势转为「金鸡独立」。","Lower body (right side)":"下势（右式）","Stand on one leg":"独立","As the left side, mirrored":"与左式相同，方向相反","Forcing the depth — a higher drop stance is fine.":"柔软度不够时硬压——可以做高一点的下势。","Mirror of posture 16.":"左下势独立的对称动作。","Hold the ball, turn and step":"抱球，转腰上步","Bow stance; the upper hand turns to shield above the forehead as the lower hand pushes forward":"弓步，上手翻掌架于额前上方，下手向前推出","Shielding hand above and in front of the forehead; push at nose height":"架掌在额前斜上方，推掌与鼻同高","Shrugging on the shield; feet on one line.":"架掌时耸肩；两脚成一直线。","The hands go back and forth like a weaver's shuttle; once each side.":"两手来回像织布梭子穿梭，左右各一次。","Follow-step and shift back":"后脚跟进半步，重心后移","Empty stance; lean slightly forward as the fingers point down and forward":"成虚步，上身稍前倾，手指向前下方插下","When leaning, keep the head and back in one line":"前倾时头与背保持一直线","Dropping the head and rounding the back; weighting the front foot.":"低头弯背；前脚承重。","The fingers point down like a needle reaching the sea floor.":"手指向下，像把针插向海底。","Rise and bring both hands up in front of the chest":"起身，两手提至胸前","Step and bow; the front hand pushes, the rear hand braces above the head":"上步弓腿，前手推出，后手撑架于头侧上方","Arms open like a fan, spreading from the back":"两臂撑开如扇，力由背部展开","Push and bow not together; shrugging.":"推掌与弓腿不同时；耸肩。","The arms open like a fan from across the back.":"两臂如扇子从背部打开。","Turn around, fist in front of the belly (deflect)":"转身，握拳于腹前（搬）","Step and parry forward with the palm (parry)":"上步，掌向前拦（拦）","Bow and punch forward, the palm near the inside of the forearm (punch)":"弓步，拳向前打出，掌附于前臂内侧（捶）","Punch with the fist upright; don't force it":"出拳时拳眼向上，不要用力过猛","Shrugging and lunging on the punch.":"出拳耸肩、身体前冲。","Deflect, parry and punch blended into one movement.":"搬、攔、捶三個動作連成一氣。","Sit back; turn the palms and draw them to the chest":"后坐，两掌翻转收回胸前","Bow forward and push with both palms":"弓步，两掌向前推出","Don't lean back when sitting back, don't lunge on the push":"后坐时不要后仰，前推时不要前冲","Elbows flaring as the hands draw in; shrugging on the push.":"收掌时两肘外张；推掌时耸肩。","Like sealing a door shut — draw in, then push.":"像把门关上、封住：先收后推。","Turn and circle both hands out to the sides":"转身，两手向两侧画弧分开","Bring the feet to shoulder-width; the wrists cross in front of the chest":"收脚开立，两手在胸前交叉成十字","Arms rounded, wrists crossing in front of the chest":"两臂撑圆，交叉点在胸前","Arms squeezed too tight; shrugging.":"两臂夹得太紧；耸肩。","From cross hands, turn the palms down":"由十字手翻掌","Slowly lower the palms":"两掌慢慢下落","Arms by the sides, bring the feet together and stand naturally":"两臂垂于身侧，收脚并步，自然站立","Stand quietly for a moment before walking away":"动作结束后安静站立片刻再走动","Rushing the close.":"收势太快，匆忙结束。","The form ends where it began — calm and still.":"全套结束，回到起始的平静。","Group 1":"第一组","Group 2":"第二组","Group 3":"第三组","Group 4":"第四组","Group 5":"第五组","Group 6":"第六组","Group 7":"第七组","Group 8":"第八组","Bow stance":"弓步","Empty stance":"虚步","One-leg stance":"独立步","Drop → one leg":"仆步 → 独立","Parallel stance":"开立步","Side step":"侧行步","Stepping back":"退步","INHALE ↑":"吸气 ↑","EXHALE ↓":"呼气 ↓","about shoulder-width, toes turned in":"约与肩同宽，脚尖内扣","CENTRELINE":"中线","Technique {n} of 8 · {type} · Cantonese {py}":"第 {n} 式 · {type} · 粤语 {py}","Found in: ":"出自：","What is Wing Chun?":"詠春是什么？","Wing Chun is a close-range southern Chinese martial art (from the Guangdong–Fujian region) known for being simple, direct and economical. It spread worldwide after Ip Man taught it in Hong Kong in the 20th century. Its core ideas are the centreline, attacking and defending at the same time, and developing touch sensitivity through chi sao (sticking hands).":"Wing Chun是源自中国南方（广东、福建一带）的近身拳术，以简洁、直接、经济著称。20世纪经叶问在香港传授后广传世界。Wing Chun的核心概念包括中线理论、攻守同时、以及透过黐手（chi sao）训练触觉。","Centreline theory":"中线理论","Imagine a vertical line running down the middle of your body. Every Wing Chun hand technique works around it: protect your own centreline and attack the opponent's along the shortest straight path. That is why the elbow stays down and the fist stays directly in front of the body.":"想象一条从头顶垂直穿过身体中央的线。咏春的手法都围绕这条线：守住自己的中线，并以两点之间最短的直线攻击对方的中线。这就是为什么咏春拳出拳时手肘向下、拳头停在身体正前方。","Cantonese":"粤语拼音","Found in":"出自","Romanisations follow common English spellings and vary between schools (e.g. Sao / Sau, Fuk / Fook).":"拼音采用常见英文拼法，不同师门写法略有不同（例如 Sao / Sau、Fuk / Fook）。","A sensible learning order":"学习顺序建议","Get comfortable holding the basic stance relaxed for 2–3 minutes.":"先站好二字钳羊马，能放松站 2–3 分钟。","Learn the vertical punch, then build to chain punching.":"练日字冲拳，再进到连环拳。","Learn tan, fuk, bong and pak sao through Siu Nim Tao.":"透过小念头学摊手、伏手、膀手与拍手。","Start single sticking hands and partner drills with a sifu.":"在师父指导下开始单黐手与对练。","Want to compare? See <a href=\"../strikes/\">basic kung fu punches &amp; kicks</a> — the Changquan punch twists palm-down from the waist, very different from the Wing Chun vertical fist.":"想比较其他拳法？可看 <a href=\"../strikes/\">功夫基本拳法与腿法</a>（长拳冲拳是转腰旋拳，与咏春日字拳很不同）。","What is the centreline?":"咏春的「中线」是什么？","An imaginary vertical line down the middle of the body. Wing Chun protects your own and attacks the opponent's along the shortest straight path.":"一条从头顶垂直穿过身体中央的假想线。咏春守住自己的中线，并用最短直线攻击对方的中线。","What are the three basic hand shapes?":"咏春三大基本手形是什么？","Tan Sao, Bong Sao and Fuk Sao, all trained first in Siu Nim Tao.":"摊手、膀手、伏手，都在第一套拳小念头中练习。","Can I learn Wing Chun at home?":"可以自己在家学咏春吗？","You can practise the stance, punches and Siu Nim Tao hand shapes at home, but chi sao and partner work need a sifu and training partners — find a qualified school.":"马步、冲拳和小念头的手形可以在家练习；但黏手与对练需要师父和同伴，建议找合格的武馆学习。","Wing Chun Basics":"咏春入门","SOUTHERN KUNG FU · WING CHUN BASICS · FROM SIU NIM TAO":"南派功夫 · 咏春拳入门 · 小念头基本手法","Wing Chun Basics: 8 Techniques, Step by Step":"咏春入门 8 式互动解析：马步、日字冲拳、摊膀伏","Wing Chun is built on the centreline: guard your own and attack along the shortest straight path. These 8 techniques come from the first form, Siu Nim Tao, plus the basic kick. Switch on the centreline guide to see whether the fist and elbow stay on line.":"咏春讲求「中线」：守住自己的中线，用最短的直线攻击对方。本页 8 个动作都来自第一套拳「小念头」与基本腿法。打开中线辅助，就能看见拳和手肘是否守在正确的线上。","1 stance · 2 punches · 4 hands · 1 kick":"1 马步 · 2 拳法 · 4 手法 · 1 腿法","Key point, this technique":"目前技巧重点","The three empty-hand forms":"咏春三套拳","Siu Nim Tao · Chum Kiu · Biu Jee":"小念头 · 寻桥 · 标指","Centreline guide (shows the centreline and the elbow)":"中线辅助线（显示中线与手肘位置）","Show centreline":"显示中线","Hide":"隐藏","Details differ between lineages (Ip Man, Yuen Kay-San and others)":"各派（叶问、阮奇山等）细节略有不同","Pick a technique (in Siu Nim Tao learning order)":"选择技巧检视细节（依小念头学习顺序）","Foot placement (top view): toes in":"脚位（俯视图）：内八字","↑ facing the opponent":"↑ 面向对方","For education only. Wing Chun lineages differ — follow your own sifu, and practise partner drills under a qualified instructor.":"本页内容仅供教育参考。咏春各派细节不同，请以你的师父指导为准；与他人对练请在合格教练指导下进行。","Wing Chun Basics: Stance, Vertical Punch, Chain Punch, Tan, Bong, Fuk & Pak Sao — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"咏春基础：马步、直拳、连环拳、粘手、膀手、伏手与拍手——互动指南 | KungfuTutor","Learn 8 Wing Chun basics from Siu Nim Tao — Yee Jee Kim Yeung Ma stance, vertical punch, chain punch, Tan Sao, Bong Sao, Fuk Sao, Pak Sao and the front kick — with step-by-step animation and a centreline guide.":"通过咏春拳的小念头学习8个基本功——叶继康杨家马步、直拳、连环拳、粘手、膀手、伏手、拍手以及前踢，配有逐步动画和中线指引。","Wing Chun Basics — Interactive Step-by-Step Guide":"咏春基础——互动式逐步指南","What is the centreline in Wing Chun?":"咏春中的中线是什么？","An imaginary vertical line down the middle of the body. Wing Chun techniques protect your own centreline and attack along the shortest, straightest path to the opponent's.":"一条从身体正中央垂直向下的假想线。咏春的招式保护自己的中线，并沿着最短、最直的路径攻向对手的中线。","What are the three basic hand shapes in Wing Chun?":"咏春中的三种基本手型是什么？","Tan Sao (dispersing hand), Bong Sao (wing arm) and Fuk Sao (bridge-on hand), all trained first in the Siu Nim Tao form.":"粘手（分散手）、膀手（翼臂）和伏手（搭桥手），三者都先在小念头套路中练习。","Why does the Wing Chun punch use a vertical fist?":"为什么咏春拳的冲拳使用竖拳？","With the thumb side up, the elbow can stay down behind the fist on the centreline, giving a short, straight and well-supported punch.":"拇指一侧朝上时，手肘可以保持在拳头后方的中线下方，使拳路短、直，并获得良好支撑。","Wing Chun Basic Stance":"二字钳羊马","Toes in, knees in, hips tucked":"内八字、膝内钳、坐胯","Opening of Siu Nim Tao":"小念头开马","Lower-body structure, centreline awareness":"下盘结构与中线意识","TOES IN · KNEES GENTLY IN · WEIGHT EVEN":"脚尖内扣 · 膝微内钳 · 重心平均","From feet together, bend the knees and sink. Pivot on the heels to turn the toes out, then pivot on the balls of the feet to push the heels out, ending pigeon-toed. Feet are about shoulder-width, knees squeeze gently inward (the \"goat-clamping\" idea), hips tucked, back upright and weight even. Fists rest at the sides of the chest.":"从并步站立，屈膝下沉；以脚跟为轴把脚尖向外打开，再以前脚掌为轴把脚跟向外推，成内八字。两脚约与肩同宽，膝盖微向内钳（像夹住一只羊），臀部微收、上身正直，重心平均在两脚。双拳收于胸侧。","Squeezing the knees so hard they ache; sticking the hips out and leaning forward; feet too wide like a horse stance; tense shoulders and a rigid body.":"膝盖夹得太用力导致膝痛；臀部翘起、上身前倾；脚太宽像马步；耸肩、全身僵硬。","Open the stance 10 times a day and hold 1–3 minutes, relaxed with natural breathing — this is also how Siu Nim Tao begins.":"每天开马 10 次，每次站 1–3 分钟，全身放松、自然呼吸；这也是练小念头的起点。","The stance squares you to the opponent, protects the groin and keeps the centreline; every Wing Chun hand technique grows from this structure.":"二字钳羊马让身体正对对方、保护下阴并保持中线，所有咏春手法都从这个结构出发。","Vertical Punch":"日字冲拳","Vertical fist, elbow down, on the centreline":"拳眼向上、肘尖向下、沿中线","Siu Nim Tao":"小念头","Straight-line power and elbow structure":"直线出力与肘部结构","ELBOW DOWN · CENTRELINE · SHOULDER RELAXED":"肘尖向下 · 拳走中线 · 肩不耸","Hold the fist upright (thumb side up) on the centreline in front of the chest, elbow pointing down. Drive the elbow forward along the centreline so the fist travels in a straight line and lands with the bottom three knuckles. Extend almost to straight without locking. Keep the shoulder relaxed — the power comes from the elbow drive and body structure.":"拳头竖立（拳眼朝上），放在胸前中线，肘尖朝下。出拳时手肘沿中线推送，拳头走直线，以下三个指节着力。伸到接近伸直但不要锁死。肩膀放松，力量来自肘部推送和身体结构。","Flaring the elbow out (losing the centreline structure); turning the fist palm-down; shrugging or lunging forward; snapping the elbow into a hard lock.":"手肘外翻（失去中线结构）；拳头转为拳心朝下；耸肩或身体前冲；猛然锁死手肘。","20 slow punches in front of a mirror, checking the fist stays on the centreline and the elbow stays down; then practise on a wall bag.":"对着镜子慢打 20 拳，检查拳头是否留在中线、肘是否朝下；然后对着墙上的沙袋练习。","The vertical punch takes the shortest, most direct path — the clearest expression of Wing Chun's centreline theory.":"竖拳路线最短、最直接，是咏春“中线理论”最清楚的体现。","Chain Punch":"连环拳","Fists alternate, rolling on the centreline":"双拳交替，沿中线滚动","Siu Nim Tao (single) → drills":"小念头（单拳）→ 对练","Two-hand coordination and continuous speed":"双手协调与连续速度","ONE OUT, ONE BACK · ALWAYS ON THE CENTRELINE":"一拳出，一拳收 · 始终守住中线","Stack both fists on the centreline. Fire the first punch; as the second rolls out over the forearm along the centreline, the first returns underneath. The fists keep cycling like a wheel, so one hand always holds the centreline. Keep the elbows down, shoulders loose and the rhythm even.":"双拳叠放在中线上。打出第一拳；第二拳沿中线从前臂上方滚出时，第一拳收回到下方。两拳像车轮一样持续循环，始终有一只手守住中线。保持肘尖向下、肩膀放松、节奏均匀。","Chasing speed and losing the centreline; arms making circles instead of lines; shrugging and holding the breath; pulling back before the punch arrives.":"只追求速度而失去中线；手臂画圆而不是走直线；耸肩、屏气；拳还没打到位就收回。","Start at 1–2 punches a second for 30 seconds, then build speed; use a wall bag and keep breathing.":"先以每秒 1–2 拳慢慢练 30 秒，再逐渐加快；可对墙靶练习，注意呼吸。","Chain punching keeps attacks continuous and is one of Wing Chun's best-known techniques for close-range pressure.":"连环拳让攻击不间断，是咏春最为人熟知的技法之一，也常用于近距离连续施压。","Tan Sao (Dispersing Hand)":"Tan Sao（摊手）","Hand":"手法","Palm up, elbow a fist from the body":"掌心向上、肘离身一拳","Siu Nim Tao, section 2":"小念头第二段","Arm structure and redirecting force":"手臂结构与引化来力","PALM UP · ELBOW ONE FIST AWAY · SHOULDER DOWN":"掌心向上 · 肘离身约一拳 · 不耸肩","Starting from the centreline, turn the palm up and send the hand forward along it. The elbow settles about a fist's distance in front of the body, forearm angled towards the centre, fingers pointing forward. The outer forearm guides incoming force aside — it doesn't collide with it.":"从中线出发，掌心向上，沿中线向前摊出；手肘停在身体前方约一拳距离，前臂斜向中线，手指指向前方。重点是以手臂外侧把来力向外引开，而不是用力去撞。","Elbow too far out or jammed against the body; palm not facing up; shrugging and pushing with force; drifting off the centreline.":"手肘伸太出去或贴身；掌心没有朝上；耸肩用力顶；手偏离中线。","Practise the tan–wu–fuk sequence slowly as in Siu Nim Tao, 10 per side, feeling where the elbow sits.":"在小念头中慢慢练习摊手、护手、伏手的转换，每边 10 次；感受肘的位置。","Tan sao, bong sao and fuk sao are Wing Chun's three core arm shapes; tan sao often redirects a straight punch while you counter at the same time.":"摊手与膀手、伏手并称咏春三大基本手形，常用于化解直拳并同时反击。","Bong Sao (Wing Arm)":"Bong Sao（膀手）","Elbow above wrist, forearm slanting to the centre":"肘高于腕、前臂斜指中线","Siu Nim Tao, section 3":"小念头第三段","Shoulder rotation, structure under pressure":"肩部转动与压力下的结构","ELBOW ABOVE WRIST · WRIST ON CENTRE · SHOULDER LOOSE":"肘高于腕 · 腕在中线 · 肩放松","Rotate from the shoulder so the elbow turns out and up, higher than the wrist; the forearm slants down to the centreline with the wrist sitting on it. The other hand guards behind on the centreline (wu sao). Bong sao is a pressure-response shape: when force comes, it turns — it never pushes back hard.":"以肩为轴，将手肘向外、向上转起，肘高于手腕；前臂斜向下指向中线，手腕停在中线上。另一手护在中线后方（护手）。膀手是被压时的“转化”动作，受力就转，不用力顶。","Forcing with the shoulder; elbow too low so it becomes tan sao; wrist leaving the centreline; the whole body twisting off line.":"用肩膀力量硬顶；手肘太低变成摊手；手腕离开中线；身体跟着转歪。","Tan–bong transitions, 20 each way, small and relaxed; later feel it in chi sao (sticking hands).":"摊膀转换练习：摊手 ↔ 膀手各 20 次，动作小而放松；之后在黐手中体会。","Bong sao turns strong incoming force aside and often flows into tan sao or a grab; it's one of the most common shapes in chi sao.":"膀手用于来力强时把它转开，之后常接摊手或拉手，是黐手中最常见的手形之一。","Fuk Sao (Bridge-On Hand)":"伏手（搭手）","Soft wrist hook, elbow in to the centre":"腕微钩、肘收回中线","Elbow control and touch sensitivity":"肘部控制与触觉","WRIST SOFTLY HOOKED · ELBOW IN TO CENTRE":"腕微屈成钩 · 肘尖收向中线","Extend the hand forward from the centreline, palm down, wrist softly bent into a hook. Slowly bring the elbow in to the centreline (in Siu Nim Tao this is done very slowly). Fuk sao rests the wrist and forearm on the other person's arm and controls it through elbow position, not by pressing down.":"手由中线向前伸出，掌心向下，手腕微屈成钩状；手肘慢慢向内收回中线（小念头中以极慢速度练习）。伏手以手腕与前臂“伏”在对方手臂上，用肘的位置控制，而不是向下压。","Pressing down with force; elbow flaring; a stiff wrist; rushing it in Siu Nim Tao.":"用力往下压；手肘向外翻；手腕僵硬；练小念头时动作太快。","In section 2 of Siu Nim Tao, extend fuk sao slowly over about a minute, focusing on the elbow and staying relaxed.":"小念头第二段的伏手慢慢推出约 1 分钟，专注手肘移动和放松。","Fuk sao is the basic contact shape in chi sao, used to feel the direction of force and control the centreline.":"伏手是黐手中最基本的接触手形，用来感觉对方的力量方向并控制中线。","Pak Sao (Slapping Hand)":"拍手","Short slap to the centre, no over-travel":"短促拍向中线、不过度","Timing and using both hands at once":"时机与双手同时运用","STOP AT THE CENTRE · OTHER HAND ATTACKS TOGETHER":"拍到中线即止 · 另一手同时进攻","With a relaxed open hand, slap from your own side towards the centreline with the palm, knocking the incoming punch off line. Stop around the centre — no wide sweeps. Usually the other hand counter-strikes along the centreline at the same moment.":"手掌放松，从本侧以掌心向中线短促拍出，把来拳拍离中线；拍到中线附近就停，不要大幅横扫。通常另一手会在同一时间沿中线反击。","Slapping too wide past the centre and opening yourself up; a stiff arm; pausing before the counter.":"拍得太大、越过中线露出空档；手臂僵硬；拍完停顿才反击。","With a partner at slow speed: one throws a slow straight punch, the other pak saos and punches at the same time, 20 per side.":"与同伴慢速对练：一方慢慢出直拳，另一方拍手并同时出拳，每边 20 次。","Pak sao with a simultaneous punch is one of the most common Wing Chun combinations — defence and attack at the same time.":"拍手配合冲拳（拍打）是咏春最常见的组合之一，体现「攻守同时」。","Wing Chun Front Kick":"Wing Chun Front Kick","Toes up, heel drives straight, kept low":"脚尖向上、脚跟直蹬、低踢","Chum Kiu, wooden dummy":"寻桥、木人桩","One-leg balance and straight thrust":"单脚平衡与直线推蹬","KNEE UP THE CENTRE · HEEL STRAIGHT OUT · NO LEANING BACK":"沿中线提膝 · 脚跟直蹬 · 不后仰","From the basic stance with hands guarding the centreline, shift weight to the support leg and lift the knee up the centreline with the toes pulled back. Drive the heel straight out at roughly knee-to-stomach height. Keep the body upright, then re-chamber and set the foot down.":"从二字钳羊马出发，双手护中线。重心移到支撑腿，沿中线提膝，脚尖勾起；以脚跟直线向前蹬出，高度约在膝到腹部之间。上身保持正直，蹬完收回提膝再落地。","Kicking too high and losing balance; leaning back; kicking with the toes; not re-chambering.":"踢太高、失去平衡；上身后仰；用脚尖踢；踢完没有收回。","Slow kicks with a hand on a wall, 10 per leg, then push into a thick pad; keep the hands on the centreline.":"扶墙慢踢每腿 10 次，再对厚垫练习推蹬；保持双手在中线上。","Wing Chun kicks stay low and direct and are often thrown together with hand techniques — height isn't the goal.":"咏春腿法低而直，常与手法同时使用，不追求高度。","Wing Chun root: the \"goat-clamping\" stance":"咏春根基：二字钳羊马","Square body · centreline · stability":"正身 · 中线 · 稳定","Signature punch: the vertical fist":"咏春代表拳法：日字拳","Centreline · straight line · short range":"中线 · 直线 · 短距离","Signature technique: chain punching":"咏春代表技法：连环冲拳","Speed · continuity · coordination":"速度 · 连续 · 协调","One of the three core arm shapes":"三大基本手形之一","Disperse · redirect · centreline":"摊开 · 引化 · 中线","Wing shape · deflect · never force":"翼形 · 转化 · 不硬顶","Cover · control · chi sao base":"伏 · 控制 · 黏手基础","Basic hand: slap the punch aside":"基本手法：拍开来拳","Short · fast · counter at once":"短 · 快 · 同时反击","Wing Chun kick: the front heel kick":"咏春腿法：正蹬脚","Low · straight · heel power":"低 · 直 · 脚跟发力","Stand with feet together, relaxed":"并步站立，全身放松","Fists to the sides of the chest, bend the knees and sink":"双拳收于胸侧，屈膝下沉","Pivot on the heels: toes turn out":"以脚跟为轴，脚尖向外打开","Pivot on the balls: heels turn out → toes in; knees gently in, hips tucked, weight even":"以脚掌为轴，脚跟向外 → 内八字；膝微向内钳，坐胯，重心平均","Stand with feet together":"并步站立","From the side: knees soft, back upright, hips tucked — no leaning":"侧看：膝微屈、上身正直，臀部微收，不前倾","Fist on the centreline in front of the chest, elbow pointing down":"拳置胸前中线，肘尖向下","Drive straight out along the centreline, fist vertical (thumb side up)":"沿中线直线打出，拳眼向上（日字拳）","Land with the bottom three knuckles, shoulder relaxed":"以下三指节触及目标，肩膀放松","Return along the same line":"沿原路收回中线","Both fists stacked on the centreline, ready":"双拳叠在中线上，准备","First punch out along the centreline":"第一拳沿中线打出","The rear fist rolls out over the front forearm as the front fist returns":"后拳从前臂上方滚出，前拳同时收回","Keep alternating, like a rolling wheel":"连续交替，像车轮一样滚动","Hand on the centreline, elbow down":"手置中线，肘尖向下","Turn the palm up and send it forward along the centreline":"掌心向上，沿中线向前摊出","Elbow about a fist from the body, forearm angled to the centre — the arm guides incoming force aside":"肘离身约一拳，前臂斜向中线，用手臂外侧把来力向外引开","Circle the wrist and return":"转腕收回","Both hands guard the centreline (wu sao)":"双手护中线（护手）","Rotate from the shoulder: the elbow turns out and up":"以肩为轴，手肘向外、向上转起","Elbow above the wrist, forearm slanting down to the centre; the other hand guards behind it":"肘高于腕，前臂斜向下指向中线；另一手护在中线后方","Relax back — bong sao deflects, it never pushes hard":"放松还原，膀手不是硬顶","Extend forward, palm down, wrist bent into a soft hook":"手掌向前伸出，掌心向下、腕关节微屈成钩","Bring the elbow in to the centre; the wrist and forearm rest on and control the other arm":"肘尖向内收回中线，以手腕和前臂“伏”住对方手臂","Stay relaxed — don't press down or push":"保持放松，不压不顶","Open hand in front of the same-side shoulder, ready":"手掌在本侧肩前，准备","A short, sharp slap with the palm towards the centreline — don't over-travel":"以掌心向中线短促拍出，不超过中线太多","Clear the incoming punch while the other hand prepares to strike":"拍开来拳，另一手准备同时反击","Return to guard":"收回护位","From the stance, hands guarding the centreline":"二字钳羊马上，双手护中线","Lift the knee along the centreline, weight onto the support leg":"沿中线提膝，重心移到支撑腿","Toes up, drive straight out with the heel at about stomach height":"脚尖向上，以脚跟向前直蹬，高度约在腹部","Re-chamber, then settle back into the stance":"收回提膝，再落回马步","RED DASHES = CENTRELINE":"红色虚线 = 中线","RED DASHES = CENTRELINE · GREEN = ELBOW (DOWN)":"红虚线 = 中线出拳路线 · 绿点 = 手肘（向下）","Lower-body structure":"下盘结构","Centreline awareness":"中线意识","Hip & knee control":"髋膝控制","Elbow structure":"肘部结构","Two-hand coordination":"双手协调","Speed endurance":"速度耐力","Redirecting sensitivity":"引化感觉","Shoulder rotation":"肩部转动","Structure under pressure":"受压结构","Elbow control":"手肘控制","Sensitivity":"触觉","Straight thrust":"直线推蹬","Upper-body control":"上身控制","When: ":"时机：","Move {n} of 8 · {type}":"第 {n} 个动作 · {type}","The five layers of self-defence":"自我防卫的五个层次","Most danger can be avoided long before anyone needs to fight. Good self-defence courses put physical moves last:":"大多数危险，在需要动手之前就可以避开。专业的防身课程都把「打」放在最后：","Stay aware: ":"留意四周：","Keep your phone down and your music low when walking; notice who is approaching and where the exits are.":"走路时少看手机、戴耳机音量放小，留意谁在靠近、出口在哪里。","Avoid trouble: ":"避开危险：","If something feels wrong, change route, cross the road or walk into a busy shop — trust your gut.":"感觉不对就换条路、过马路、走进有人的店家，相信你的直觉。","Talk it down: ":"说话化解：","Use the fence and say \"No\" and \"Stay back\" clearly and firmly. Don't argue or insult.":"用戒备姿势、清楚坚定地说「不」和「退后」。不要争吵、不要挑衅。","Leave and get help: ":"离开求助：","Hand over your wallet or phone if asked — you matter more than things. Head towards people, shout for help and call the police.":"钱包、手机都可以给，你的安全最重要。往人多的地方走，大声求助并报警。","Defend only if you must: ":"最后才动手：","Only when you cannot get away, use the moves on this page to create a moment — then leave at once.":"真的无法离开时，才用本页的动作制造空档——然后立刻离开。","The eight moves at a glance":"八个动作一览","Move":"动作","When":"使用时机","Why these targets?":"为什么选这些目标？","The chin, nose, knees and shins can stop someone without great strength, and striking with tough surfaces — the heel of the palm, the bottom of the fist, the elbow and the heel — keeps you from hurting yourself. The aim is to stop them for a few seconds so you can leave, not to injure them.":"下巴、鼻子、膝盖和小腿都是不需要很大力气就能让人停下来的部位，而且用掌根、拳底、手肘和脚跟这些「硬又不易受伤」的部位去打，自己比较不会受伤。目的是让对方停住几秒，让你有时间离开，而不是伤害对方。","Only strike pads, kick shields or cushions — never hit your practice partner.":"击打类动作只打手靶、踢靶或软垫，绝对不要真的打练习伙伴。","Do escapes slowly and gently, and stop the moment your partner says stop.":"脱困练习要慢、要温和，伙伴喊停就立刻停。","End every rep by stepping back and leaving, so getting away becomes a habit.":"每次练习都以「后退、离开」结束，把离开练成习惯。","To go further, join a self-defence class with a qualified instructor.":"想更进一步，请报名有合格教练的防身课程。","To build stronger basic strikes and kicks, see <a href=\"../../kungfu/strikes/\">basic punches &amp; kicks</a>.":"想加强出拳与踢腿的基本功，可以参考 <a href=\"../../kungfu/strikes/\">基本拳法与腿法</a>。","What is the most important rule?":"自我防卫最重要的是什么？","Avoid the fight and leave early. Awareness, distance and a firm \"No\" prevent far more harm than any technique.":"避免冲突、尽早离开。留意四周、保持距离、坚定说不，能避免的伤害远比任何招式都多。","How do I escape a wrist grab?":"手腕被抓住怎么脱困？","Don't pull straight back. Bend your elbow, step closer and rip out through the gap between their thumb and fingers, then step back and leave.":"不要硬拉。屈肘、身体靠近一点，朝对方拇指与食指之间（虎口）快速转出，然后后退离开。","Is it legal to hit someone in self-defence?":"自我防卫时打人合法吗？","Laws differ, but generally you may only use reasonable and necessary force to protect yourself, and you must stop and leave once you are safe. Check the law where you live.":"各国法律不同，但一般只允许使用“合理且必要”的力量保护自己，安全后就必须停止并离开。请了解你所在地的法律。","Does this work if I am small or not strong?":"体型小、力气小也有用吗？","These moves rely on distance, direction (like the thumb gap) and tough body surfaces rather than strength. Still, nothing is guaranteed — leaving is always the first choice.":"这些动作都选择不靠蛮力的方法：利用距离、方向（例如拇指弱点）和身体的硬部位。不过任何人都无法保证成功，所以离开永远是第一选择。","PERSONAL SAFETY · BASICS ANYONE CAN LEARN":"个人安全 · 人人都能学的基本防身","Self-Defence Basics: 8 Simple Moves to Stay Safe":"基本防身术：8 个保护自己的简单动作","From setting a boundary and keeping your distance to getting free when someone grabs you — every move is animated, with the grey figure showing the other person. Click a step to freeze it. Every move has the same goal: create a moment, then get away and get help.":"从设立界线、保持距离，到被抓住时如何脱身——每个动作都附动画，灰色人形代表对方。点击步骤可定格查看。所有动作的目标都一样：制造空档，然后离开、求助。","First rule: if you can leave, leave":"先记住：能离开就离开","Self-defence is about getting away safely, not winning. Physical moves are a last resort, and you may only use force that is reasonable and necessary — stop and leave as soon as you are safe. Laws differ from place to place, so learn the rules where you live. These animations are an introduction, not a substitute for a real class: train with a qualified instructor and proper pads.":"自我防卫的目的是让你安全离开，不是打赢。动手只是最后手段，而且只能使用合理、必要的力量；安全后就停止并离开。各地法律不同，请了解你所在地的规定。这些动画只是入门介绍，无法取代实际课程——请到合格的防身课程，与教练和护具一起练习。","Stay aware":"留意四周","Avoid trouble":"避开危险","Talk it down":"说话化解","Leave & get help":"离开求助","Defend only if you must":"最后才动手","Basic moves":"基本动作","2 prevent · 4 strike · 1 escape · 1 defend":"2 预防 · 4 反击 · 1 脱困 · 1 防守","This move is for":"目前动作用途","Safe gap":"安全距离","arm":"臂","Out of reach of their hands":"对方伸手碰不到你的距离","Moves you have mastered":"动作掌握进度","Mark each move as mastered below":"可在下方标记为「已熟悉」","Choose the pace (the animation updates instantly)":"选择播放速度（动画即时改变）","Pick a move (best learned in order)":"选择动作查看细节（建议依序学习）","When to use it":"使用时机","Why it works":"为什么有效","SIDE VIEW · GREY = OTHER PERSON":"侧面 · 灰色＝对方","What this move trains":"此动作训练重点","For education only — not legal advice and no substitute for a real self-defence class. In danger, leave and call the police first. When practising with a partner, go slowly, use pads and train under a qualified instructor.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，不构成法律意见，也无法取代实际的防身课程。遇到危险请优先离开并报警。与他人练习时请放慢速度、使用护具，并在合格教练指导下进行。","Self-Defence Basics: 8 Simple Moves to Stay Safe — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"防身基础：8个保持安全的简单动作——互动指南 | KungfuTutor","Learn eight basic self-defence moves with step-by-step animation: the fence, keeping distance, palm heel strike, hammer fist, elbow strike, low stomp kick, wrist-grab release and head cover — plus how to avoid trouble and get away safely.":"通过分步动画学习八个基础防身动作：格挡式（the fence）、保持距离、掌根击、锤拳、肘击、低位踩踢、手腕抓握脱离，以及护头；同时了解如何避免麻烦并安全脱身。","Self-Defence Basics — 8 Moves, Step by Step":"防身基础——8个动作，逐步学习","What is the most important rule of self-defence?":"防身最重要的原则是什么？","Avoid the fight and get away. Awareness, keeping your distance, a firm voice and leaving early prevent far more harm than any strike. Physical moves are a last resort to create a moment to escape.":"避免冲突并尽快离开。保持警觉、保持距离、语气坚定，以及及早离开，远比任何一击更能防止伤害。身体动作只是最后手段，用来争取脱身的机会。","How do you escape a wrist grab?":"如何摆脱手腕被抓？","Don't pull straight back. Bend your elbow, step a little closer and rip your wrist out through the gap between their thumb and fingers, which is the weakest part of the grip. Then step back and leave.":"不要直接往后拉。屈肘，稍微靠近一步，从对方拇指和其他手指之间的缝隙把手腕抽出来，那里是握力最弱的地方。然后后退一步并离开。","Laws differ between countries, but generally you may only use force that is reasonable and necessary to protect yourself, and you should stop and leave as soon as you are safe. Check the law where you live.":"各国法律不同，但一般而言，你只能使用合理且必要的武力保护自己，并且一旦安全就应停止并离开。请查询你所在地的法律。","The Fence (Ready Stance)":"戒备姿势","Prevent":"预防","— (no strike)":"—（不攻击）","Someone closes in and things feel wrong":"对方靠近、气氛不对时","Setting a calm, clear boundary":"冷静、清楚地设下界线","HANDS UP · PALMS OUT · FIRM VOICE":"手在胸前 · 掌心向外 · 声音坚定","Step one foot back half a pace and turn slightly side-on, knees soft, weight even. Raise your open hands between chest and chin height, palms out and elbows bent — like signalling \"stop\". Say \"Stay back!\" loudly and firmly. It looks calm to anyone watching, but your hands are already between you and them, ready to block or push.":"一脚后退半步，身体稍微斜向对方，膝盖微屈、重心平均。双手张开、掌心向外举到胸前与下巴之间，手肘微屈，就像在说\"停\"。大声、坚定地说\"退后！\"。这个姿势看起来不具攻击性，旁人会看到你在拒绝，但你的双手已经挡在中间，随时可以防守或推开。","Raising fists (looks like you want a fight and can escalate it); hands low or in pockets; standing square with feet together so one push knocks you over; speaking quietly or apologising instead of saying \"No\".":"握拳举起（看起来像要打架、容易激怒对方）；双手放太低或插口袋；站得太正、两脚并拢，一推就倒；小声道歉、不敢说「不」。","In front of a mirror, go from relaxed standing to the fence in one step, saying \"Stay back!\" each time — 10 times each side until it happens without thinking.":"对镜练习从自然站立「一步」进入戒备姿势，每次配合说出「退后！」，左右各 10 次，直到不用想就做得到。","Almost every self-defence course starts here: it is both a message and a guard. Every other move on this page starts from it.":"所有自我防卫课程几乎都从这个姿势开始：它既是沟通，也是防守的起点。后面每个动作都从这里出发。","Keep Your Distance":"保持距离","They keep stepping towards you":"对方一直逼近","Spatial awareness and footwork":"空间感与移动","MORE THAN AN ARM · SMALL STEPS · FIND THE EXIT":"一臂以上 · 小步后退 · 找出口","Stay in the fence and keep more than an arm's length between you. When they step in, take a small step back or back-and-to-the-side — never cross your feet. Keep your eyes on them while using your peripheral vision to find an exit or people, and shout for help.":"保持戒备姿势，让你和对方之间至少隔着一只手臂以上的距离。对方往前一步，你就用小步后退或斜退一步，不要交叉双脚。后退时眼睛看着对方，用眼角找出口、人多的地方，并大声求助。","Turning your back; big steps or crossed feet that trip you; backing into a corner; retreating silently instead of calling for help.":"转身背对对方；大步后退或交叉脚步而跌倒；退到墙角、无路可走；只顾后退忘了求助。","Have a friend walk slowly towards you while you keep the gap with small steps for one minute; then do it again while saying where the exit is.":"请朋友慢慢向你走近，你用小步保持距离，练习 1 分钟；再练习一边后退一边说出出口在哪里。","The bigger the gap, the harder you are to reach and the easier it is to leave. The best self-defence never needs a strike.":"距离越远，对方越难碰到你，你也越容易离开。最好的自我防卫是根本不需要动手。","Palm Heel Strike":"掌根击","Chin or nose":"下巴、鼻子","They attack and you cannot get away":"对方已经动手、无法离开时","Whole-body pushing power":"全身发力推击","FINGERS UP · HEEL OF THE PALM · STRIKE AND RETURN":"手指向上 · 用掌根 · 打完就收","From the fence, bend the rear wrist back with the fingers up and drive the hard base of the palm upward into their chin or nose. Push off the back foot and turn the hips so your body weight goes with it. Pull straight back to the fence, open the distance and leave.":"从戒备姿势，后手手腕向后弯、手指向上，用手掌最下面的硬骨（掌根）由下往上推向对方下巴或鼻子。后脚蹬地、转腰，让身体的力量一起送出去。打完立刻收回戒备，拉开距离、离开。","Hitting with the fingers (they bend back); arm-only with no body behind it; staying to watch what happens; slow recovery.":"手指先碰到目标（会扭伤）；只用手臂、身体不动；打完停在原地看结果；收手太慢。","On a pad or a cushion against a wall, 10 strikes each side — focus on landing with the heel of the palm, fingers up, and snapping back to the fence.":"对着手靶或挂在墙上的厚枕头，左右各 10 下，重点是掌根接触、手指向上，以及打完马上回到戒备。","Many self-defence courses teach the palm heel first: it is simple, natural and much less likely to injure your own hand than a punch.":"许多自我防卫课程把掌根击当作第一个学的反击动作：简单、自然，而且不容易弄伤自己的手。","Hammer Fist":"锤拳","Reaching arm or face":"伸来的手臂、脸","They reach out to grab you":"对方伸手抓你","Downward striking speed":"向下砸击的速度","TIGHT FIST · LITTLE-FINGER SIDE · TOP TO BOTTOM":"拳头握紧 · 用小指那侧 · 由上往下","Make a tight fist, raise the lead hand above the shoulder, then bring the bottom of the fist (the fleshy little-finger side) down fast onto the reaching arm or face — like banging a table. Let your body weight drop with it. Return to the fence, step back and leave.":"握紧拳头，把前手举到肩膀上方，然后像用拳头敲桌子一样，用拳底（小指那侧的肉）快速往下砸向对方伸过来的手臂或脸。身体重心跟着往下沉。打完收回戒备、后退离开。","Hitting with the knuckles (an injury risk); a loose fist; a huge wind-up they can see coming; not leaving afterwards.":"用指节打（容易受伤）；拳头没握紧；手举太高、动作太大让对方看到；打完没有离开。","On a cushion or pad resting on a table, 10 each side — feel the contact on the bottom of the fist and bend your knees slightly to drop your weight.":"对着放在桌上的枕头或软垫，左右各 10 下，感受用拳底接触，并配合膝盖微弯让重心下沉。","The hammer fist is instinctive — people can do it under stress with no training — and the bottom of the fist is far tougher than the knuckles.":"锤拳是很直觉的动作，即使没有训练也能用得出来，而且拳底比指节耐打得多。","Elbow Strike":"肘击","Close-range strike":"近身反击","Jaw or side of the face":"下巴、脸侧","They are very close or holding you":"对方太近、抓住你","Short-range hip rotation":"近距离转腰发力","ELBOW LEVEL · TURN THE HIPS · THEN SHOVE AWAY":"手肘水平 · 转腰 · 打完推开","When they are close enough to grab you, fold the arm so your hand is near your own chest, then turn the hips and swing the elbow forward, level, striking the jaw or side of the face with the point of the elbow. Follow with a two-handed shove and get away immediately.":"当对方近到抓住你时，手臂弯起、手掌靠近自己的胸口，转腰把手肘水平往前甩，用手肘前端打向对方下巴或脸侧。接着双掌用力推开对方，马上后退离开。","Elbow travelling down or up instead of level; arm not folded tight so it becomes a swing; no hip turn; staying to grapple afterwards.":"手肘往下或往上歪；手臂没弯紧，变成甩手；只动手臂不转腰；打完继续纠缠。","Slowly on a pad, 10 each side — elbow at shoulder height, power from the hips; then add the follow-up \"shove → step back\".":"对着手靶慢速练习左右各 10 次，确认手肘与肩同高、转腰发力；接着加上「推开 → 后退」两步。","The elbow is one of the hardest parts of the body; when there is no room to extend the arm it works far better than a punch or palm.":"手肘是身体最硬的部位之一，距离太近、手臂伸不直时，肘击比拳头或掌击更有用。","Low Stomp Kick":"低位踹腿","Knee or shin":"膝盖、小腿胫骨","They are closing in from about a leg's length away":"对方逼近，还在一腿距离外","One-leg balance and thrusting power":"单脚平衡与推蹬力量","KNEE UP · HEEL OUT · KEEP IT LOW · RECOIL FAST":"提膝 · 脚跟踹出 · 踢低 · 马上收回","From the fence, lift the back knee with the toes pulled up and thrust the heel forward and down into their knee or shin. Pull the leg straight back, plant it, then step away. High kicks are easy to catch and easy to fall from, so in self-defence keep every kick low.":"从戒备姿势把后腿膝盖提起，脚尖勾起，用脚跟往前、往下踹向对方的膝盖或小腿胫骨。踹完立刻把脚收回、落地站稳，再后退离开。高踢容易被抓住或失去平衡，自我防卫只踢低位。","Kicking high and getting the leg caught; kicking with the toes (they jam); leaving the leg out; leaning far back and falling.":"踢太高、被抓住脚；用脚尖踢（容易扭伤）；踢完脚停在空中；身体后仰太多而跌倒。","Holding a wall or chair, practise \"knee up → heel out → pull back → plant\" slowly, 10 per leg; once balanced, try it on a kick shield.":"扶着墙或椅背，慢速练习“提膝 → 踹出 → 收回 → 落地”，每腿 10 次；平衡稳定后再对着踢靶练。","Knees and shins are hard to protect; one low kick can stop someone long enough for you to leave.":"膝盖与胫骨很难防守，一记低踹就能让对方停下来，给你时间离开。","Wrist-Grab Release":"手腕被抓脱困","— (the gap at their thumb)":"—（对方的虎口）","Someone grabs your wrist":"手腕被人抓住","Finding the weak point and exploding out":"找出抓握弱点、快速转出","BEND THE ELBOW · STEP IN · OUT THROUGH THE THUMB":"屈肘 · 靠近一点 · 朝拇指方向转出","Don't pull straight back — four gripping fingers beat your pull. Bend your elbow and step a little closer, then find their thumb: the gap between thumb and fingers is the weakest part of any grip. Rip your wrist out through that gap, leading with the elbow. Once free, go straight to the fence and get away.":"被抓住时不要硬往后拉——四根手指的力量比你的拉力大。先屈肘、身体靠近一点，再看对方拇指在哪一边：拇指和食指之间（虎口）是最弱的地方。把手腕朝那个方向快速转、往上抽出，手肘带着手前进。脱开后立刻回到戒备、后退离开。","Pulling straight back; a straight arm, using only the wrist; turning towards the fingers instead of the thumb; staying put after you are free.":"用力往后拉；手肘伸直、只靠手腕；转错方向（朝四根手指那边）；脱开后还留在原地。","Have a friend hold your wrist lightly; slowly find the thumb side and turn out, 10 times each side, then let them grip harder as you improve. Go gently — don't twist each other's wrists.":"请朋友轻轻抓住你的手腕，先慢慢找出拇指方向、转出，左右各 10 次；熟练后对方逐渐加力。练习时请温和，不要扭伤手腕。","A wrist grab is one of the most common situations; this release needs technique, not strength, so it works for smaller people too.":"被抓手腕是很常见的情况；这个动作不需要力气，小个子对大个子也有效。","Head Cover":"护头防守","Defend":"防守","— (protect the head)":"—（保护头部）","A sudden punch comes at your head":"对方突然挥拳打来","Protecting the head under surprise":"在惊吓中保护头部","ARMS FRAME THE HEAD · CHIN DOWN · LEAN IN · SHOVE":"双臂护头 · 收下巴 · 身体前倾 · 推开","When a punch comes suddenly, everyone flinches — hands up, head down. Train that flinch into a real guard: raise both forearms with the hands against the sides or back of your head, elbows forward, chin tucked and body leaning in slightly so your arms and elbows take the impact. The moment it stops, shove them away with both palms, step back, leave and get help.":"有人突然挥拳时，人本能会举手、缩头。把这个反应练成好防守：双手前臂举起，掌心贴近头的两侧或后脑，手肘朝前，收下巴、身体稍微向前，让前臂和手肘吸收打击。对方一停，双掌用力推开，后退离开并求助。","Closing your eyes and turning your back; arms too wide so the head is exposed; leaning back (easy to be knocked over); covering and never leaving.":"闭眼转身、背对对方；双臂张太开，头部露出；身体往后仰（容易被打倒）；一直护头不离开。","Have a friend swing slowly at your head from different angles with a soft glove or pillow; practise cover → shove → step back for a minute at a time.":"请朋友用软手套或枕头慢慢从不同方向挥向你的头，练习护头 → 推开 → 后退，每次 1 分钟。","Head injuries are the most dangerous kind; covering first gives you the chance to shove and get away.":"头部受伤是最危险的；先护住头，才有机会推开和离开。","Step one: protect yourself":"第一步：先保护自己","Side-on · open hands · loud voice":"斜站 · 张开双手 · 大声说话","Distance is safety":"距离就是安全","They step in, you step back":"对方进一步，你退一步","Safer for your hand than a fist":"比拳头更不易伤手","Straight from the fence":"从戒备姿势直接出手","Bottom of the fist — knuckles stay safe":"用拳底，不怕伤指节","Comes down from above":"由上往下砸","Best when they are very close":"距离太近时最有效","Hips drive the elbow":"转腰带动手肘","Legs are longer and stronger than arms":"腿比手长，力量更大","Kick low, never high":"踢低不踢高","Use the weak point at the thumb":"利用拇指弱点","Direction beats strength":"不比力气，比方向","Turn the flinch into a good guard":"本能反应变成好防守","Protecting the head comes first":"保护头部最重要","Someone approaches and their words or body language feel wrong":"对方走近，语气或动作让你不安","Step one foot back, turn slightly side-on, raise open hands to chest height":"后脚退半步斜站，双手张开举到胸前","Palms forward, firm loud voice: \"Stay back!\"":"手掌向前、声音坚定：「退后！」","In the fence, watch their hands":"戒备姿势，留意对方双手","They step in…":"对方上前一步…","…you step back, keeping more than an arm's length between you":"…你就后退一步，保持一臂以上的距离","Look for the exit, shout for help, get ready to leave":"同时找出口、大声求助，准备离开","They close in and reach for you — you are in the fence":"对方逼近、伸手——你在戒备姿势中","Drive the heel of the rear palm up into the chin, pushing off the back foot and turning the hips":"后手掌根由下往上推向下巴，后脚蹬地、转腰","Snap straight back to the fence":"立刻收回戒备","Open the distance, leave, get help":"拉开距离，离开现场、求助","Make a fist with the lead hand and raise it above the shoulder":"前手握拳，举到肩上","Bring the bottom of the fist (little-finger side) down onto the reaching arm or face":"用拳底（小指那侧）往下砸向伸来的手臂或脸","Back to the fence":"收回戒备","Step back and leave":"后退、离开","They are too close and grab your collar":"对方太近，抓住你的衣领","Draw the elbow back and load the hips":"手肘向后收，准备转腰","Turn the hips and swing the elbow forward, level, into the jaw":"转腰，手肘水平向前打向下巴","Shove them away with both palms":"双掌推开对方","In the fence; they keep closing in":"戒备姿势，对方一步步逼近","Lift the back knee":"后腿提膝","Thrust the heel into their knee or shin":"脚跟踹向对方膝盖或小腿胫骨","Pull the leg back, stay balanced":"收回腿，保持平衡","Plant the foot, step back, leave":"落地后退、离开","They grab your wrist":"对方抓住你的手腕","Don't pull straight back: bend the elbow and step a little closer":"不要硬拉：屈肘、身体靠近一点","Rip the arm out towards their thumb — the gap where the grip is weakest":"朝对方拇指的方向（虎口）快速转出","Straight back into the fence":"立刻回到戒备","They swing a punch at your head":"对方挥拳打向头部","Raise both forearms to frame the head, chin tucked, body leaning in slightly":"双臂抬起护住头两侧，收下巴、身体微向前","Shove with both palms to make space":"双掌推开，制造空间","Step back, leave, get help":"后退、离开、求助","SAFE GAP: MORE THAN AN ARM":"安全距离：一臂以上","\"STAY BACK!\"":"\"退后！\"","Setting a boundary":"设立界线","Stable stance":"站姿稳定","Hand position":"双手位置","Voice & confidence":"声音与自信","Spatial awareness":"空间感知","Spotting exits":"观察出口","Calling for help":"呼救","Whole-body power":"全身发力","Fast recovery":"快速收回","Downward drive":"向下砸击","Dropping your weight":"重心下沉","Getting away after":"事后脱离","Thrusting power":"推蹬力量","Fast recoil":"快速收腿","Finding the weak point":"找出弱点","Explosive release":"爆发式挣脱","Leading with the elbow":"以肘部带动","Leaving after":"脱困后离开","Cover reflex":"护头反射","Guard structure":"防守架构","Shoving away":"推开对方","Escape & get help":"脱离与求助","What is Krav Maga?":"什么是 Krav Maga？","Krav Maga (Hebrew for \"close combat\") is a self-defence system developed in Israel that borrows practical movements from boxing, wrestling and other fighting arts. It has no competition rules: training focuses on real situations — reacting fast, using the body's natural reflexes, defending and countering together, and getting away safely.":"Krav Maga（希伯来文意思是“近身格斗”）是在以色列发展起来的自我防卫系统，结合拳击、摔跤等格斗技的实用动作。它没有比赛规则，训练重点是真实情况：快速反应、利用身体自然的反射、防守和反击同时进行，最后安全离开。","Three core principles":"三个核心原则","Defend and counter together: ":"同时防守与反击：","Don't block and then hit — do both at once to spend less time on the back foot.":"不要先挡完再打，两者同时进行，缩短被动的时间。","Continuous motion (retzev): ":"连续攻击（Retzev）：","Once you must fight back, keep going without pausing until you can escape.":"一旦必须反击，就不停顿，直到能够离开。","Scan and leave: ":"观察与离开：","The goal is getting home safe, not winning. Every move ends with scanning and leaving.":"目标是安全回家，不是打赢。每个动作都以观察四周、离开现场结束。","Strike only pads, shields or protective gear.":"击打只打手靶、踢靶或护具。","In choke and grab drills, the partner rests their hands lightly — no real squeezing.":"掐喉、抓握练习时，伙伴只是轻轻放上手，不要真的用力。","End every drill by backing off, scanning and leaving.":"每一次练习都以“后退、观察、离开”结束。","To go further, join a Krav Maga class with a qualified instructor.":"想更进一步，请报名有合格教练的 Krav Maga 课程。","You can also start with <a href=\"../basics/\">self-defence basics</a> for the fence and keeping your distance.":"也可以先看 <a href=\"../basics/\">基本防身术 8 招</a>，学习戒备姿势与保持距离。","How is Krav Maga different from other martial arts?":"Krav Maga 和一般武术有什么不同？","It has no competitions or forms — only real self-defence situations, simple movements and getting out fast.":"它没有比赛和套路，只专注在真实的自我防卫情况，动作简单，强调尽快脱身。","What do I do if I'm choked from the front?":"被正面掐住脖子怎么办？","Bring both hands up, hook the thumbs and pluck down and out with your chin tucked, then counter and get away.":"双手立刻举起勾住对方的拇指，往下往外拉开，下巴收紧，接着反击并离开。","Does it work for smaller people?":"体型小的人也有用吗？","Krav Maga is designed not to rely on strength — it uses weak points, timing and continuous counters. Still, nothing is guaranteed; leaving is always the first choice.":"Krav Maga 的动作设计就是不靠蛮力：利用弱点、时机与连续反击。不过没有任何方法保证成功，离开永远是第一选择。","Krav Maga":"以色列格斗术","SELF-DEFENCE · KRAV MAGA FOR BEGINNERS":"自我防卫 · 以色列格斗术入门","Krav Maga Basics: Defend, Counter, Get Away":"以色列格斗术（Krav Maga）入门：防守、反击、离开","Krav Maga is a self-defence system developed in Israel built on simple, natural movements: defend and counter at the same time, keep going once you fight back, and finish by getting away safely. The grey figure is the attacker; the red ring marks where your counter lands.":"Krav Maga 是以色列发展的防身系统，重点是简单、自然的动作：防守与反击同时进行，反击时连续不停，最后安全离开。灰色人形代表攻击者，红圈标示反击的位置。","If you can avoid it or leave, do. Use only reasonable, necessary force when you cannot get away, and stop and call the police as soon as you are safe. Laws differ from place to place. In training, strike only pads or protective gear — never really hit, choke or kick your partner — and train under a qualified instructor.":"能避开就避开、能离开就离开。只在无法离开时使用合理、必要的力量保护自己，安全后立刻停止并报警。各地法律不同。练习时只打手靶或护具，绝对不要真的打、掐或踢同伴；请在合格教练指导下训练。","Core principle":"核心原则","Defend = counter":"防守＝反击","At the same time, not one after the other":"同时进行，不是先后","When to use this move":"目前动作使用时机","Last step of every move":"每个动作的最后一步","Leave":"离开","Scan, then get to safety":"观察四周、到安全的地方","SIDE · GREY = ATTACKER":"侧面 · 灰色＝攻击者","For education only — not legal advice and no substitute for a real Krav Maga class. In danger, leave and call the police first. When practising with a partner, go slowly, use pads and train under a qualified instructor.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，不构成法律意见，也无法取代实际的 Krav Maga 课程。遇到危险请优先离开并报警。与他人练习时请放慢速度、使用护具，并在合格教练指导下进行。","Krav Maga Basics: Stance, Defences, Choke Release & Counters — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"Krav Maga 基础：站姿、防守、解脱抱颈与反击 — 互动指南 | KungfuTutor","Learn 8 Krav Maga self-defence basics with animated demos against an attacker: fighting stance, straight-punch burst, inside defence, 360° outside defence, front-choke release, groin kick, knee from the clinch, and breaking away to safety.":"通过动画示范学习 8 项 Krav Maga 基础防身技术，对付攻击者：格斗站姿、直拳爆发、内侧防守、360° 外侧防守、正面抱颈解脱、踢裆、近身膝击，以及脱身逃离到安全处。","Krav Maga Basics — Defend, Counter, Get Away":"Krav Maga 基础：防守、反击、脱身","A self-defence system developed in Israel that focuses on simple, instinctive movements: defend and counter at the same time, keep attacking until you can escape, and get away to safety.":"一套源自以色列的防身体系，专注于简单、本能的动作：同时防守和反击，持续攻击直到能够脱身，然后逃到安全处。","How do you escape a front choke?":"如何从正面抱颈中脱身？","Bring both hands up, hook your fingers over the attacker's thumbs and pluck them down and out while tucking your chin, then counter and get away.":"双手抬起，把手指勾住攻击者的拇指，向下、向外扳开，同时收下巴，然后反击并脱身。","What does retzev mean in Krav Maga?":"Krav Maga 中的 retzev 是什么意思？","Continuous motion: once you have to fight back, you keep moving and striking without pausing until you can escape.":"持续移动：一旦必须还击，就不停地移动和出击，直到能够脱身为止。","Fighting Stance":"戒备姿势","When you sense a threat":"感觉到威胁时","Readiness and balance":"准备与平衡","SOFT KNEES · LEAN IN · HANDS UP":"膝微屈 · 身体前倾 · 双手举起","Stand with feet staggered about shoulder-width, knees soft, weight on the balls of the feet and the upper body leaning slightly forward. Hold your hands up in front of your face — open (which looks less aggressive) or closed — with the elbows in and the chin down. From here you can defend, counter or get away at any moment.":"双脚前后站立，约与肩同宽，膝盖微屈，体重放在脚掌前部，上身略微前倾。双手举在脸前——张开（看起来较不具攻击性）或握拳——手肘收在身体内侧，下巴收低。从这个姿势，你随时可以防守、反击或脱离。","Standing upright with weight on the heels (easy to push over); hands too low; feet on one line; stiffness.":"站得笔直、体重放在脚跟（一推就倒）；双手太低；双脚站成一条直线；身体僵硬。","Step from relaxed standing into the stance 10 times, then move forward and back in it for a minute.":"从自然站立「一步」进入戒备姿势 10 次，再在戒备姿势中前后移动 1 分钟。","Every Krav Maga defence and counter starts from this stance.":"Krav Maga 的每一个防守与反击都从这个姿势开始。","Straight-Punch Burst":"连续直拳","When you can't get away and must fight back":"无法脱离、必须反击时","Continuous attack":"连续攻击","LEAD · REAR · KEEP MOVING IN · NO PAUSES":"前手 · 后手 · 持续向前 · 不停顿","Krav Maga teaches that once you have to fight back, you keep going: lead punch, rear punch, pressing forward as you strike, so the attacker has no time to recover or hit back — until you can get away safely.":"Krav Maga 强调，一旦必须反击，就要连续不停：前手直拳、后手直拳，一边打一边向前压，让对方没有喘息和反击的机会，直到你能安全脱离为止。","Throwing one punch and stopping to look; punching while backing up; pauses between punches; dropping the hands.":"打一拳就停下来看结果；后退着打；拳与拳之间有停顿；双手掉下来。","10 seconds of non-stop punches on pads, 10 seconds rest, 6 rounds, always moving forward.":"在手靶上连续打 10 秒、休息 10 秒，重复 6 轮，并始终向前移动。","This continuous, forward-pressing counter-attack is what Krav Maga calls retzev (\"continuous motion\").":"这种连续、向前施压的反击，在 Krav Maga 中称为「Retzev」（连续动作）。","Inside Defence vs Straight Punch":"对抗直拳的内侧拨挡反击","Their face":"对方的脸","A straight punch comes at you":"对方的直拳打过来","Timing and coordination":"时机与协调","LEAD PALM REDIRECTS · REAR HAND PUNCHES AT THE SAME TIME":"前手掌拨开 · 同时后手出拳","As the straight punch comes, use your lead palm to deflect it to the side from the inside while your body moves slightly off line, and at the same moment fire your rear hand straight into their face. Defence and counter happen together, not one after the other. Then keep striking or get away.":"对方直拳打来时，用前手掌从内侧把拳头拨向一旁，同时身体稍微偏开，后手直拳直接打回对方脸部。防守和反击同时发生，而不是先挡再打。之后继续反击或离开。","Blocking without countering; a big swatting movement; blocking first and punching after (too slow); closing your eyes.":"只挡不打；撥挡动作太大；先挡完再打（太慢）；眼睛闭起来。","Partner throws slow straight punches with gloves; deflect and counter at the same time, 10 each side.":"夥伴戴拳套慢速出直拳，你练习挡拨＋反击同时进行，左右各 10 次。","Defending and countering at once is a core Krav Maga principle — it cuts the time you spend on the back foot.":"同时防守与反击是 Krav Maga 最核心的原则之一，能大幅缩短你处于被动的时间。","360° Outside Defence":"360° 外侧防守","Swinging or overhead attacks from the side":"从侧面或上方打来的挥拳或攻击","Reflex and structure":"反射与结构","FOREARM UP · ELBOW ~90° · COUNTER AT ONCE":"前臂立起 · 手肘约 90° · 同时反击","The 360° defence is a family of forearm blocks for curved attacks from any angle — high, side or low. Against a swing from the side, raise the forearm with the elbow bent about 90° so the outside of the forearm meets the attack beside your head, while your other hand punches straight back. The block's height changes with the attack, but the principle stays the same: meet it with the forearm and counter at once.":"360° 防守是一组可以挡住各种角度（上、侧、下）弧线攻击的前臂防守。对方从侧面挥拳时，前臂立起、手肘弯约 90°，用前臂外侧挡在头侧，同时另一手直拳反击。挡的位置会依攻击高度改变，但原则都一样：用前臂迎击、同时反击。","Blocking with the hand (it gets driven through); the arm too far from the head; blocking without countering; shrinking backwards.":"用手掌挡（会被打穿）；手臂离头太远；只挡不反击；身体往后缩。","Partner swings slowly with a pad from different angles; block with the forearm and counter, 5 reps per angle.":"同伴用手靶从不同角度慢速挥向你，练习前臂挡＋反击，各角度 5 次。","Real attacks are often big looping swings; the 360° defence lets one principle cover every angle.":"真实的攻击常是大弧线的挥拳，360° 防守让你用同一个原则应付不同角度。","Front Choke Release (Pluck)":"正面掐喉脱困","Release":"脱困","Their thumbs → then a knee":"对方的拇指 → 膝击","Choked from the front":"被人从正面掐住脖子","Speed and reaction":"速度与反应","HOOK THE THUMBS · PLUCK DOWN AND OUT · CHIN DOWN · KNEE":"双手勾拇指 · 往下往外拉 · 下巴收 · 膝击","If someone chokes you from the front with both hands, immediately bring your hands up and hook your fingers over their thumbs from above — the thumbs are the weakest part of the grip — and pluck them down and out hard while tucking your chin and pushing your head slightly forward. As soon as you are free, grab hold and counter with a knee, then shove away, step back and leave.":"被人从正面双手掐住脖子时，双手立刻举起，从上方把手指勾在对方的拇指上（拇指是握力最弱的地方），用力往下往外拉开，同时下巴收紧、头稍微往前。拉开后马上抓住对方，用膝盖反击，接着推开、后退、离开。","Pulling or stepping backwards (it tightens the choke); pulling at the wrists instead of the thumbs; not countering after the release; hesitating.":"往后退或往后拉（掐得更紧）；用力拉对方的手腕而不是拇指；拉开后不反击；动作太慢。","Partner rests their hands lightly on your neck (no squeezing); slowly practise hook the thumbs → pluck → knee (no contact), 10 reps.":"同伴双手轻轻放在你的脖子上（不要用力掐），慢速练习「勾拇指 → 拉开 → 膝击（不碰到）」10 次。","A choke leaves you only seconds; this release is simple, fast and needs no strength.":"被掐住脖子只有几秒钟的反应时间，这个动作简单、快速、不需要力气。","Groin Kick":"踢鼠蹊","Groin":"鼠蹊部","They are a leg's length away":"对方在一腿距离","KNEE UP · SNAP UP · INSTEP OR SHIN · FAST RECOIL":"提膝 · 往上弹 · 脚背或胫骨 · 快收","From your stance, lift the rear knee and snap the lower leg upward so the instep or shin strikes the groin, then pull the leg back fast and plant it. Step back and leave straight away, or keep countering.":"从戒备姿势把后腿膝盖提起，小腿由下往上快速弹出，用脚背或胫骨踢向对方鼠蹊部，然后快速收腿、落地。踢完立刻后退、离开，或继续反击。","Kicking with the toes (they jam); a slow, obvious kick; leaving the leg out; staying put afterwards.":"用脚尖踢（容易扭伤）；踢得太慢、预告明显；踢完腿停在空中；踢完站在原地。","On a low-held kick shield, 3 × 10 per leg, fast out and fast back. Never actually kick a training partner there.":"对着放低的踢靶练习，每腿 3 × 10，重点是快踢快收。训练时绝对不要真的踢到伙伴。","Even a much smaller person can use it to stop an attacker and buy time to get away.":"这是体型较小的人也能有效使用的反击，能让对方停下来，给你离开的时间。","Knee from the Clinch":"抓肩膝击","Close-range counter":"近身反击","Groin, stomach":"鼠蹊部、腹部","They are right up against you":"对方贴得太近","GRAB THE SHOULDERS · PULL DOWN · KNEE UP":"双手抓肩 · 往下拉 · 膝往上顶","When they are right up against you, grab their shoulders or the back of the neck, pull them down and drive your rear knee up into the groin or stomach at the same time. Repeat if needed, then shove away, step back and leave.":"对方贴得太近时，双手抓住对方的肩膀或后颈，把对方往下拉，同时后腿膝盖往上顶向鼠蹊部或腹部。可以连续膝击，然后推开、后退、离开。","Lifting the knee without pulling them down; kicking forward instead of driving up; leaning back; hanging on instead of leaving.":"只抬腿不拉人；膝盖往前踢而不是往上顶；身体往后仰；抓住不放而不是离开。","3 × 10 per leg on a knee pad or bag; with a partner, light touch or no contact only.":"对膝击靶或沙袋每腿 3 × 10；和伙伴练习时只做轻触或不接触。","When there is no room to punch, the knee is the most natural and powerful counter.":"当没有空间出拳时，膝击是最自然也最有力的反击。","Break Away & Scan":"脱离与观察四周","— (leave)":"—（离开现场）","After every counter":"每一次反击之后","Awareness and judgement":"警觉与判断","GUARD UP · BACK AWAY · SCAN · LEAVE AND GET HELP":"保持戒备 · 后退 · 观察 · 离开求助","Once your counter has stopped them for a moment, don't stay to keep fighting. Keep your guard up, back away to open the distance and turn your head to scan around you — other attackers, weapons, obstacles, the exits. Then move to a safe, busy place, get help and call the police.":"反击让对方暂时停下后，不要留下来继续打。保持戒备、后退拉开距离，转头观察四周：其他攻击者、武器、障碍物、出口。然后前往安全、人多的地方，求助并报警。","Staying to \"finish\" the attacker; turning your back too early; tunnel vision on one person; forgetting to call the police.":"反击后留下来「教训」对方；过早转身背对对方逃跑；只盯着一个人，没注意其他人；忘了报警。","End every drill with three steps back, a scan both ways, and naming the exit out loud.":"每次练习任何技术后，都要加上「后退 3 步、左右观察、说出出口在哪」。","Krav Maga's goal is getting home safe, not winning a fight; scanning and leaving are part of every technique.":"Krav Maga 的目标是安全回家，而不是赢得打斗；观察与离开是每个技术的一部分。","Where everything starts":"所有动作的起点","Ready to defend and strike":"随时能防也能打","Non-stop combinations":"不间断的连续攻击","Punch while moving forward":"边前进边出拳","Defend and counter at the same time":"同时防守与反击","Stops attacks from the outside":"挡住从外侧来的攻击","The forearm is the shield":"前臂当盾牌","One of the most urgent situations":"最紧急的情况之一","Pluck the thumbs, counter at once":"拨开拇指，立即反击","The simplest effective kick":"最简单有效的腿法","Snaps upward":"向上弹击","The strongest weapon up close":"近身最有力的武器","Pull down, drive up":"向下拉，向上顶","The last step of every technique":"每个技术的最后一步","Is anyone else there?":"还有别人在吗？","Feet staggered, knees soft, leaning slightly forward":"双脚前后错开站立，膝盖放松微屈，身体略微前倾","Hands up in front of the face, open or closed":"双手举在脸前，手掌张开或握拳皆可","Chin down, weight on the balls of the feet, ready to move either way":"下巴收低，重心在前脚掌，随时可以向任一方向移动","Fighting stance":"战斗姿势","Lead straight punch":"前手直拳","Rear straight punch while you keep moving forward":"后手直拳，同时继续向前推进","Keep firing without pausing until you have a chance to get away":"不停歇地持续出击，直到有机会脱身","A straight punch comes in":"对方直拳打来","The lead palm redirects the punch while the rear hand punches back at the same time":"前手掌把拳拨开，同时后手直拳反击","Keep countering or break away":"继续反击或脱离","A swinging punch comes from the side":"对方从侧面挥拳打来","Raise the forearm to block at the side of the head (elbow about 90°) while the rear hand counters":"前臂立起挡在头侧（手肘约 90°），同时后手反击","Keep striking, then get away":"持续反击，然后脱身","They choke you from the front with both hands":"对方双手从正面掐住你的脖子","Immediately bring both hands up and hook your fingers over their thumbs":"立刻双手举高，手指勾住对方的拇指","Pluck them down and out hard, chin tucked, head forward":"用力往下往外拉开，下巴收、头往前","Grab hold and counter with a knee":"抓住对方，膝击反击","Shove away, step back, leave":"推开、后退、离开","Fighting stance, a leg's length away":"戒备姿势，对方在一腿距离","Lift the rear knee":"后腿提膝","Snap the lower leg up, striking the groin with the instep or shin":"小腿向上弹出，用脚背或胫骨踢向鼠蹊部","Snap the leg back":"快速收腿","Plant, step back and leave":"落地后退、离开","They are too close":"对方靠得太近","Grab their shoulders or the back of the neck":"双手抓住对方的肩膀或后颈","Pull them down while driving the knee up":"把对方往下拉，同时膝盖往上顶","Repeat the knee if needed":"可以连续膝击","After your counter, they are stopped for a moment":"反击后对方暂时停住","Keep your guard up and back away":"保持戒备，后退拉开距离","Turn your head to scan around you: other attackers, weapons, exits":"左右转头检查四周，有没有其他人或物品","Move to safety, get help and call the police":"往安全的地方离开，求助并报警","Readiness":"反应准备","Forward pressure":"前进压迫","Reflex":"反射","Getting away":"脱离","Judgement":"判断","Getting help":"求助","Setup (Address)":"准备站姿（Address）","Fundamentals":"基本功","Flat back, soft knees":"背部平直、膝盖微屈","A stable, balanced posture":"稳定、平衡的姿势","HINGE AT THE HIPS · SOFT KNEES · ARMS HANG":"从髋部前倾 · 膝微屈 · 手臂自然下垂","Set your feet about shoulder-width apart. Bend forward from the hips (not the waist), pushing your seat back with a flat back and softly bent knees. Let your arms hang straight down from the shoulders to hold the club, with the clubhead just behind the ball. From the front, your upper body tilts slightly away from the target, and your weight is even on both feet.":"双脚张开约与肩同宽，从髋部（而非腰部）向前弯曲，臀部向后推，背部保持平直，膝盖微弯。双臂从肩膀自然垂下握住球杆，杆头正好位于球的后方。从正面看，上身略微向远离目标的方向倾斜，双脚均匀承担体重。","Rounding the back; bending the knees so much it looks like sitting; standing too far away and reaching for the ball; standing too upright.":"弯腰驼背；膝盖弯太多像坐椅子；站太远，手臂伸出去够球；站得太直。","Hold a club along your spine (touching head, upper back and seat) and hinge to your setup angle 10 times; then check side-on in a mirror.":"把球杆贴在背上（头、上背、臀部三点接触），从髋部前倾到准备角度，练 10 次；再对镜从侧面检查。","Most swing faults start at setup. The right posture lets the body turn freely and makes the swing repeatable.":"大部分挥杆问题都源自站姿。站姿正确，身体才能顺利转动、挥杆才能重复。","Takeaway":"起杆","Swing phase 1":"挥杆阶段 1","Move together, clubhead low":"一起转、杆头低","Shoulder-led movement and rhythm":"肩膀带动、节奏","SHOULDERS LEAD · CLUBHEAD LOW · DON'T RUSH":"肩膀带动 · 杆头低 · 不要急","Turn the shoulders, arms and club back together as one piece, keeping the clubhead low to the ground and the wrists quiet. By the time your hands pass your back leg, the shaft is roughly parallel to the ground with the toe of the club pointing up.":"肩膀、手臂和球杆像一个整体一起往后转，杆头贴着地面低低地往后拉，手腕先不要折。到手大约在右腿前方（右手球员）时，杆身与地面平行、杆头朝上。","Lifting the club with the hands only; hinging the wrists too early; snatching it back too fast; swaying the body away from the target.":"只用手把球杆提起来；手腕太早折；起杆太快；身体往后晃动。","Lay a second club or ruler on the ground behind the ball and let the clubhead track along it for the first foot (30 cm) of the takeaway, 15 times.":"把第二支球杆或尺放在球后方地上，起杆时让杆头沿着它往后走 30 公分，练 15 次。","The takeaway sets the path and tempo of the whole swing — start it right and the rest follows more easily.":"起杆决定了整个挥杆的路线和节奏，开始对了，后面就容易对。","Top of the Backswing":"上杆顶点","Swing phase 2":"挥杆阶段 2","Shoulders 90°, back to the target":"肩转 90°、背对目标","Upper-body rotation and flexibility":"上身转动与柔软度","SHOULDERS ~90° · HIPS ~45° · LEAD ARM STRAIGHT":"肩转约 90° · 髋转约 45° · 左手臂伸直","Keep turning until your back faces the target — about 90° of shoulder turn and 45° of hip turn. The wrists hinge naturally, the lead arm stays straight but not stiff, and most of your weight sits on the inside of the back foot. The head stays roughly where it started.":"继续转动，直到背部朝向目标，肩膀转约 90°、髋部约 45°。手腕自然折起，左手臂（右手球员）保持伸直但不僵硬，重心大多在后脚内侧。头部大致留在原位。","Lifting the arms without turning; bending the lead arm a lot; swaying so the weight goes to the outside of the back foot; overswinging so the club droops.":"只抬手臂不转身；左手臂弯曲很多；晃动身体让重心移到后脚外侧；上杆过头，球杆下垂。","Cross your arms over your chest, turn your back to the target, hold 2 seconds and turn back, 10 times; then do it with a club and pause at the top.":"双臂交叉抱胸，背对目标转身，停 2 秒，再转回来，练 10 次；然后拿球杆做，在顶点停住。","The top is where the power is loaded; a full turn gives the downswing room and speed.":"顶点是力量蓄积的地方。转身转够，下杆才有足够的空间和速度。","Downswing":"下杆","Swing phase 3":"挥杆阶段 3","Lower body leads":"下半身先动","Sequencing and explosive power":"动作顺序与爆发力","WEIGHT SHIFT · THEN HIPS · THEN ARMS":"先移重心 · 再转髋 · 最后手臂","The downswing starts from the ground up: shift your weight towards the front foot, then turn the hips towards the target, and let the shoulders and arms follow. As the arms drop, keep the wrist hinge (like cracking a whip) so the stored speed is released just before impact.":"下杆从下半身开始：先把重心移向前脚，接着髋部转向目标，肩膀和手臂最后跟上。手臂落下时保持手腕折角（像甩鞭子），让蓄积的速度在接近击球时释放。","Starting with the hands and shoulders (an over-the-top, slicing path); releasing the wrists too early (\"casting\"); leaving the weight on the back foot.":"用手和肩膀先发力（造成由外向内的切球路径）；太早放开手腕（\"甩杆\"）；重心留在后脚。","Pause at the top for a second, then \"step\" into the front foot before swinging down — 15 slow reps, feeling the hips pull the arms.":"在顶点停 1 秒，然后先“踩”向前脚再挥下来，慢速练 15 次；感受髋部带动手臂。","The right order adds speed link by link until it peaks in the clubhead — why good players look effortless yet hit it far.":"正确的顺序让速度一节一节累加，到杆头最快——这就是职业球员看起来不费力却打得很远的原因。","Impact":"击球","Swing phase 4":"挥杆阶段 4","Hands ahead, weight forward":"手在球前、重心在前脚","Strike quality":"击球品质","HANDS AHEAD · WEIGHT FORWARD · HEAD BEHIND THE BALL":"手在球前 · 重心在前脚 · 头在球后","At impact your hands are slightly ahead of the ball (towards the target) with the shaft leaning forward, roughly 70–80% of your weight is on the front foot, the hips have opened towards the target, and the head is still behind the ball. With irons you strike the ball first, then brush the turf.":"击球时，双手位置在球的前方（靠目标那侧），杆身微微向前倾，重心大约 70–80% 在前脚，胯部已经转开面向目标一些，头部仍在球的后方。铁杆是“先击球、再擦过草皮”。","Trying to scoop the ball into the air (flipping the wrists, hands behind the ball); falling back onto the back foot; looking up early to see where it went.":"想把球“捞”起来（手腕翻、手在球后）；重心往后倒；抬头看球飞去哪。","Put a coin or towel 10 cm in front of the ball and make the club brush that spot after the ball — 20 slow half-swings.":"在球前约 10 公分放一枚硬币或毛巾，挥杆时让杆头击球后也擦过那个点；慢速半挥杆 20 次。","Everything else in the swing exists to get this instant right; a solid impact position sends the ball straight and solid.":"挥杆的其他部分都是为了在这一瞬间做对；击球位置正确，球就会飞得又直又扎实。","Follow-through & Finish":"送杆与收杆","Swing phase 5":"挥杆阶段 5","Face the target, hold it":"面向目标、站稳","Balance and a full turn":"平衡与完整转身","CHEST TO TARGET · WEIGHT ON FRONT FOOT · BACK TOE DOWN":"胸口面向目标 · 重心在前脚 · 后脚尖点地","After impact let the arms and club extend towards the target and keep turning until your chest and belt buckle face it. In the finish nearly all your weight is on the front foot, the back foot is up on its toe, the club wraps over your shoulder, and you are balanced and still.":"击球后让双手和球杆顺势朝目标伸出，身体继续转到胸口和皮带扣面向目标。收杆时几乎全部重心在前脚，后脚只剩脚尖点地，球杆绕到肩后，站稳不晃。","Stopping at the ball with no follow-through; falling backwards; leaving the back foot flat; wobbling at the finish.":"击到球就停（没有送杆）；收杆时往后倒；后脚整个平贴地面；收杆站不稳。","After every swing hold your finish for 3 seconds like posing for a photo; if you can't, you are swinging too hard.":"每次挥杆后都在收杆位置站 3 秒不动，像拍照一样；站不稳就代表挥杆太用力。","The finish is the result of the whole swing: holding it means your weight shift and turn were complete.":"收杆是整个挥杆的结果：能站稳，代表重心转移和转身都做到了。","Full Swing (Iron)":"完整挥杆（铁杆）","Full swing":"完整挥杆","Tempo 3 : 1":"节奏 3 : 1","Tempo and flow":"节奏与流畅度","TEMPO: BACKSWING 3 : DOWNSWING 1":"节奏：上杆与下杆时间约 3 : 1","Join setup, takeaway, top, downswing, impact and finish into one smooth motion. Most good players swing with a tempo of about 3 : 1 — roughly 0.75 s back and 0.25 s down. Switch to \"Real tempo\" to see it at true speed.":"把站姿、起桿、顶点、下桿、击球、收桿连成一个流畅的动作。大多数好球员的节奏是上桿时间约为下桿的 3 倍：上桿约 0.75 秒、下桿约 0.25 秒。切换「实际速度」可以看真实节奏。","Rushing the backswing; hurrying from the top; gripping and tensing everything (tension slows you down); swinging in separate jerky pieces.":"上杆太快；在顶点急着打；全程用力（肌肉越紧越慢）；每个阶段分开做、不连贯。","Count \"one-two-three\" going back and \"hit\" coming down, or use a metronome app. Start with a 7-iron and half swings.":"挥杆时心中数「一、二、三」上杆，「打」下杆；或用节拍器 App。先用 7 号铁、半挥杆练节奏。","Irons are the clubs you use most to hit greens; a steady tempo beats raw strength for good shots.":"铁杆是最常用的球杆，用来把球打上果岭；稳定的节奏比力气更能打出好球。","Driver Swing":"一号木开球","Ball off the front heel, sweep up":"球在前脚跟内侧、往上扫","Speed and an upward strike":"速度与往上击球","WIDER STANCE · BALL OFF FRONT HEEL · TILT BACK A LITTLE":"站姿较宽 · 球在前脚跟 · 上身稍向后倾","With the driver the ball sits on a tee opposite the inside of your front heel; stand a little wider than for an iron and tilt the upper body a bit more away from the target. The swing is the same, but you meet the ball just after the club bottoms out, on the way up — sweep it, don't hit down.":"开球木的球放在球座上，位置在前脚跟内侧；站姿比铁杆宽一些，上身向远离目标的方向多倾一点。挥杆动作和铁杆相同，但击球时杆头已经过了最低点、开始往上，把球“扫”出去，不要往下打。","Ball too far back; chopping down like an iron; swinging out of your shoes for distance; lunging the head towards the target.":"球放太中间；像铁杆一样往下砍；为了打远用尽全力而失去平衡；头往前冲。","Tee the ball a little higher and practise sweeping the ball off without hitting the tee; swing at 80% and hold your finish.":"把球座插高一点，练习只把球扫走而不打到球座；用 80% 力量挥杆、维持收杆平衡。","The driver is usually your first shot on long holes, aiming for distance and the fairway.":"每一洞的第一杆通常用一号木，目标是又远又在球道上。","Chip Shot":"切球","Short game":"短杆","Weight forward, hands ahead":"重心在前、手在球前","NARROW STANCE · WEIGHT FORWARD · SMALL PENDULUM":"站窄 · 重心偏前脚 · 小钟摆","Stand with a narrow stance, ball slightly back of centre and 60–70% of your weight on the front foot — and keep it there. With quiet wrists, rock the shoulders in a small pendulum: short back, brush down through the ball with the hands ahead. The ball flies low for a short way, lands and rolls to the hole.":"站姿较窄，球放在中间偏后脚，重心约 60–70% 在前脚并保持不动。手腕几乎不折，用肩膀做小幅钟摆：后摆小、往下轻擦过球，手保持在球前。球会低低飞起一小段，落地后滚向洞口。","Trying to scoop it up; shifting weight back; a big backswing that decelerates; flicking the wrists.":"想把球捞起来；重心移回后脚；后摆太大、下杆减速；手腕翻动。","Lay a towel on the green as a landing spot and land 10 balls on it from different distances, letting them roll out.":"在果岭边放一条毛巾当落点，练习让球落在毛巾上再滚，换不同距离各 10 球。","Most strokes are played near the green; a reliable chip saves more shots than anything else.":"大部分的杆数其实在果岭附近；切球好，能省下最多杆数。","Putting Stroke":"推杆","Shoulders rock, head still":"肩膀摆动、头不动","Line and pace control":"方向与力道控制","EYES OVER THE BALL · ROCK THE SHOULDERS · EVEN BACK AND THROUGH":"眼睛在球上方 · 肩膀摆动 · 前后等距","Set your eyes directly over the ball, let the arms hang and keep the wrists still. Rock the shoulders like a pendulum while the body and head stay quiet. Make the follow-through about as long as the backstroke, at a smooth even pace, and let the ball roll.":"双眼在球的正上方，手臂自然下垂，手腕固定。用肩膀像钟摆一样前后摆动，身体和头部保持不动。送杆长度和后摆差不多，速度平稳，让球顺顺地滚出去。","Flicking with the wrists; looking up straight away; a long backstroke that slows down; swaying the body.":"用手腕拨球；击球后马上抬头看；后摆很大但减速；身体跟着晃动。","Start at 1 m and hole 10 in a row before moving to 2 m; for long putts, practise stopping the ball within half a metre of the hole.":"从 1 公尺开始，连进 10 球再退到 2 公尺；远距离推杆则练习把球停在洞口半公尺内。","Putts are around 40% of an amateur's strokes; a steady putting stroke lowers scores fastest.":"业余球员大约四成杆数是推杆；推杆稳定，成绩马上进步。","A good swing starts here":"好挥杆从站姿开始","Side view for posture · front view for width":"侧面看姿势 · 正面看宽度","The first move of the swing":"挥杆的第一个动作","Low, slow, together":"低、慢、一体","Where the power is stored":"储存力量的位置","Turn, don't lift":"转身，不是抬手","Ground-up sequence":"由下往上的顺序","Keep the wrist hinge":"保持手腕折角","The moment that matters most":"挥杆中最重要的一瞬间","Ball first, then the ground":"先击球、再击地","A good finish shows a good swing":"好收杆代表好挥杆","Hold it for 3 seconds":"平衡站 3 秒","All five phases joined up":"把五个阶段连起来","Slow back, fast through":"上杆慢、下杆快","The longest club in the bag":"距离最远的球杆","Wider stance, ball forward":"站宽一点、球放前面","The small shot near the green":"果岭旁的小击球","Fly it low, let it roll":"低飞、多滚","Rolling the ball on the green":"果岭上的滚地球","Half your strokes happen here":"一半的杆数在这里","Stand tall, feet together, club behind the ball":"双脚并拢站直，球杆放在球后","Feet about shoulder-width, upper body tilted slightly away from the target":"双脚打开约肩宽，上身微微向远离目标的方向倾斜","Setup position":"准备站姿","Shoulders, arms and club move back together; the clubhead stays low":"肩膀、手臂、球杆一起转动；杆头贴地低低地往后","Wrists hinge; the club points up to the sky":"手腕自然折起，球杆指向天空","Top: back to the target, shoulders turned about 90°":"上杆顶点：背对目标，肩膀转约 90°","Top of the backswing":"上杆顶点","Lower body starts first: weight shifts to the front foot":"下半身先动：重心往前脚移","Arms drop with the wrists still hinged — stored power":"手臂落下，手腕保持折角（蓄力）","Impact: hands ahead of the ball, weight on the front foot":"击球：手在球的前方，重心在前脚","Follow-through: arms extend towards the target":"送杆：双手伸直朝目标","Finish: chest facing the target, balanced on the front foot, back toe on the ground":"收杆：胸口面向目标，站稳在前脚，后脚脚尖点地","Setup":"准备站姿","Top (about 0.75 s)":"上杆顶点（约 0.75 秒）","Downswing (about 0.25 s)":"下杆（约 0.25 秒）","Balanced finish":"收杆，平衡站好","Ball slightly back, weight leaning on the front foot":"球放在中间偏后，重心偏前脚","Small pendulum backswing, wrists barely hinge":"像钟摆一样小幅后摆，手腕几乎不折","Brush down through the ball, hands staying ahead":"向下轻擦过球，手保持在球前","Short finish — the ball pops up, lands and rolls":"短收杆，球轻轻飞起后滚向洞口","Eyes over the ball, arms hanging naturally":"双眼在球的正上方，手臂自然下垂","Rock the shoulders back like a pendulum":"用肩膀摆动，像钟摆一样后摆","Body still, smooth even pace through the ball":"身体不动，等速穿过球","Follow through as far as you swung back; keep the head still":"送杆距离和后摆差不多，头留在原地","Stand tall holding the club out in front":"站直，双手握杆放在身前","Hinge forward from the hips, push the seat back, soften the knees, keep the back flat":"从髋部向前倾、臀部往后推，膝盖微弯，背部保持平直","Arms hang straight down from the shoulders; club rests behind the ball":"手臂从肩膀自然垂下，杆头放在球后","RED LINE = SPINE ANGLE (KEEP IT FLAT)":"红线＝背部角度（保持平直）","GREEN RING = KEEP THE HEAD STEADY":"绿圈＝头部保持稳定","Distance from the ball":"与球距离","Alignment":"瞄准方向","Shoulder turn":"肩膀带动","Tempo":"节奏","Club path":"杆头路线","Quiet wrists":"手腕稳定","Weight control":"重心控制","Weight shift":"重心转移","Wrist lag":"手腕蓄力","Sequencing":"动作顺序","Impact position":"击球位置","Weight forward":"重心在前","Wrist position":"手腕结构","Steady head":"头部稳定","Full rotation":"完整转身","Club speed":"挥杆速度","Upward strike":"往上击球","Stance width":"站姿宽度","Line":"方向","Pace":"力道","Stillness":"身体稳定","7-iron":"7 号铁杆","Driver":"一号木（开球木）","Wedge":"挖起杆","Putter":"推杆","Learning (3× slower)":"学习（慢 3 倍）","Real tempo":"实际节奏","Lesson {n} of 10 · {type} · {club}":"第 {n} 课 · {type} · {club}","First, the grip":"先学会握杆","For a right-handed golfer: the left hand goes on first, with the grip running diagonally across the base of the fingers; looking down you should see 2–3 knuckles. The right hand goes below it, palm facing the target, covering the left thumb. The overlap, interlock and ten-finger grips all work — pick the most comfortable. Grip pressure should be about 4–5 out of 10; squeezing tight locks up the arms and slows the club.":"右手球员：左手先握，球杆斜放在手指根部，握好后从上往下看能看到左手 2–3 个指节；右手接着握上，右手掌心面向目标，盖住左手拇指。三种常见握法——重叠式、交错式、十指式——都可以，选最舒服的。握力大约是 10 分中的 4–5 分，太紧会让手臂僵硬、挥不快。","Club":"球杆","Where should the ball go?":"球要放在哪里？","Mid and short irons: middle of the stance or slightly forward.":"中短铁杆：站姿中间或稍微偏前。","Driver: opposite the inside of the front heel, on a tee.":"一号木：前脚跟内侧，球放在球座上。","Chip: slightly back of centre so the hands are naturally ahead.":"切球：中间偏后脚，让手自然在球前。","Putt: slightly forward of centre, eyes directly over the ball.":"推杆：中间偏前，眼睛在球的正上方。","Two ways to watch a swing":"两个看挥杆的角度","Coaches watch a swing from two angles: face-on (in front of the golfer) for weight shift, head position and the swing arc, and down the line (behind the golfer, looking at the target) for posture and swing plane. Filming yourself from both angles on your phone and comparing with these animations is the cheapest, most effective practice there is.":"教练通常从两个角度看挥杆：「正面」（站在球员前方）看重心转移、头部位置和挥杆弧线；「侧面（球线后方）」（站在球员后面，看向目标）看姿势角度和挥杆平面。用手机从这两个角度录下自己的挥杆，和本页动画比较，是最便宜有效的练习方法。","Safety and warm-up":"安全与热身","Always check nobody is nearby or in front before you swing.":"挥杆前先确认周围和前方没有人。","Warm up shoulders, hips and back with gentle turns, then start with short clubs and half swings.":"先做肩膀、髋部和背部的转体热身，再从短杆、半挥杆开始。","If your back or elbows hurt when you swing, stop and get it checked by a coach or doctor.":"挥杆时背部或手肘疼痛，请停止并请教练或医师检查。","Why does my ball curve to the right (a slice)?":"为什么我的球总是往右弯（右曲球）？","Most often the hands and shoulders start the downswing, so the club cuts across the ball from outside to in with an open face. Practise the lower-body-first sequence (lesson 4) and check your grip isn't too weak.":"最常见的原因是下杆时手和肩膀先动，杆头由外往内切过球，加上杆面打开。练习「下半身先动」的下杆顺序（第 4 课），并检查握杆不要太弱。","How fast should I swing?":"揮杆节奏要多快？","Ratio matters more than speed: the backswing takes about three times as long as the downswing. Swinging at 80% and holding your finish usually gives the best results.":"重点是比例，不是速度：上杆约为下杆的 3 倍时间。用 80% 的力量、能站稳收杆，通常打得最好。","Does my head really have to stay perfectly still?":"头真的要完全不动吗？","Not perfectly — it moves a little as the body turns. The key is no big sway or bob, and keeping the head behind the ball until impact.":"不必完全不动，头会随身体转动有一点点移动；重点是不要明显上下或左右大幅晃动，击球前头保持在球后方。","SPORTS SKILLS · GOLF FOR BEGINNERS":"运动技巧 · 高尔夫入门","The Golf Swing, Step by Step: Setup to Finish":"高尔夫挥杆，一步一步看：从站姿到收杆","The swing broken into six positions — setup, takeaway, top, downswing, impact and finish — then the full iron and driver swings, the chip and the putt. The face-on view (target to the right) shows the swing arc best; the green trail follows the clubhead and the green ring reminds you to keep your head steady. Left-handed? Press L-HAND.":"把挥杆拆成站姿、起杆、上杆顶点、下杆、击球、收杆六个位置，再看完整的铁杆与一号木挥杆、切杆和推杆。正面视角（目标在右边）最容易看懂挥杆弧线；绿色轨迹显示杆头路线，绿圈提醒头部保持稳定。左手球员请按「左手」。","Swing positions":"挥杆位置","Setup → takeaway → top → down → impact → finish":"站姿 → 起杆 → 顶点 → 下杆 → 击球 → 收杆","Ideal tempo":"理想节奏","About 0.75 s back · 0.25 s down":"上杆约 0.75 秒 · 下杆约 0.25 秒","Learning · 3× slower":"学习 · 慢 3 倍","Practice drill":"练习方法","Why it matters":"为什么重要","SIDE":"侧面","R-HAND":"右手","L-HAND":"左手","For education only; the animations are simplified. Every body is different — a qualified golf coach can check your swing. Warm up first, and always check nobody is near you before you swing.":"本页内容仅供教育参考，动画为简化示意。每个人的身体条件不同，建议找合格的高尔夫教练检查你的挥杆。练习前请热身，挥杆时注意周围是否有人。","Golf Swing Basics: Setup, Backswing, Impact & Finish — Interactive Guide | KungfuTutor":"高尔夫挥杆基础：站位、上杆、击球与收杆 — 互动指南 | KungfuTutor","Learn the golf swing step by step with animation: setup posture, takeaway, top of the backswing, downswing, impact and finish, plus the full iron swing, driver, chip shot and putting stroke. Includes tempo, common mistakes and drills.":"通过动画逐步学习高尔夫挥杆：站位姿势、起杆、上杆顶点、下杆、击球和收杆，并包括铁杆挥杆、一号木、切杆和推杆动作。内容包括节奏、常见错误和练习方法。","Golf Swing Basics — Interactive Step-by-Step Guide":"高尔夫挥杆基础 — 互动式分步指南","What are the main phases of the golf swing?":"高尔夫挥杆的主要阶段有哪些？","Setup (address), takeaway, top of the backswing, downswing, impact and follow-through to a balanced finish.":"站位（准备姿势）、起杆、上杆顶点、下杆、击球，以及保持平衡的收杆。","What is a good golf swing tempo?":"好的高尔夫挥杆节奏是怎样的？","Many good players swing with roughly a 3 to 1 ratio: the backswing takes about three times as long as the downswing, for example about 0.75 seconds back and 0.25 seconds down.":"许多优秀球员的挥杆比例大约为 3 比 1：上杆的时间约为下杆的三倍，例如上杆约 0.75 秒，下杆约 0.25 秒。","Where should the ball be in my stance?":"我的站位中球应该放在哪里？","For a mid-iron, about the middle of the stance or slightly forward; for the driver, opposite the inside of the front heel; for a chip, slightly back of centre.":"中铁杆一般位于站位中间或稍微靠前；一号木位于前脚脚跟内侧的正对位置；切杆则稍微位于中心偏后。"};
